<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- PART I: AVAIDAH 3, §15-16 (Subdivision under Lost and Found 3) -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="halacha-title">Laws of Unloading and Loading (<i>Perikah u&rsquo;Te&rsquo;inah</i>)<br><span style="font-size:0.82em; color: var(--accent-blue);">Subdivision of Laws of Lost and Found, Halacha 3, &sect;&sect; 15&ndash;16</span></div>

<div class="torah-ref">Based on Likutay Moharan I:13 &mdash; <i>&ldquo;Ashray ha&rsquo;Am&rdquo;</i> &mdash; <i>Hashgachah Shelaimah</i> (Complete Providence)</div>

<!-- Section 15 -->
<div class="section-num">&sect; 15</div>

<p>This is the aspect of the mitzvah of <span class="key-term">perikah u&rsquo;te&rsquo;inah</span> [unloading and loading], the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;When you see the donkey of one who hates you crouching beneath its burden, and you would hold back from helping him &mdash; you shall surely help with him&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 23:5)</span>.</p>

<p>For it is explained in the Torah [discourse] mentioned above that the <span class="key-term">tzadik</span>, through his great power, elevates and raises up through the aspect of <span class="key-term">ibbur</span> [spiritual gestation] even those souls that are very distant &mdash; those who have not yet left from the profane to the holy even a hairsbreadth. This is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Go out and see the might of your Master&rdquo;</span> etc. [i.e. that even the lowest depths are reached], see there.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;When you see the donkey of one who hates you crouching beneath its burden.&rdquo;</span> And our Sages of blessed memory expounded: <span class="precise">&ldquo;one who hates you&rdquo;</span> &mdash; this refers to one whom you saw transgress a sin, etc. And this is <span class="verse">&ldquo;crouching beneath its burden&rdquo;</span> &mdash; meaning that it is difficult to elevate him and raise him up because of the greatness of the burden placed upon him, which is the aspect of the burden of sins, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;as a heavy burden, they are too heavy for me&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 38:5)</span>. And therefore it could be that it would enter your mind to hold back from helping him, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and you would hold back from helping him,&rdquo;</span> for it would seem to you that it is too difficult to raise him because of the greatness of the burden upon him. But Hashem, may He be blessed, is merciful and gracious, and His compassion is exceedingly great. Therefore He warned in His mercy: <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall surely help with him&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that even such a soul, one must help and endeavor with all one&rsquo;s strength to elevate and raise it up, for the <span class="key-term">tzadik</span> has such power, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is <span class="precise">&ldquo;with him&rdquo;</span> precisely, as our Sages of blessed memory expounded: <span class="verse">&ldquo;One might think even if he [the owner] sits down and says, &lsquo;since you have a mitzvah [to help]&rsquo;&rdquo;</span> etc.? <span class="verse">&ldquo;Therefore it says: &lsquo;with him.&rsquo;&rdquo;</span> That is to say, certainly it is a great mitzvah to occupy oneself with him and to help him also to elevate and renew his soul. However, all this is <span class="precise">&ldquo;with him&rdquo;</span> &mdash; meaning, when he himself also wants to engage in this, to have compassion on himself, to endeavor in the rectification of his soul, to remove the great burden that is upon him, only that he cannot do so by himself and he is waiting for someone who will help him in this. Then it is a great mitzvah to help him with all one&rsquo;s strength, to occupy oneself with him, to raise him up. For there is the power to renew his soul as well, if he himself has some genuine desire for this, to engage in the rectification of his soul. But if he wants to exempt himself entirely and does not want to endeavor in rectifying his soul at all, but rather wants the <span class="key-term">tzadik</span> himself to do everything for him while he does nothing at all and does not engage in this at all &mdash; then certainly the <span class="key-term">tzadik</span> need not occupy himself with him, for it is impossible to help him when he does not want to engage in his own rectification at all, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And as our Master, our Teacher and our Rebbe, of blessed memory, said to someone: &ldquo;You without me cannot do anything at all&rdquo; (i.e. to rectify his soul by himself), &ldquo;but I too without you cannot do a thing&rdquo; &mdash; meaning, if you yourself do nothing at all, certainly it is impossible for me to do everything for you. For a person has free will, and it is impossible to raise him up unless he has some arousal from himself. And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;One might think even if he sits down&rdquo;</span> etc.? <span class="verse">&ldquo;Therefore it says: &lsquo;with him,&rsquo;&rdquo;</span> etc., as mentioned above.</p>

<!-- Section 16 -->
<div class="section-num">&sect; 16</div>

<p>This is also the aspect of the mitzvah of <span class="key-term">perikah u&rsquo;te&rsquo;inah</span> in its simple, literal sense. For the fact that one&rsquo;s donkey crouches beneath its burden and one has such distress and weariness on the road &mdash; this derives from the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;by the sweat of your brow shall you eat bread&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Genesis 3:19)</span>, the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;in sorrow shall you eat of it&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Genesis 3:17)</span>. For from there come all the suffering and weariness that a person has in the pursuits he engages in for his livelihood. And it is impossible to rectify this and be saved from it except through the rectifications stated in the Torah [discourse] mentioned above &mdash; namely, through breaking the desire for money by means of <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span>. Through this, one merits to nullify the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;by the sweat of your brow,&rdquo;</span> etc., and through this one merits <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> [holy knowledge]. Through this, one can gather <span class="key-term">nefashos</span> [souls] and draw forth <span class="key-term">Torah</span>, etc. Through this, <span class="key-term">hashgachah shelaimah</span> [complete providence] is drawn down, as explained there.</p>

<p>And when <span class="key-term">hashgachah shelaimah</span> is drawn down, then everything is rectified in completeness. For all the suffering and distress and weariness, etc. &mdash; all of it is because one is distant from Hashem, may He be blessed, namely from the Torah. Through this distance, one does not merit <span class="key-term">hashgachah shelaimah</span>, and from there come all the lack of livelihood and the withholding of <span class="key-term">shefa</span> [abundance], and all the suffering and weariness that one has in matters of livelihood. For all livelihood and <span class="key-term">shefa</span> flow from the eyes of His providence, may He be blessed. But when one is distant, G&ndash;d forbid, from the Torah, so that the <span class="key-term">hashgachah</span> does not reach him in completeness, etc., as explained there &mdash; then the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> that flows from His providence, may He be blessed, is scattered, G&ndash;d forbid, and goes to the place where it goes, G&ndash;d forbid, and does not reach him. And from this comes all the difficulty of livelihood, may the Merciful One save us. For because one is distant from the Torah, G&ndash;d forbid, and distant from complete <span class="key-term">hashgachah</span>, the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> flows to the place that it flows to, as mentioned above &mdash; namely, to the outer [impure] places, and the nations of the world and the great wicked ones who are connected there receive all the <span class="key-term">shefa</span>, while Israel is sustained from the dregs. For Israel clings to Hashem, may He be blessed, and they need to receive the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> specifically from the aspect of <span class="key-term">hashgachah shelaimah</span>.</p>

<p>And this is what is written regarding the Land of Israel: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Constantly, the eyes of Hashem your G&ndash;d are upon it&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Deuteronomy 11:12)</span>. <span class="precise">&ldquo;Constantly&rdquo;</span> precisely &mdash; this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">hashgachah shelaimah</span>, that His eyes, may He be blessed, gaze constantly upon the Land of Israel. For the eyes of His providence reach there in the aspect of a striking [of the gaze] until it returns and is depicted in His eyes, and therefore His eyes are attached there constantly. For the <span class="key-term">hashgachah shelaimah</span> is in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and the <i>chayos</i> were running and returning&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Ezekiel 1:14)</span>, as explained there &mdash; meaning that at every moment the <span class="key-term">hashgachah</span> runs and returns from above to below and returns from below to above, and so it cycles continuously at every moment in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;running and returning.&rdquo;</span> This is the aspect of <span class="key-term">hashgachah shelaimah</span>, the aspect of the Land of Israel, the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;constantly the eyes of Hashem your G&ndash;d are upon it&rdquo;</span> &mdash; <span class="precise">&ldquo;constantly&rdquo;</span> precisely. For the Land of Israel is near to Him, may He be blessed, more than anywhere in the world, for there is the essential drawing of the Torah, as is known.</p>

<p>And therefore, one whose donkey crouches beneath its burden and has such weariness &mdash; which derives from the blemish of the desire for money, from the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;by the sweat of your brow,&rdquo;</span> etc., from the aspect of the blemish of <span class="key-term">hashgachah shelaimah</span>, whose essential rectification comes through returning and renewing his soul through the aspect of <span class="key-term">ibbur</span>, through which <span class="key-term">hashgachah shelaimah</span> is once again drawn upon him, as mentioned above &mdash; therefore it might enter your mind that it is impossible to help such a person, since he has fallen so far. And therefore the Torah warned: <span class="verse">&ldquo;You shall surely help with him&rdquo;</span> &mdash; for in truth one must share in his suffering and help him with all one&rsquo;s strength. And through helping him physically and fulfilling the mitzvah <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall surely help&rdquo;</span> and <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall surely raise up,&rdquo;</span> through this kindness that one does with him, one subdues and nullifies from him the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;by the sweat of your brow,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; which is the aspect of the blemish of the desire for money &mdash; and one draws upon him the aspect of <span class="key-term">hashgachah shelaimah</span>.</p>

<p>For upon each and every one of Israel this matter is incumbent: to endeavor in rectifying one&rsquo;s fellow both physically and spiritually, and to fulfill with one&rsquo;s fellow <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall surely help&rdquo;</span> and <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall surely raise up.&rdquo;</span> For even though one&rsquo;s fellow is very distant from Hashem, may He be blessed, nevertheless one can help him too through the power of the true <span class="key-term">tzadik</span>, who has the power to elevate even his soul in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Go out and see the might of your Master,&rdquo;</span> etc., as mentioned above. See there well what is brought there: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And the wave cries out to its fellow: &lsquo;Is there anything in the world?&rsquo;&rdquo;</span> etc., <span class="verse">&ldquo;Go out and see the might of your Master,&rdquo;</span> etc. See there. It emerges that each and every one must arouse and remind his fellow in <span class="key-term">yiras shamayim</span> [the fear of Heaven], even though they are as they are. Nevertheless, through the power of the <span class="key-term">tzadik</span>, they can all ascend, as mentioned above. And therefore the Torah warned to help even the <span class="heb-word">sonay</span> [the &ldquo;enemy&rdquo;] &mdash; i.e. one whom you saw transgress a sin &mdash; for even him one must help greatly, for there is the power to elevate him as well through the power of the great <span class="key-term">tzadik</span> who is engaged in this, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Go out and see the might of your Master,&rdquo;</span> etc., as mentioned above.</p>

<p class="closing">&bull; &bull; &bull;</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- PART II: PERIKAH U'TE'INAH, HALACHA 1 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="halacha-title">Laws of Unloading and Loading &mdash; Halacha 1</div>

<div class="torah-ref">Based on Likutay Moharan I:59 &mdash; <i>&ldquo;Mi She&rsquo;Osaik L&rsquo;Karaiv&rdquo;</i> &mdash; Whoever engages in drawing close [to Hashem those who are far]</div>

<p style="text-indent:0; text-align:center; font-style:italic; color: var(--accent-blue); margin-bottom:18px;"><span class="verse">&ldquo;When you see the donkey of one who hates you crouching beneath its burden&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall surely help with him,&rdquo;</span> and the Targum renders: <span class="verse">&ldquo;You shall abandon what is in your heart against him, and you shall unload with him.&rdquo;</span></p>

<!-- Section 1 -->
<div class="section-num">&sect; 1</div>

<p>For the heaviness of the burden that becomes heavy and falls &mdash; this is through <span class="key-term">sinah</span> [hatred]. For hatred is a blemish of <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> [knowledge/mind], as Rabbainu, may his light shine, wrote many times, as mentioned above. And when <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> is blemished, then the burden becomes heavy and falls, for <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> raises all things, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;the living carries itself&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Talmud)</span>. And the essential life-force is through <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span>, as it is written <span class="inline-source">(Ecclesiastes 7:12)</span>: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Wisdom gives life.&rdquo;</span> And therefore, through <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span>, a person can raise all the burdens in the world with ease, through stratagems and counsel. But when <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> departs, the life-force departs, and then the burden falls.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">choli nofel</span> [falling sickness, i.e. epilepsy] that Rabbainu, may his light shine, wrote about in the discourse <i>&ldquo;Hai man d&rsquo;ba&rsquo;ay l&rsquo;minsav&rdquo;</i> <span class="inline-source">(LM I:29)</span>. See there, that it comes about through a blemish of <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span>, through the overpowering of the bloods, and through this one falls. See there. And hatred and anger are the aspect of overpowering of the bloods, as Rabbainu, may his light shine, wrote <span class="inline-source">(LM I:57)</span>: for <span class="verse">&ldquo;the liver is angry&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Berachos 61a)</span>, and the liver is full of blood, which is the aspect of hatred and murder, which is the spilling of blood. And therefore, through hatred, there comes the overpowering of the bloods, and through this <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> is blemished, and through this one falls in the aspect of <span class="key-term">choli nofel</span>, as mentioned above. For then the burden becomes heavy, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;for my sins have gone over my head; as a heavy burden they are too heavy for me&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 38:5)</span>. For through sins, which are the aspect of the overpowering of the bloods, as Rabbainu, may his light shine, wrote there &mdash; through this <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> is blemished, and then all things fall through the heaviness, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;as a heavy burden, they are too heavy for me.&rdquo;</span> See the discourse <i>Ha&rsquo;i Man</i> mentioned above, where Rabbainu, may his light shine, brought this very verse. See there well.</p>

<p>And this is what is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;When you see the donkey of <i>one who hates you</i> crouching&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; <span class="precise">&ldquo;one who hates you&rdquo;</span> precisely, for the essential falling of the burden is through hatred, as mentioned above. And therefore the Torah commanded to help one&rsquo;s fellow to unload and load, in order that there should be love and affection between them. And through this, the blemish of the falling of the burden &mdash; which comes through hatred &mdash; is rectified, as mentioned above. And this is the meaning of the Targum: <span class="verse">&ldquo;You shall abandon what is in your heart&rdquo;</span> etc. For the essential purpose of this mitzvah is for the sake of love, as mentioned above. And as our Sages of blessed memory said regarding this mitzvah, on the verse <span class="verse">&ldquo;You have established equity&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 99:4)</span> &mdash; that one who sees his enemy unloading and loading with him will certainly embrace him and kiss him. For the essential purpose of this mitzvah is for the sake of love, through which the blemish of the falling of the burden is rectified, which comes through hatred, which is a blemish of <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span>, as mentioned above.</p>

<!-- Section 2 -->
<div class="section-num">&sect; 2</div>

<p>And this is what our Sages of blessed memory said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;If he is an elder and it is not in accordance with his honor, he is exempt&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Bava Metzia 30a)</span>. For one must be careful not to blemish the <span class="key-term">kavod</span> [honor/glory]. For <span class="key-term">kavod</span> is the root of the <span class="key-term">nefesh</span> [soul], as mentioned above. It follows that it is the life-force of the soul, and it is in the aspect of <span class="key-term">mochin</span> [expanded consciousness] and life-force for the soul. For <span class="key-term">kavod</span> depends on <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span>, for <span class="verse">&ldquo;it is not fitting for a fool to have honor&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Proverbs 26:1)</span>. And as it is written <span class="inline-source">(Proverbs 3:35)</span>: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The wise shall inherit honor.&rdquo;</span> And as Rabbainu, may his light shine, wrote <span class="inline-source">(LM I:67)</span> that <span class="key-term">kavod</span> returns to those who perceive knowledge, for there is the root of <span class="key-term">kavod</span>. And therefore a blemish of <span class="key-term">kavod</span> is a blemish of <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span>.</p>

<p>Also, love and unity depend on <span class="key-term">kavod</span>, for there all the souls are unified, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;in their assembly let my honor not be united&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Genesis 49:6)</span> &mdash; for <span class="key-term">kavod</span> is in the aspect of unity, for <span class="key-term">kavod</span> is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span> [Kingship], which is the aspect of unity, as brought above. For the king restrains the nation and gathers them and unifies them, as it is written <span class="inline-source">(I Samuel 9:17)</span>: <span class="verse">&ldquo;This one shall restrain My people.&rdquo;</span> And similarly, it is found in the words of Rabbainu, may his light shine <span class="inline-source">(LM I:14)</span>, that through rectifying <span class="key-term">kavod</span> &mdash; namely through giving honor to those who fear Hashem &mdash; through this, peace is drawn into the world. See there.</p>

<p>It emerges that the rectification of all the souls and their life-force is the aspect of <span class="key-term">kavod</span>, as mentioned above. And when <span class="key-term">kavod</span> is blemished, then their <span class="key-term">mochin</span> and life-force are blemished, and then they fall, as mentioned above. For they become in the aspect of a <span class="heb-word">masa kavaid</span> [heavy burden], as mentioned above, which is the aspect of a blemish of <span class="key-term">kavod</span>. For the blemish of <span class="key-term">kavod</span> is that the <span class="key-term">Vav</span> &mdash; which is the aspect of life-force &mdash; departs, and then from <span class="heb-word">kavod</span> [כָּבוֹד, honor] it becomes <span class="heb-word">kavaid</span> [כָּבֵד, heavy], the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;a heavy burden&rdquo;</span> &mdash; as Rabbainu wrote in another place, in the discourse <i>&ldquo;Ani Hashem Hu Sh&rsquo;mi&rdquo;</i> <span class="inline-source">(LM I:11)</span>.</p>

<p>And therefore, if he is an elder and it is not in accordance with his honor, he is exempt from <span class="key-term">perikah u&rsquo;te&rsquo;inah</span> &mdash; and there is an opinion that it is forbidden &mdash; for the essential blemish of the falling of the burden is in the aspect of the blemish of <span class="key-term">kavod</span>, as mentioned above. And therefore one must be careful with one&rsquo;s honor so as not to blemish it through the falling of the burden. For on the contrary, now one must be extremely careful with one&rsquo;s honor, which is the aspect of rectifying the falling, as mentioned above. And the essential rectification of <span class="key-term">kavod</span> is through the honor of the elder, as found in the words of Rabbainu, may his light shine, many times.</p>

<p>And therefore the elder, who merits completeness of <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span>, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;this one has acquired wisdom,&rdquo;</span> and merits <span class="key-term">kavod</span>, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;the wise shall inherit honor,&rdquo;</span> as it is written <span class="inline-source">(Job 15:10)</span>: <span class="verse">&ldquo;and with the elders is honor&rdquo;</span> &mdash; therefore he can bear and raise all the burdens, as Rabbainu, may his light shine, wrote <span class="inline-source">(LM I:54)</span> that the <span class="key-term">tzadik</span> is called <span class="heb-word">masa</span> [burden-bearer], for he bears everything, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;as a nurse carries the infant&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Numbers 11:12)</span>. For the <span class="key-term">tzadik</span> lifts and raises all the fallings. And all this is through rectifying <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span>, as mentioned above, and the rectification of <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> is the rectification of <span class="key-term">kavod</span>, as mentioned above, and as is implied from the words of Rabbainu, may his light shine, in many places.</p>

<!-- Section 3 -->
<div class="section-num">&sect; 3</div>

<p>And this is what our Sages of blessed memory said regarding this verse &mdash; that the <span class="heb-word">sonay</span> [enemy] spoken of here is one whom you saw transgress a sin. This is the aspect of the overpowering of the bloods of the 365 sinews, which correspond to the 365 negative commandments, as Rabbainu, of blessed memory, wrote there. And from this very thing comes the aspect of the falling, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;for my sins have gone over my head; as a heavy burden&rdquo;</span> etc., as mentioned above. For it is forbidden to hate a fellow Jew unless one saw him transgress a sin, in which case it is a mitzvah to hate him, as our Sages of blessed memory said regarding this matter. For the sin comes through the overpowering of the bloods of the 365 sinews, as mentioned above. And from there comes the aspect of hatred &mdash; through the bloods, as mentioned above. And therefore one is permitted to hate him, for he is in the aspect of hatred, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And nevertheless the Torah commanded not to leave him to fall completely, but rather one must abandon what is in one&rsquo;s heart against him and turn his [situation] favorably, to bring him to the aspect of love, as the Targum renders: <span class="verse">&ldquo;You shall abandon&rdquo;</span> etc. And through this, one raises him from his falling, as mentioned above.</p>

<!-- Section 4 -->
<div class="section-num">&sect; 4</div>

<p>And now, let us hint at this mitzvah as applied to a person himself. <span class="verse">&ldquo;When you see the donkey of one who hates you crouching,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; when one sees the <span class="heb-word">chomro</span> [his materiality, his body; a wordplay on <i>chamor</i>, donkey] of one who has sinned, as mentioned above, crouching beneath its burden and unable to bear upon itself the burden and yoke of Torah, and he falls, G&ndash;d forbid &mdash; for it is known that a person must be <span class="verse">&ldquo;as an ox to the yoke and as a donkey to the burden&rdquo;</span> &mdash; and when one sees a person falling from the service of Hashem, G&ndash;d forbid, and this is through sins, G&ndash;d forbid, the aspect of <span class="heb-word">son&rsquo;acha</span> [one who hates you], as mentioned above &mdash; the Torah commanded not to hide oneself from him, but rather <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall surely help with him&rdquo;</span>: one must see to help him and draw him close and raise him from his falling. And one must love him specifically, as the Targum renders <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall abandon&rdquo;</span> etc., as mentioned above.</p>

<p>For one must judge every person favorably. And even in a completely wicked person, one must find some merit. And through finding some point of good in him, one takes him out of his wickedness and brings him genuinely into the scale of merit, and he returns in <span class="key-term">teshuvah</span> [repentance]. As Rabbainu, may his light shine, wrote <span class="inline-source">(LM I:282)</span> on the verse <span class="verse">&ldquo;Yet a little while and the wicked is no more&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 37:10)</span>. See there. And this is the mitzvah of <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall surely help&rdquo;</span> &mdash; for the essential purpose of the mitzvah is love, as the Targum renders, etc., as mentioned above. For also to raise a person himself from his falling is only through love &mdash; namely, through bringing him into the scale of merit and love, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is what our Sages of blessed memory said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;An elder and it is not in accordance with his honor &mdash; he is exempt, and some say it is forbidden.&rdquo;</span> For when one engages in drawing people close to the service of Hashem, may He be blessed, to raise them from their fallings, one must guard one&rsquo;s honor very carefully &mdash; namely, that one should not draw close those who are not fit to be drawn close, for through them one&rsquo;s honor would be blemished, G&ndash;d forbid. As it is written regarding Moshe: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Go down&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 32:7)</span>, etc. &mdash; because he drew close the <span class="key-term">airev rav</span> [mixed multitude]. For these wicked ones are in the aspect of the <span class="key-term">airev rav</span>, who are the aspect of Aisav, as is brought. And of them it is said <span class="inline-source">(Obadiah 1:2)</span>: <span class="verse">&ldquo;You are greatly despised&rdquo;</span> &mdash; for they have no share in the <span class="key-term">kavod</span> of holiness. And therefore it is forbidden to draw them close, for one&rsquo;s honor would be blemished, G&ndash;d forbid, through them.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;an elder and it is not in accordance with his honor&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that it is forbidden to raise him from his falling when one sees that it is not in accordance with one&rsquo;s honor, meaning that one&rsquo;s honor would be blemished through this, G&ndash;d forbid, as mentioned above. For the essential thing is <span class="key-term">kavod</span>. For when one draws close to Hashem, may He be blessed, those who are fit to be drawn close, His honor, may He be blessed, is magnified. For this is the essential honor: when those who are far away draw close to His service, may He be blessed, as Rabbainu, may his light shine, wrote all this. And they become the aspect of the <span class="key-term">Haichal HaKodesh</span> [Holy Temple], in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and in His Temple everything says: &lsquo;Honor!&rsquo;&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 29:9)</span>. And this is the aspect of the nullification of the forbidden in sixty &mdash; the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;sixty are the queens&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Song of Songs 6:8)</span>, the aspect of the King of Honor, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">Haichal HaKodesh</span> mentioned above, through which the prohibition and evil within them is nullified. See all this in the discourse <i>&ldquo;Mi She&rsquo;Osaik L&rsquo;Karaiv&rdquo;</i> etc. <span class="inline-source">(LM I:59)</span>.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall surely help&rdquo;</span> &mdash; meaning, to support him and raise him from his falling. This is the aspect of the nullification of the forbidden in <span class="key-term">Samech</span> [ס, the letter whose numerical value is 60], as mentioned above, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Hashem supports all who fall&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 145:14)</span>. As our Sages of blessed memory said <span class="inline-source">(Berachos 4b)</span>: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Why is there no <i>Nun</i> in <i>Ashray</i>? Because it contains falling&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="verse">&ldquo;Yet even so, David returned and supported it through <i>ruach ha&rsquo;kodesh</i>, as it is written: &lsquo;Hashem supports all who fall.&rsquo;&rdquo;</span> It emerges that <span class="key-term">Samech</span> is the aspect of supporting the falling, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;She has fallen; she shall not rise again &mdash; the maiden of Israel&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Amos 5:2)</span>. And this is also the nullification of all prohibitions through [the letter] <span class="key-term">Samech</span>, for all prohibitions come from the aspect of fallen things, as explained above in the Laws of Mixtures. See there.</p>

<p>It emerges that the essential mitzvah of <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall surely help&rdquo;</span> &mdash; meaning, to support him and raise him from his falling &mdash; is through the aspect of <span class="key-term">kavod</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Samech</span>, the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;sixty are the queens,&rdquo;</span> etc., as mentioned above. And from there comes the support for all who fall, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Hashem supports,&rdquo;</span> etc., as mentioned above. And therefore those who are remote from <span class="key-term">kavod</span> and no longer have any hold in it &mdash; it is forbidden to draw them close, for the essential thing is <span class="key-term">kavod</span>, which is the root of all the souls of holiness, as mentioned above. And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;an elder and it is not in accordance with his honor,&rdquo;</span> as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And therefore there are two opinions: according to one opinion, he is exempt, but if he wants [to help], it is permitted; and according to the second opinion, it is forbidden. And each master stated one thing and the other master stated another, and they do not dispute one another. For it all depends on the degree of their wickedness and the extent of their distance from <span class="key-term">kavod</span>. For some are so far away that there is great danger in drawing them close, and because of this the Torah exempted the elder, for he is not obligated to endanger himself in such great danger. Nevertheless, if he wishes to go beyond the letter of the law and descend to raise even these &mdash; he certainly performs an exceedingly great mitzvah. But some are even more distant, to the point that there is an absolute prohibition to draw them close, and it is forbidden for him to endanger himself on their account, as found in the discourse mentioned above regarding the statement of our Sages of blessed memory: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Why are the eyes of the Tarmudians bleary?&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(LM I:59)</span>. But those who still have some hold in <span class="key-term">kavod</span>, even though they are very far &mdash; regarding them it is said <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall surely help,&rdquo;</span> as mentioned above, for this is the essential honor, as mentioned above.</p>

<p class="closing">Blessed is Hashem forever, Amen and Amen.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- PART III: PERIKAH U'TE'INAH, HALACHA 2 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="halacha-title">Laws of Unloading and Loading &mdash; Halacha 2</div>

<div class="torah-ref">Based on Likutay Moharan II:7 &mdash; <i>&ldquo;Ki M&rsquo;Rachamam Y&rsquo;nahagaim&rdquo;</i> &mdash; For the One Who has mercy on them shall lead them</div>

<p style="text-indent:0; text-align:center; font-style:italic; color: var(--accent-blue); margin-bottom:18px;"><span class="verse">&ldquo;When you see the donkey of one who hates you crouching beneath its burden, and you would hold back&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall surely help with him.&rdquo;</span></p>

<p>For it is found in the discourse <i>&ldquo;Vay&rsquo;hi Mi'Kaitz &mdash; Ki M&rsquo;Rachamam Y&rsquo;nahagaim&rdquo;</i> etc. in <i>Likutay Tinyana</i> <span class="inline-source">(LM II:7)</span>, that the essential <span class="key-term">rachamanus</span> [compassion] is when one of Israel falls into sins, G&ndash;d forbid. For this is a heavy burden that it is impossible for a Jew to bear at all &mdash; such a heavy burden, etc. See there. And one must have compassion on Israel, to extract them from sins and to instill <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> in them, etc. For one must illuminate the <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> in children and students, etc. See there. And through the combined aspect of &ldquo;child and student,&rdquo; from there the <span class="key-term">parnasah</span> [livelihood] is drawn, which the <span class="key-term">Malchus</span> receives from the &ldquo;sea of wisdom,&rdquo; etc. See there all this well.</p>

<p>And this is hinted at in the mitzvah mentioned above. For <span class="heb-word">sonay</span> [enemy], our Sages of blessed memory explained, refers to one whom you saw transgress a sin. And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;crouching beneath its burden&rdquo;</span> &mdash; for the heaviness of the burden overpowers him, which is the burden of sin. And because of this he crouches beneath his burden, for it is impossible for him to bear at all such a burden, as mentioned above. And this is <span class="verse">&ldquo;When you see the donkey of one who hates you crouching,&rdquo;</span> etc. For the overpowering of sin is in the aspect of <span class="heb-word">chomer</span> [materiality] and the animal spirit. For when the burden of sin overpowers, G&ndash;d forbid, one is not called by the name <span class="heb-word">adam</span> [human], for the essential humanity is <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span>. Rather, one is in the aspect of an animal in human form, as explained in the discourse mentioned above. See there.</p>

<p>And the Torah warned each person who sees his fellow upon whom the burden of sin has overpowered, G&ndash;d forbid &mdash; for only this is truly called a <span class="heb-word">masa</span> [burden], as mentioned above &mdash; that it is forbidden to hide one&rsquo;s eyes, but rather one is obligated to have compassion on one&rsquo;s fellow and to help him, to fulfill <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall surely help with him.&rdquo;</span> For it is incumbent upon each and every Jew to have compassion on one&rsquo;s fellow with the true compassion, which is greater than every other kind of compassion &mdash; namely, to help him unload from upon himself the heavy burden of sin, which it is impossible for him to bear at all, such a heavy burden, as mentioned above. For every person is obligated to endeavor to look after his fellow, to speak with him about <span class="key-term">yiras shamayim</span> [fear of Heaven], to extract him from the heavy burden of sins, which is heavier than all other burdens. For this is the essential compassion, as mentioned above. And this is <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall surely help with him.&rdquo;</span></p>

<p>And also the mitzvah itself in its literal sense &mdash; namely, actual <span class="key-term">perikah u&rsquo;te&rsquo;inah</span>, to help one&rsquo;s fellow actually unload the burden from upon his donkey &mdash; is also in this very aspect. For the burden upon the animal, which is his money and livelihood, is drawn from the &ldquo;sea of wisdom,&rdquo; which comes through the combined aspect of &ldquo;child and student&rdquo; &mdash; namely through illuminating <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> in child and student, in proportion to how much one extracts them from the heavy burden of sin. This connection is well understood in the discourse mentioned above. See there.</p>

<p>And therefore one who merits to emerge from the heavy burden of sins and merits <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> &mdash; which is the aspect of illuminating &ldquo;child and student&rdquo; &mdash; similarly, his livelihood comes to him easily. For from there is the essential source of livelihood, as mentioned above. And conversely, G&ndash;d forbid, one upon whom the burden of sin overpowers, G&ndash;d forbid, and who lacks <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span>, G&ndash;d forbid &mdash; then his livelihood comes with great heaviness and immense weariness, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;the people went about and gathered&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Numbers 11:8)</span> &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;in foolishness, they ground it in mills or crushed it in a mortar.&rdquo;</span> This is the aspect of the heaviness of livelihood for one who has not driven out the spirit of foolishness, as found in the holy Zohar, which hints at the heaviness of livelihood for one who lacks <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span>, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;A person&rsquo;s sustenance is as difficult as the splitting of the Sea of Reeds&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Pesachim 118a)</span>. For the splitting of the Sea of Reeds alludes to the &ldquo;sea of wisdom&rdquo; mentioned above. For this is the essential aspect of the splitting of the Sea of Reeds: that the sea of wisdom was split open and revealed, as is brought. This is the aspect of the &ldquo;sea of wisdom&rdquo; mentioned above that is revealed in proportion to how much one merits to emerge from sins, as mentioned above. And from there livelihood is drawn, as mentioned above. And this is <span class="verse">&ldquo;sustenance is as difficult as the splitting of the Sea of Reeds&rdquo;</span> &mdash; for specifically from there is sustenance and livelihood drawn, from the aspect of the splitting of the Sea of Reeds, from the aspect of the &ldquo;sea of wisdom&rdquo; mentioned above. For the essential difficulty of the splitting of the Sea of Reeds was because of sins, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;these are idolaters and these are idolaters,&rdquo;</span> as our Sages of blessed memory said. And similarly, sustenance is difficult, for in proportion to how much one merits to emerge from sins, so one merits that the sea of wisdom is revealed &mdash; which is the aspect of the splitting of the Sea of Reeds &mdash; and so one merits sustenance and livelihood, for from there livelihood is drawn, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>It emerges that the essential heaviness and yoke of livelihood is because of the heaviness of the burden of sins. And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;When you see the donkey of one who hates you crouching beneath its burden&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that the burden of his money and livelihood is heavy upon him, and he has suffering and great heaviness. And this derives only from the heavy burden of sins, as mentioned above. And this is the aspect of <span class="precise">&ldquo;one who hates you&rdquo;</span> &mdash; for <span class="heb-word">sonay</span> [enemy] is none other than one who transgressed a sin, as our Sages of blessed memory explained. And the Torah warned not to hold back from helping him, but rather one must abandon from the heart what one holds against him and help him, as the Targum renders: <span class="verse">&ldquo;You shall abandon what is in your heart against him, and you shall unload with him.&rdquo;</span></p>

<p>And at first glance the matter is puzzling. For granted, if the meaning of <span class="heb-word">sonay</span> were the simple sense &mdash; that he hates him on his own account, because of a quarrel or dispute or the like &mdash; it would be fitting to say <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall abandon,&rdquo;</span> etc., that one must forgive him. But since our Sages of blessed memory explained that the <span class="heb-word">sonay</span> stated in the Torah is because one saw him transgress a sin, how is it fitting to say <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall abandon what is in your heart against him&rdquo;</span>? Yet in truth, based on what is explained in the words of Rabbainu, of blessed memory, in many places &mdash; that one must judge every person favorably, and one must find merit even in a completely wicked person, for how is it possible that he has not done some small amount of good in his days? And through finding some good point in him, one genuinely brings him into the scale of merit, and it is possible to return him in <span class="key-term">teshuvah</span> through this, as brought on the verse <span class="verse">&ldquo;Yet a little while and the wicked is no more&rdquo;</span> etc. See there <span class="inline-source">(LM I:282)</span>.</p>

<p>And this is the matter mentioned above: that even though he is <span class="heb-word">son&rsquo;acha</span> &mdash; that you saw him transgress a sin &mdash; nevertheless, do not refrain from helping him. On the contrary: <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall abandon what is in your heart against him,&rdquo;</span> for you must find merit in him and have compassion on him and forgive him. For through finding merit in him, one genuinely brings him into the scale of merit, and one returns him in <span class="key-term">teshuvah</span>. It emerges that it is in the power of each Jew to forgive the sins of his fellow, for he can bring him into the scale of merit by finding some merit in him, as mentioned above. And therefore, when one sees that his fellow has suffering on the road, that his donkey crouches beneath its burden &mdash; and the heaviness of this burden is because of the heaviness of the burden of sin, as mentioned above &mdash; one is obligated to have compassion on him and forgive him, namely, to find merit in him and bring him into the scale of merit, as mentioned above, which is the essential compassion. And to help him unload the burden. And through abandoning the hatred and having compassion on him and instilling compassion within him, because one seeks and finds some merit in him &mdash; through this one genuinely brings him into the scale of merit and unloads from upon him the heavy burden of sins. And through this very act, one unloads from upon him the actual [physical] burden, for the essential heaviness of the burden is because of the burden of sin, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>For in truth, the essential purpose of this mitzvah of <span class="key-term">perikah u&rsquo;te&rsquo;inah</span> is for the sake of love and compassion, as our Sages of blessed memory said on the verse <span class="verse">&ldquo;You have established equity&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 99:4)</span>: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Do you have an enemy who sees&rdquo;</span> etc. For the essential purpose of the mitzvah is to unload the burden of sin, and this is accomplished through love and compassion, as mentioned above.</p>

<p class="closing">Blessed is Hashem forever, Amen.</p>

<p style="text-indent: 0; text-align: center; font-size: 0.9em; color: #888; margin: 10px 0;">
<i>[The following halacha, Perikah u&rsquo;Te&rsquo;inah 3 (corresponding to Avaidah u&rsquo;Metziah 3, &sect;15), is a cross-reference and has been included above in the subdivision.]</i>
</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- PART IV: PERIKAH U'TE'INAH, HALACHA 4 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="halacha-title">Laws of Unloading and Loading &mdash; Halacha 4</div>

<div class="torah-ref">Based on Likutay Moharan II:2 &mdash; <i>&ldquo;Y&rsquo;may Chanukah Haim Y&rsquo;may Hoda&rsquo;ah&rdquo;</i> &mdash; The days of Chanukah are days of thanksgiving (&sect;5)</div>

<!-- Section 1 -->
<div class="section-num">&sect; 1</div>

<p>One must draw the holiness of <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> into the six days of the week. For <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> is the aspect of a &ldquo;son,&rdquo; the aspect of rest for those above and those below, etc. And the weekdays are the aspect of a &ldquo;servant&rdquo; and sadness, etc. And one must draw the rest and joy of <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> into the weekdays, etc. And through this, the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> [simple unity] of the Blessed One is revealed &mdash; that all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> [diverse activities/phenomena] flow from the One Who is Simple, may He be blessed. This is impossible to understand through human intellect, but only through <span class="key-term">emunah</span> [faith] that is drawn through <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> &mdash; through drawing the holiness and joy of <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> into the weekdays, etc.</p>

<p>And through this, the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, may He be blessed, is revealed &mdash; that all the diverse activities flow from the One Who is Simple, may He be blessed, which is impossible to understand through human intellect, but only through <span class="key-term">emunah</span> drawn through <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span>, through drawing the holiness and joy of <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> into the six weekdays, etc. And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;an individual and a majority &mdash; the halachah follows the majority.&rdquo;</span> For when the many agree to the view of one &mdash; this is the aspect of diverse activities being included in the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>. And this is very precious before Hashem, may He be blessed, etc. See there.</p>

<!-- Section 2 -->
<div class="section-num">&sect; 2</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of the great emphasis placed on the mitzvah of <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall surely help&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that one should abandon the hatred in one&rsquo;s heart toward one&rsquo;s fellow and unload with him, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;When you see the donkey of one who hates you crouching beneath its burden, and you would hold back from helping him &mdash; you shall surely help with him,&rdquo;</span> and the Targum renders: <span class="verse">&ldquo;You shall abandon what is in your heart against him, and you shall unload with him.&rdquo;</span> And similarly our Sages of blessed memory said in the Gemara that this is the essential purpose of the mitzvah of <span class="key-term">perikah u&rsquo;te&rsquo;inah</span>.</p>

<p>For all the suffering that a person has from the heaviness of burdens &mdash; all of it derives from a blemish of the aspect mentioned above, namely, that one did not merit to properly connect all the diverse activities to the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, because one did not draw the holiness of <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> into the six weekdays, as mentioned above. For all the suffering that a person has, G&ndash;d forbid, in body, soul, and money, may the Merciful One save us &mdash; all of them are the aspect of burdens. For suffering is against one&rsquo;s will, and they are like a heavy burden upon him. And all of them come from the aspect of diverse activities when one does not endeavor to reveal and illuminate within them the aspect of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>. Then the multiplicity of changes intensifies and things do not proceed in the proper order fitting for them from their root, and from there come all the heaviness of burdens and all the suffering, G&ndash;d forbid.</p>

<p>For all suffering, G&ndash;d forbid, is the aspect of <span class="key-term">machlokes</span> [strife/conflict], for it derives from the conflict of the elements with one another. And it is against the person&rsquo;s will, for the person wants things to be thus, according to his will, that they should proceed in orderly fashion, but they stand against him and dispute with him and proceed not according to his will. And the greater the change against his will, the greater the suffering, G&ndash;d forbid. And all this derives from the blemish of the aspect mentioned above &mdash; that one did not endeavor to draw the joy and rest of <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> into the weekdays, and did not draw the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from within the diverse activities.</p>

<p>For according to the order by which the life-force flows from the One Who is Simple to all the diverse activities, everything should proceed in the proper order. For from Him, may He be blessed, no good is withheld, and He in His mercy, may He be blessed, created His world for good &mdash; that the life-force should flow from His simple unity to all the diverse activities, to each and every activity as is fitting, in the proper order, for good. Only because everything was created for the sake of man&rsquo;s free will &mdash; that according to one&rsquo;s complete faith and according to one&rsquo;s deeds, so one draws the life-force from the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> to all the diverse activities, for good, or to the contrary, G&ndash;d forbid. And therefore the essential rectification is through <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span>, when there is rest and cessation. Through <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span>, through drawing the holiness of <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> into the weekdays, through this the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from within the diverse activities, and then everything proceeds in the proper order. For from <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> the aspect of rest and cessation is drawn even to all the diverse activities that are done during the weekdays &mdash; to sweeten and nullify the aspect of sadness and the harsh servitude of <span class="heb-word">uvdin d&rsquo;chol</span> [weekday occupations], so that all of one&rsquo;s affairs and endeavors proceed in the proper order, without weariness and harsh labor.</p>

<p>But each person, according to the extent of his blemish in this &mdash; that he does not endeavor to draw the holiness of <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> into the weekdays and does not reveal the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from within the diverse activities &mdash; so the multiplicity of changes of the diverse activities intensifies and they do not proceed in the proper order, and from there come all the suffering, G&ndash;d forbid, which are the aspect of burdens, which are the aspect of <span class="key-term">machlokes</span>, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;When you see the donkey of one who hates you crouching beneath its burden&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that the burden is heavy upon him and the person has suffering from this. All of this derives from the blemish mentioned above, which is the blemish of <span class="key-term">machlokes</span>, which is the aspect of the blemish of <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span>, etc. For regarding <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;So that your ox and your donkey may rest, like you&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 23:12)</span>. And our Sages of blessed memory said: &ldquo;Give it rest.&rdquo; And from there, rest is drawn upon the ox and the donkey and the like also during the weekdays &mdash; so that even when work is done with them, the labor should not be excessively heavy upon them, as explained above, that one must draw the holiness of <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> into the weekdays, as mentioned above. And therefore, when the animal crouches beneath its burden, this derives from the aspect of the blemish of <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span>, which is the aspect of the blemish of <span class="key-term">machlokes</span>, etc., as mentioned above.</p>

<p>Therefore the verse warned that one should abandon the hatred in one&rsquo;s heart toward one&rsquo;s fellow, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;you shall surely help &mdash; you shall abandon what is in your heart against him, and you shall unload with him.&rdquo;</span> For the essential abandoning and helping that one helps him regarding the burden is through abandoning the hatred and seeking love &mdash; namely, through the nullification of <span class="key-term">machlokes</span> and the difference of opinions. Through this, all are included as one in the aspect of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, as explained above: that the more Israel is included together in greater love and friendship, the more the aspect of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from within the diverse activities, which is the aspect of the holiness of <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span>. Through this, all the heaviness of burdens and all the suffering are nullified, for rest is drawn upon everything, as mentioned above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- SUBDIVISION: HEFKER V'NICHSAY HA'GER -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="division-title">Ownerless Property and the Convert&rsquo;s Estate (<i>Hefker v&rsquo;Nichsay HaGer</i>)<br><span style="font-size:0.82em;">&sect;&sect; 3&ndash;4, continuing from Perikah u&rsquo;Te&rsquo;inah 4</span></div>

<!-- Section 3 -->
<div class="section-num">&sect; 3</div>

<p>This is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;whoever is first in the estate of a convert acquires it&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Bava Basra 54a)</span>. For the convert who converts &mdash; this is the aspect of the diverse activities that are very remote being included within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>. For the convert, who was initially a gentile from among the seventy nations, is the essential aspect of <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> [diverse activities]. For the holy nation of Israel is called <span class="verse">&ldquo;one nation in the land&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(II Samuel 7:23)</span>, and therefore they are in the aspect of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, as opposed to the seventy nations. For <span class="verse">&ldquo;the Torah and the Holy One, blessed is He, and Israel are all one,&rdquo;</span> and therefore the seventy souls of the house of Yaakov are called one <span class="heb-word">nefesh</span> [soul], while the six souls of Aisav are called <span class="heb-word">nefashos</span> [souls] in the plural, as Rashi explained there &mdash; for they are far from unity and simplicity, because they did not receive the Torah. And therefore they are the essential aspect of the diverse activities.</p>

<p>And when one of them comes and converts, this is the aspect of the very remote diverse activities being included within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>. For initially he was in the aspect of a very changed activity, as mentioned above. And now he wants to draw close to Hashem, may He be blessed, to the One Who is Simple, and to be included among Israel, <span class="verse">&ldquo;one nation in the land,&rdquo;</span> through whom is the essential inclusion of all the diverse activities within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>. For all the souls of Israel, the more they increase, the more they are included within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is the great level of the convert who converts, about whom the Torah warned to draw him close and to love him, as it is written <span class="inline-source">(Deuteronomy 10:19)</span>: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And you shall love the convert.&rdquo;</span> For this is very precious in the eyes of Hashem, may He be blessed, when the diverse activities are included within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>. And the more the activity is changed and remote, when it merits to overcome and be included in the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, the more precious it is. For this is His will, may He be blessed: that specifically through the very remote and changed activities, the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> should be revealed. This is the aspect of the great level of the <span class="key-term">ba&rsquo;al teshuvah</span> [penitent] that our Sages of blessed memory spoke of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;In the place where <i>ba&rsquo;alay teshuvah</i> stand, completely righteous people cannot stand&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Berachos 34b)</span>. For because they were initially very far through their sins &mdash; which is the essential aspect of the diverse activities, for through each sin, G&ndash;d forbid, one distances oneself from there to the <span class="heb-word">alma d&rsquo;feruda</span> [world of separation], G&ndash;d forbid, which is the essential aspect of the very remote changed activities, as our Sages of blessed memory said &mdash; and therefore when one returns in <span class="key-term">teshuvah</span>, the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from within the very remote and changed activities, which is very precious in the eyes of Hashem, may He be blessed, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And all the more so the convert, who was even more remote because he is not at all of the seed of Israel. Therefore when he comes to convert and is included in the holiness of Israel, <span class="verse">&ldquo;one nation in the land,&rdquo;</span> it is precious in the eyes of Hashem, may He be blessed, because the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from the very remote changed activities, which is very precious in the eyes of Hashem, may He be blessed. And the more changed and remote the activities, the more precious it is in His eyes, may He be blessed, when the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from there, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of what is found in the holy Zohar and brought in the words of Rabbainu, of blessed memory: <span class="verse">&ldquo;When Yisro came and said, &lsquo;Now I know that Hashem is great,&rsquo; then the Name of the Holy One, blessed is He, was exalted and glorified above and below,&rdquo;</span> etc., as mentioned above.</p>

<!-- Section 4 -->
<div class="section-num">&sect; 4</div>

<p>It emerges that the drawing close of the convert to the holiness of Israel is the aspect of the diverse activities being included within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, which is the aspect of the holiness of <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> being drawn into the weekdays. This is drawn through all the rectifications explained there, whose essence is through the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah</span> [thanksgiving], <span class="key-term">halachah</span>, etc. And it is explained there that this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">holadah</span> [birth/generation] &mdash; the aspect of <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraisah</span> [supporters of Torah] who diminish their money and wealth to sustain the <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span> [Torah scholars]. Through this, <span class="key-term">halachos</span> are born, etc. Through this, truth shines, etc., until one merits that the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from within the diverse activities, etc.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of why children inherit their father&rsquo;s money. For all the birth of children is drawn through the aspect mentioned above &mdash; through <span class="key-term">halachah</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraisah</span>. From there come all the births in the world &mdash; whether children that one begets, or all the profit and wealth and livelihood that each person earns, which is called by the name <span class="heb-word">laidah</span> [birth]. For everything in the world is drawn through the <span class="key-term">halachos</span> that are born by the true <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span> through the <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraisah</span> who sustain them. For it is known that all <span class="key-term">hashpa&rsquo;ah</span> [abundance] and all births are drawn from the Torah. (And even though for the most part wealth is found among those distant from <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span>, etc. &mdash; this is because of the intensification of the exile, which causes the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> of Israel to be drawn to them, etc. And everything is for the good, as explained elsewhere. But in any case, the entire root of the <span class="key-term">shefa</span> comes only from the <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span>, etc., as mentioned above.)</p>

<p>And therefore when a person passes away, his money belongs to his children whom he fathered, for all their birth was drawn from there &mdash; from the money of the <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraisah</span>, from where comes all the money in the world and all the births in the world, as mentioned above. And therefore, in truth the essential thing is that the children should take the money they inherit and sustain with it the true <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span>, so that through this they will in turn give birth to children in holiness &mdash; through the <span class="key-term">halachos</span> that the <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span> will birth through their money, as mentioned above. Through this, His G&ndash;dliness, may He be blessed, will be revealed from generation to generation forever, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and from generation to generation is His faithfulness,&rdquo;</span> which concludes the psalm <i>Mizmor L&rsquo;Sodah</i> [Psalm 100], which speaks of all this &mdash; birth and thanksgiving and <span class="key-term">halachah</span> &mdash; as explained there in the Torah [discourse] mentioned above.</p>

<p>And therefore the convert who converts &mdash; which is the aspect of diverse activities being included within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, which is drawn from the aspect of the <span class="key-term">halachos</span> drawn through the <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraisah</span>, etc., from where comes all the money in the world &mdash; therefore when the convert dies, all his money returns to Israel, and <span class="verse">&ldquo;whoever is first in the convert&rsquo;s estate acquires it.&rdquo;</span> For all of Israel are, relative to the convert, in the aspect of <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span>, since they are all included in the receiving of the Torah. And all his drawing-close was through his money ascending and being included in the holiness of Israel &mdash; the aspect of <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span>, from where came the birth of his soul to be included in the holiness of Israel, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;a convert who converts is like a newborn child&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Yevamos 22a)</span>. And therefore when he dies and has not left children who were born in the holiness of Israel, his money returns to Israel, and whoever is first acquires it &mdash; for from there was the essential source of his drawing close to the holiness of Israel, which is the aspect of birth, the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;a convert who converts,&rdquo;</span> etc. For everything is drawn from the aspect of the <span class="key-term">halachos</span> that are born through the money, etc., as mentioned above. Through this, one merits all the above, until the diverse activities are included within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> &mdash; which is the essential aspect of the drawing close of the convert to the holiness of Israel, as mentioned above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- HEFKER §5 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;5</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And Avram took&hellip; and all their possessions that they had acquired, and the souls they had made&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Genesis 12:5)</span> &mdash; which are the converts. For the essential drawing-close of the converts comes through the wealth and riches that Avraham Avinu received &mdash; in the aspect of the true tzadik &mdash; through the <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraisah</span>, as above. And this is the aspect of the great wealth they took out of Egypt, through which many converts were drawn close &mdash; namely Yisro, etc. &mdash; meaning as above. And therefore in the future, when all wealth returns to Israel as it is written <span class="verse">&ldquo;Instead of bronze I will bring gold&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Isaiah 60:17)</span>, etc. &mdash; then all will convert, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Then I will turn to the peoples a pure language, that they may all call upon the Name of Hashem, to serve Him with one shoulder&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Zephaniah 3:9)</span>. For all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> in the world, the very remote and greatly changed, will be included within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> &mdash; which is the essential aspect of His greatness and glory, may He be blessed, as above. May it be speedily in our days, Amen.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- HEFKER §6 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;6</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">hefkair</span> [ownerless property]. For the essential law of <span class="key-term">hefkair</span> is learned from <span class="key-term">Shemitah</span> [the sabbatical year], as is explained in the Gemara, which learned it from the verse <span class="verse">&ldquo;And the seventh year you shall let it rest and lie fallow&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 23:11)</span>, etc., and as is brought in the <i>Shulchan Aruch</i> that one must declare ownerless as in Shemitah, etc. And the entire matter of Shemitah is the aspect mentioned above. For Shemitah is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span>, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;A year of complete rest shall it be for the land&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Leviticus 25:4)</span>, and as Rashi explains: &ldquo;Like Shabbos Baraishis,&rdquo; etc. That is, in the seventh year, the holiness of Shabbos is drawn upon the land. And therefore all the fruits and produce of the land are <span class="key-term">hefkair</span> to all, because all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> and all the diverse opinions are nullified and are included within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>. And therefore all the produce is ownerless to all &mdash; for it is forbidden that there should be any insistence or difference of opinion over the produce in the seventh year, to say that this produce belongs to the owner of this field and that produce belongs to the owner of another field &mdash; for that would be the aspect of diverse activities and difference of opinions. For now, all are equal, because the land is then included within the aspect of Shabbos, where all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> are included together within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, where everything is included together, and it is forbidden that there be any difference of opinion and insistence among them.</p>

<p>And therefore all labors of the land are then forbidden, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Your field you shall not sow,&rdquo;</span> etc., <span class="verse">&ldquo;a year of complete rest shall it be for the land&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Leviticus 25:4&ndash;5)</span>. For then it is the aspect of Shabbos, when the aspect of the servant Metatron is nullified and is included within the aspect of the son, the aspect of <span class="heb-word">naicha</span> [rest]. And because the essential aspect of servitude takes hold most strongly in the aspect of the land &mdash; where all the hard labors are, which were drawn about through the sin of Adam HaRishon, when it was decreed <span class="verse">&ldquo;Cursed is the ground because of you; in sorrow shall you eat of it&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Genesis 3:17)</span> &mdash; therefore it is there that the essential rectification is needed. Therefore, the main prohibition of labor in Shemitah applies to the labor of the land &mdash; to nullify from there the aspect of servitude through the aspect of Shabbos, as above. And similarly, the entire nullification of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> applies to the produce of the land: it is forbidden for each person to hold onto his produce as if it belongs to him alone and to be insistent, G&ndash;d forbid, against his fellow, preventing him from eating from it &mdash; for that would be the aspect of difference of opinions, the aspect of diverse activities. And now, in Shemitah, all of this is forbidden &mdash; for now one must draw the holiness of Shabbos upon the land, and then all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, which are the aspect of all the diverse opinions, are nullified and included as one within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, and then all servitude is nullified, as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- HEFKER §7 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;7</div>

<p>And now one understands well what our Sages of blessed memory said: that the entire exile of Bavel [Babylon], seventy years, was on account of the seventy sabbatical years that they had annulled &mdash; as they expounded from the verse <span class="verse">&ldquo;Then the land shall be appeased for its sabbaths&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Leviticus 26:34)</span>, etc. For the essential cause of all the exiles is that the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> overpower, through an abundance of divergent opinions and <span class="key-term">machlokes</span> [strife], until they are not included within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>. Then the seventy nations dominate &mdash; they who are the essential aspect of <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, as above &mdash; and they overpower Israel, the holy nation, who are comprised of the seventy souls of the house of Yaakov, whose entire labor in Torah and mitzvos is to include within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> &mdash; which is the essential ultimate purpose of all service, for this is very precious to Hashem, may He be blessed, as above. And therefore, because they blemished the mitzvah of Shemitah &mdash; through which the diverse opinions are nullified, etc., as above &mdash; therefore through this very transgression the exile came about, which is drawn from divergent opinions and strife, as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- HEFKER §8 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;8</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of what Moshe said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Indeed, the matter is known!&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 2:14)</span> &mdash; when he saw <span class="key-term">machlokes</span> among Israel, he then said: &ldquo;Now the matter is known &mdash; why Israel is so singled out to be in exile &mdash; for I see that they are deserving of it on account of the <span class="key-term">machlokes</span>,&rdquo; as Rashi explains there in the parashah. This means as above: that the essential exile of Israel, in which the nations rule over them, comes through <span class="key-term">machlokes</span> &mdash; which is the aspect of the overpowering of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> through many divergences, until they are not included within one <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span>, and the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is not revealed. Then the nations overpower &mdash; they who are drawn from the <span class="heb-word">alma d&rsquo;feruda</span> [world of separation], from the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, as above &mdash; and Israel, <span class="verse">&ldquo;one nation,&rdquo;</span> is in exile among them, and the <span class="key-term">Shechinah</span> is with them in exile, as it were &mdash; for the overpowering of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> dominates until it conceals and hides the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, which is the essential holiness of Israel, &ldquo;one nation,&rdquo; as above.</p>

<p>And similarly, the exile of Bavel came about because they mocked the messengers of G&ndash;d, etc., and because they annulled the sabbatical years &mdash; through all of which the aspect of the seventy nations, who are rooted in the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, overpowered Israel, &ldquo;one nation,&rdquo; as above. And especially this last, long exile, which began from the destruction of the Second Temple &mdash; the essential destruction came about through <span class="key-term">sin&rsquo;as chinam</span> [baseless hatred], as our Sages of blessed memory said. And because the baseless hatred then intensified so greatly, as our Sages said, therefore the exile has been prolonged so greatly, in our many sins &mdash; for the Satan still dances among us, multiplying <span class="key-term">machlokes</span> among Israel in many forms, and especially among the <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span>. The entire prolonging of the exile is on account of this, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And I will surely hide [My face]&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Deuteronomy 31:18)</span> &mdash; that the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is not revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, on account of the abundance of <span class="key-term">machlokes</span> and divergent opinions, as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- HEFKER §9 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;9</div>

<p>And for this reason, Moshe greatly refused his mission at the vision of the burning bush, and Hashem, may He be blessed, contended with him for seven days to go and redeem Israel, but he did not want to &mdash; as is brought in Rashi&rsquo;s commentary there. All of this was because he saw and understood the great intensity of the divergent opinions among Israel, through the disputants and slanderers &mdash; Dasan and Aviram, etc. Therefore he foresaw the many complaints and trials with which they would test Hashem, may He be blessed, until they would come to the sin of the Golden Calf &mdash; through which the Bais HaMikdash would be destroyed and they would return to exile, etc. Therefore he did not want to begin to go and engage in this matter at all, and said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;I am not a man of words, not from yesterday&hellip;&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 4:10)</span> &mdash; hinting that it was still difficult to draw down the completeness of the fourfold speech (as explained there in the Torah discourse mentioned above), through which one draws the holiness of Shabbos into the weekdays, through which the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, through which the power of Egypt and all the nations ruling over Israel &mdash; who are the aspect of <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> &mdash; would be nullified, as above. But now the speech was not yet complete, for <span class="verse">&ldquo;I am not a man of words,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; and the <span class="key-term">machlokes</span>, the aspect of the overpowering of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, kept increasing &mdash; therefore he did not want to go on his mission.</p>

<p>And even at the end, when Hashem said to him <span class="verse">&ldquo;Who gave man a mouth?&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 4:11)</span> etc., he replied: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Send, please, by the hand You will send&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 4:13)</span> &mdash; &ldquo;for I know that I will not be their final redeemer,&rdquo; etc., as our Sages said. For the essential thing was that he gazed with his holy spirit upon the end of this last long exile, which would be prolonged through the abundance of <span class="key-term">machlokes</span>, as above &mdash; and therefore he refused to go.</p>

<p>And [Hashem] said to him: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Is there not Aharon your brother, the Levite?&hellip; Behold, he is coming out to meet you, and he will see you and rejoice in his heart&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 4:14)</span>. That is, He revealed to him that even though it is not yet possible to draw down peace in its completeness &mdash; to harmonize all the divergent opinions together, upon which the redemption depends, as above &mdash; nevertheless, through Aharon and his disciples who will be included with him in love and joy, through this the redemption will come. And similarly He hinted to him regarding the very end [of history]: that in every generation, through the few tzadikim and upright people who are included together with the true tzadik, the <span class="heb-word">Rebbe</span> &mdash; who is the aspect of Moshe &mdash; through this itself, the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, until ultimately there will be a complete redemption through this.</p>

<p>And therefore our Sages of blessed memory exhorted: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Be of the disciples of Aharon &mdash; loving peace and pursuing peace&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Avos 1:12)</span>, etc. For the essential first redemption that came about through Moshe was through Aharon &mdash; through his going out to meet him in great peace, as above. And similarly the final redemption will come about through Eliyahu, who will make peace in the world &mdash; and through this, Mashiach will come speedily in our days &mdash; for Eliyahu is of the seed of Aharon, as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- HEFKER §10 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;10</div>

<p>For the Torah [discourse] mentioned above has its end embedded in its beginning (and so too all the Toros, etc., as is explained elsewhere) and its beginning in its end. For it is explained in the Torah mentioned above that <span class="key-term">todah</span> &mdash; meaning, to give thanks and praise to Hashem, may He be blessed, always &mdash; this is the aspect of the delight of the World to Come, etc. And it is the aspect of the study of <span class="key-term">halachos</span>, etc. And for this reason the <span class="key-term">todah</span> is called <span class="key-term">halachah</span> &mdash; on account of the <span class="heb-word">tahaluchos</span> [courses/processions] of the bloods, which flow in their proper order when one emerges from distress. For at first, in a time of distress, the bloods rush upon the heart, etc. And afterward, when one emerges from the distress, the bloods flow in their proper order, etc. And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">holadah</span> [birth], etc. And through this, truth illuminates within the fourfold speech, etc. And through the completeness of the speech, which is bound to Shabbos, the holiness of Shabbos is drawn into the six weekdays, etc. And through this, the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> &mdash; which is very precious to Hashem, may He be blessed &mdash; and this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;the <i>halachah</i> follows the majority,&rdquo;</span> for when many agree to one <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span>, this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> being included within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> &mdash; for each one has his own unique opinion, and they are all included together, etc. See all of this there well, for this is the summary of the entire Torah mentioned above, from beginning to end.</p>

<p>It turns out that the essential inclusion of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> comes about through <span class="key-term">todah/halachah</span> &mdash; which comes about through the orderly procession of the bloods when one emerges from distress, when one then brings a <span class="key-term">todah</span> [thanksgiving offering], which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">halachah</span> &mdash; and through this, truth illuminates, etc. For at first, when the bloods were rushing upon the heart, it was in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;men of blood hate the wholesome&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Proverbs 29:10)</span>, etc. And now, when the bloods flow in their proper order, truth illuminates &mdash; through which one merits all the above, until all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> are included, etc., as above. And from the opposite it is self-evident: when the bloods rush upon the heart, G&ndash;d forbid, in a time of distress &mdash; then truth does not illuminate, as above, and then the speech is not complete, and then the holiness of Shabbos is not drawn into the weekdays, and then the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> are not included together, etc. For from the affirmative you can infer the negative, and in truth each depends upon the other: the more the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> overpower, G&ndash;d forbid, through many divergences and are not included together &mdash; the more the sufferings and exiles intensify, G&ndash;d forbid. For all the afflictions, distresses, and exiles come about through the overpowering of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> through many divergences that are not included together, and the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> does not illuminate within them &mdash; which is the essential rectification of all the worlds and all that is in them, in every detail.</p>

<p>And this itself is the aspect of the overpowering of the bloods upon the heart in a time of distress, G&ndash;d save us. For all the distresses and afflictions come about because the many divergences are not conducted in an equal balance. For Hashem, may He be blessed, created the entire world with many wondrous divergences, and all of them are included within the four elements &mdash; fire, air, water, earth &mdash; from which come all the inanimate, vegetative, living, and speaking, which are the aspect of the four general worlds: <span class="key-term">Atzilus, Beriah, Yetzirah, Asiyah</span>, as is known. And all of them are drawn from His <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, may He be blessed &mdash; for at their root they are all included in one. But in their descent below, He created them with wondrous divergences, for the elements differ greatly from one another &mdash; this one fire and this one water, this one air and this one earth, this one hot and dry and this one cold and moist, etc. How much more so all the creatures that came into being from them, whose divergences are without number. And all of them need to be conducted in an equal balance &mdash; that the elements should be evenly tempered as they were drawn from the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, to carry out their function properly &mdash; and then everything proceeds as it should. But when the divergences multiply and the elements overpower one another not in their proper order, from this come all the afflictions and all the distresses, G&ndash;d forbid, and similarly all the exiles under the nations &mdash; for the seventy nations are the essential aspect of <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, as above, and as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;When the Most High gave nations their inheritance, when He separated the children of man, He set the boundaries of the peoples according to the number of the children of Israel&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Deuteronomy 32:8)</span>. That is, the nations exist in the aspect of separation &mdash; the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;when He separated the children of man&rdquo;</span> &mdash; as above, for they are the essential aspect of <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>: seventy nations corresponding to the seventy souls of the house of Yaakov &mdash; the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;He set the boundaries of the peoples according to the number of the children of Israel,&rdquo;</span> as Rashi explains there.</p>

<p>And according to the proper order of creation, and as it will be in the future: all the seventy nations must be nullified and included within the seventy souls of the house of Yaakov, who are reckoned as one and are included within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> &mdash; in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;for the portion of Hashem is His people,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Deuteronomy 32:9)</span>. And this is the entire rectification of creation. But when the Satan overpowers and the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> are not included together &mdash; through the abundance of <span class="key-term">machlokes</span> &mdash; then the seventy nations, who are the essential <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, overpower Israel, G&ndash;d forbid, as above. And similarly, through this come, G&ndash;d forbid, many, many distresses and afflictions &mdash; all of which come about because the divergences of all four elements are not properly tempered and are not properly included together, as above.</p>

<p>And this itself is the aspect of the bloods rushing upon the heart in a time of distress, G&ndash;d forbid. For all the life-force is in the blood, and the life-force spreads to all the limbs and senses, which contain many divergences. And the root of the life-force, which is the <span class="key-term">neshamah</span> [soul], is one single power, and from it are drawn all the divergences that exist in the limbs of a person, which are composed of four elements. And everything is in the aspect mentioned above: everything needs to be conducted in an equal balance. And when <span class="key-term">machlokes</span> arises among them and the divergences multiply, from this come all the distresses and afflictions, G&ndash;d forbid, and the bloods &mdash; in which the life-force flows &mdash; become confused, and then they rush upon the heart. And this itself is the aspect of the Egyptian exile, which includes all the exiles &mdash; for the essential exile was the aspect of the overpowering of the bloods, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And I passed over you and I saw you wallowing in your bloods&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Ezekiel 16:6)</span>, etc., and as is explained in the Kavanos of the Ari z&rdquo;l at length.</p>

<p>It turns out that the more the divergences of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> overpower, G&ndash;d forbid, when they are not included together &mdash; the more the bloods that rush upon the heart intensify. And conversely: the more the bloods rush upon the heart, G&ndash;d forbid &mdash; through which truth does not illuminate, etc. &mdash; the more the divergences of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> overpower, when they are not included together, as above. And so it goes, cycling, G&ndash;d forbid. And therefore, in truth, the beginning of the redemption is exceedingly difficult &mdash; and therefore Moshe refused to go, as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- HEFKER §11 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;11</div>

<p>But Hashem, may He be blessed, compelled him to go. For Hashem, may He be blessed, performed great wonders even though Israel were not worthy, and He performed great and awesome signs and miracles in Egypt. And through all of this, He demonstrated that all the diverse activities come from Him, may He be blessed, Himself, and they are in His hand like clay in the hand of the potter, and He can change them at any time as He wishes &mdash; for He can make a staff into a snake and a snake into a staff, and water into blood and then blood back into water, and so with all of them. For all the diverse activities are in His hand, for they all are drawn from Him alone, from His <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>. And through this He brought them out of Egypt and out of all the distresses, from the flooding of the bloods, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And I said to you: In your blood, live!&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Ezekiel 16:6)</span>, etc. And everything was in order that they should give thanks and praise His Name, may He be blessed, always, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;In order that My Name be declared throughout all the earth&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 9:16)</span>, and <span class="verse">&ldquo;in order that you tell in the ears of your child and your grandchild&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 10:2)</span>, etc.</p>

<p>And so Israel did, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And the people believed, and they heard that Hashem had remembered the children of Israel, and that He had seen their affliction, and they bowed and prostrated themselves&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 4:31)</span>. The bowing and prostrating &mdash; this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span> [thanksgiving] with a whole heart, the aspect of the bowing of <span class="heb-word">Modim</span>. And as soon as they began to draw forth the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah</span>, truth began to illuminate, etc. &mdash; through which the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> began to illuminate. And correspondingly, the power of the Egyptians was nullified &mdash; they who draw sustenance from the divergences of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> when they are not included together. And the more their power was nullified and the more the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> illuminated, the more the processions of blood returned to flow in their proper order &mdash; and so it cycled around for the good until they merited to leave Egypt.</p>

<p>And then, on that very night, they sang a song and <span class="key-term">Hallel</span>, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The song shall be yours like the night when a festival is sanctified&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Isaiah 30:29)</span>. And then they drew forth the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah</span> even more &mdash; for this is the essence of the redemption &mdash; until they merited the splitting of the Sea of Reeds, which was the completion of their redemption. For then they sang the Song at the Sea with great joy, because then the <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span> was completed in wondrous fullness through the Song at the Sea &mdash; for each depends upon the other, as above. And the essential merit for all of this was through Aharon, who did not dispute with Moshe &mdash; on the contrary, he went out to meet him with joy. And Aharon was a prophet and the great one of the generation, and the majority of Israel relied upon him and were included with Moshe through him. And through this was the essential revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> &mdash; through many agreeing to one true <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span>, as above &mdash; and this was accomplished through Aharon, as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- HEFKER §12 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;12</div>

<p>And the essential intent of our words is that each person should understand from all this hints for himself &mdash; to revive and restore his soul at all times, in all that passes over him throughout all the days of his life. For upon every person it is inevitable that many, many kinds of misfortunes and troubles pass over him, etc. &mdash; for <span class="verse">&ldquo;man is born to toil&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Job 5:7)</span>, and as our Sages of blessed memory said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;All bodies are subject to misfortune&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Berachos 5a)</span>, etc. Especially in this exile, where troubles press upon us &mdash; and we have no vitality except through the expanses that Hashem, may He be blessed, grants us between one trouble and the next, and also within the trouble itself there are great expanses, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;In distress, You expanded for me&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 4:2)</span>, as is explained in Torah 195. And it is known that whatever passes over a person, certainly the intent of Hashem, may He be blessed, is for good &mdash; in order to remind him to return and draw close through it, and to scour away transgression and seal up sins, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;For He said: Surely they will return from iniquity&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Isaiah 63:8)</span>.</p>

<p>But many people offer themselves false excuses and deceive themselves, saying that because of the abundance of troubles and afflictions they are unable to learn and to pray and to draw close to Hashem, may He be blessed. But in truth it is the very opposite &mdash; for all the troubles and hardships and afflictions that Hashem, may He be blessed, sends upon each person, to each one according to his sins &mdash; everything is only to draw close and not to push away. For the intent of Hashem, may He be blessed, is certainly for good and not for evil, G&ndash;d forbid &mdash; and as our Sages of blessed memory said, that a person is obligated to say at all times: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Whatever the Merciful One does, He does for the good&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Berachos 60b)</span>.</p>

<p>Therefore, the essential counsel is through the path mentioned above &mdash; to accustom oneself to <span class="key-term">todah</span> and <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span> to Hashem, may He be blessed, which is the aspect of the delight of the World to Come &mdash; to give thanks and praise to Hashem, may He be blessed, for all the kindnesses and wonders He has done with us until now, and that He has saved and delivered one&rsquo;s soul from how many troubles and hardships in body, soul, and money. As we say on Shabbos and Yom Tov in <i>Nishmas</i>: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Were our mouths full of song as the sea&hellip; we would not suffice to thank You&hellip; for even one of a thousand thousand, thousands of thousands, and myriads of myriads of times the good things&hellip; that You have done with our fathers and with us.&rdquo;</span> And similarly, we say every day three times: <span class="verse">&ldquo;We thank You&hellip; for Your miracles that are with us every day, and for Your wonders and good things at every time &mdash; evening and morning and afternoon,&rdquo;</span> etc.</p>

<p>For upon every person in the world, certainly many troubles have already passed and he was saved from them, or he was saved from many troubles that he saw come upon others but that never came upon him at all &mdash; and as our Sages of blessed memory said on the verse: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Who alone does great wonders, and blessed is His glorious Name forever&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 72:18&ndash;19)</span> &mdash; &ldquo;The one who experiences a miracle does not himself recognize his miracle,&rdquo; etc. For this reason our Sages of blessed memory established for us to say every day: &ldquo;For Your miracles that are with us every day,&rdquo; etc., as above. And therefore one must give thanks and praise to Hashem, may He be blessed, with a whole heart for all of this.</p>

<p>And the main thing is to give thanks and praise Him, may He be blessed, for the essential, eternal kindness and good &mdash; that He performed His great, wondrous kindness with us and set us apart from those who go astray, and chose us from all the nations and gave us His Torah. And even when one knows his own lowliness and failings &mdash; even so, it is a wondrous kindness that He did not make me a gentile. And also, within every Jew there are many good points, as is explained on the verse <span class="verse">&ldquo;I will sing to my G&ndash;d while I yet live&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 146:2; LM I:282)</span>, etc. And with all of this one must revive himself and give praise and thanksgiving with joy every day to Hashem, may He be blessed, for this. And especially at a time when some trouble or affliction passes over him, G&ndash;d forbid, may the Merciful One save us &mdash; precisely then he should remember all the kindnesses and good things that Hashem, may He be blessed, has done with us until now, as above. And also within the trouble itself, there are certainly many expanses, if one looks at them with the eye of truth, as above. And for all of this he should give <span class="key-term">todah</span> and <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span> and <span class="key-term">Hallel</span> to Hashem, may He be blessed. And through this, he will merit to be saved from the trouble &mdash; for as soon as he gives thanks and praises Hashem, may He be blessed, and draws forth the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah/halachah</span>, as above, truth will illuminate and the speech will be completed, and he will be able to engage in Torah and prayer &mdash; which are the lines of truth &mdash; and to speak words of <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span> and <span class="key-term">teshuvah</span>, etc. And through this the speech will be completed, through which the holiness of Shabbos will be drawn down, and it will be revealed that all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> are drawn from the <span class="key-term">Echad Ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, may He be blessed &mdash; through which the troubles that come from the many divergences are nullified, as above. And the more the divergences from which the troubles come are nullified, the more one increases the <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span> and births more <span class="key-term">halachos</span>, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;the goings (<i>halichos</i>) of the world&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Habakkuk 3:6)</span> &mdash; that one will merit to find through the <span class="key-term">halachos</span> a path and a way to draw close to Hashem, may He be blessed, from whatever passes over him. And the more the <span class="key-term">todah/halachah</span> grows, the more the divergences of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> are nullified and are included within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> even more &mdash; which is the aspect of the nullification of the trouble, as above. And so it cycles around until one emerges from the trouble entirely, as above.</p>

<p>And also: through finding an expansion within the trouble itself and engaging in giving thanks and praise to Hashem, may He be blessed, for all the kindnesses He has already done for him since his earliest days, and for all the expanses He grants him even now &mdash; through this, precisely, one will be able to pray and beseech Hashem, may He be blessed, and pour out his speech before Him, to lay out his entire conversation before Him, may He be blessed, and to plead before Him: &ldquo;Behold, Your kindness has already been great toward me, that You have saved my soul from the lowest depths, to be among the seed of Israel, Your servants. Have compassion and mercy upon me now as well, and deliver me from this trouble and these afflictions and this hardship,&rdquo; etc. And as Dovid said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;You have been my help; do not abandon me and do not forsake me, G&ndash;d of my salvation!&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 27:9)</span>. For this is the essential argument before Hashem, may He be blessed: even if, G&ndash;d forbid, I have no merit, behold, You have already made Your kindness great upon me, and You have been my help &mdash; now too, do not abandon me and do not forsake me, G&ndash;d of my salvation! (And see in the Laws of <i>Kil&rsquo;ay Bahaimah</i>, Halacha 4, based on this Torah, where this matter is explained at length; see there.)</p>

<p>And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The deep calls unto the deep at the sound of Your channels; all Your waves and billows have passed over me&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 42:8)</span> &mdash; that Dovid HaMelech cries out that the troubles, which are as vast and deep as actual abysses, intensify greatly, and as Rashi explains there: &ldquo;One trouble calls to its fellow,&rdquo; etc. &ldquo;And all Your waves and billows&rdquo; &mdash; which are the abundance of hardships, etc. &mdash; &ldquo;have passed over me&rdquo; &mdash; until hope was almost lost, G&ndash;d forbid. But in this I sustain myself and still hope for salvation: <span class="verse">&ldquo;By day Hashem commands His kindness&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 42:9)</span> &mdash; for even though the troubles are great, especially the troubles of the soul &mdash; that we are like ones rebuked before our Father in Heaven because of our many failings, etc. &mdash; even so, <span class="verse">&ldquo;by day Hashem commands His kindness.&rdquo;</span> And <span class="heb-word">yomam</span> [by day] means every single day, as Rashi explains elsewhere <span class="inline-source">(on Ezekiel 12)</span> &mdash; meaning that every single day, Hashem, may He be blessed, commands His kindness upon us, for He performs miracles and wonders with us every day. And these indeed are His mighty acts, these indeed are His awesome deeds: that we survive in so bitter an exile, in body and soul and money and livelihood, etc.</p>

<p>And through this: <span class="verse">&ldquo;and at night His song is with me&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 42:9)</span> &mdash; that through the kindnesses and wonders that Hashem, may He be blessed, does with us every single day, through this even at night His song is with me. That is, even in the time of trouble and darkness itself, which is the aspect of night &mdash; even then I say song and thanksgiving and praise to Hashem, may He be blessed, for all the kindnesses He has already done with us, and that even now He expands for us, as above. And through this, precisely: <span class="verse">&ldquo;a prayer to the G&ndash;d of my life&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 42:9)</span> &mdash; that I am able to pray to Hashem, may He be blessed, as above, in the aspect of &ldquo;giving thanks for the past and entreating for the future&rdquo; &mdash; for precisely through giving thanks for the past, one is able to entreat for the future. (And as is explained in the Laws of <i>Kil&rsquo;ay Bahaimah</i> mentioned above, at length; see there.)</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- HEFKER §13 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;13</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of what our Sages of blessed memory said <span class="inline-source">(Avodah Zarah, Chapter 1 [4a])</span>, and this is their language: &ldquo;And this is what Rava said: What is meant by the verse <span class="verse">&lsquo;But He will not stretch out His hand to the <i>pid</i>; when they cry out He saves them&rsquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Job 30:24)</span>? The Holy One, blessed be He, said: When I judge Israel, I do not judge them like the nations of the world, regarding whom it is written: <span class="verse">&lsquo;Ruin, ruin, ruin I shall make it!&rsquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Ezekiel 21:32)</span>. Rather, Israel &mdash; I exact from them a little at a time, like the <i>pid</i> [pecking] of chickens that peck at the refuse-heap. Another interpretation: Even if Israel perform mitzvos before Me only a little, like the <i>pid</i> of chickens that peck at the refuse-heap, I combine it into a great reckoning, as it says: <span class="verse">&lsquo;When they cry out, He saves them.&rsquo;</span> Another interpretation: In the reward for crying out before Me, I will save them. And this is what Rava said: What is meant by the verse <span class="verse">&lsquo;And I will redeem them, but they have spoken lies about Me&rsquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Hosea 7:13)</span>? &lsquo;I said: I will redeem them through their money in this world so that they merit the World to Come &mdash; but they have spoken lies about Me.&rsquo; And this is what Rav Pappi said in the name of Rava: What is meant by the verse <span class="verse">&lsquo;And I have chastised them, I have strengthened their arms &mdash; yet they think evil of Me&rsquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Hosea 7:15)</span>? The Holy One, blessed be He, said: &lsquo;I said: I will chastise them with sufferings in this world in order that their arms be strengthened for the World to Come &mdash; yet they think evil of Me.&rsquo;&rdquo; End of the language of the Gemara.</p>

<p>And behold, I have transcribed before you this entire teaching, and in it you will see and understand very well all our words mentioned above. For our Sages of blessed memory arouse and urge us to walk in the path mentioned above that we have explained &mdash; that a person should not be pushed away, G&ndash;d forbid, on account of the troubles, hardships, and sufferings that pass over him and his household, whether sufferings of the body or hardships of livelihood, G&ndash;d forbid. Rather, he should look at all times at the expanses that Hashem, may He be blessed, grants him at all times, even within the trouble itself. And all the sufferings, G&ndash;d forbid, come through great kindness, a little at a time, so that one can bear them, and through this one will merit the World to Come &mdash; if he is not a fool, etc., to deceive himself into saying that he cannot serve Hashem, may He be blessed, on account of the troubles and sufferings. For on the contrary, all the troubles and sufferings in body and money all come for great good &mdash; so that precisely through them one will merit the World to Come, as is explained well in these holy words of our Sages of blessed memory, who revealed to us that the Holy One, blessed be He, does not send upon Israel sufferings and obstacles that they cannot bear, to push them away entirely, G&ndash;d forbid. For all the sufferings are only like chickens pecking at the refuse-heap &mdash; for He exacts from them a little at a time, and He does not judge them like the nations of the world, G&ndash;d forbid, of whom it is said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Ruin, ruin, ruin I shall make it!&rdquo;</span> etc., as above.</p>

<p>And now you will see how these words of our Sages of blessed memory mentioned above are connected and tightly bound together in a wondrous construction, and they constitute a path and good counsel and wondrous encouragement, so that a person should always draw close to Hashem, may He be blessed, from whatever passes over him in body, money, and soul. For there are those who deceive themselves, saying that they cannot draw close to Hashem, may He be blessed, because of the abundance of sufferings and hardships and financial pressures that pass over them and their households. To this, it is explained in these words mentioned above that the sufferings come through great kindness, to draw close precisely through them to Hashem, may He be blessed, and not to become distant through them. For Hashem, may He be blessed, does not exact from Israel in a manner that destroys them entirely; rather, He exacts from them a little at a time, like the <i>pid</i> of chickens &mdash; in a manner that precisely through this they will remember and return and draw close to Hashem, may He be blessed, and merit the World to Come. And as is explained in the conclusion of their words itself: &ldquo;And this is what Rava said: What is meant by <span class="verse">&lsquo;And I will redeem them, but they have spoken lies about Me&rsquo;</span>? &lsquo;I said: I will redeem them through their money in this world so that they merit the World to Come &mdash; but they have spoken lies about Me.&rsquo;&rdquo; That is, as above &mdash; Hashem, may He be blessed, arranges for the person to have financial pressures and hardship in livelihood, and it is only for good &mdash; in order to redeem him through this from Gehinnom and the lowest depths of the grave that would have been his due according to his deeds, as he knows in his own soul. And not only this, but he will also merit through this the World to Come. For the essential intent of Hashem, may He be blessed, is only for good &mdash; so that precisely through this one will draw close to Hashem, may He be blessed. &ldquo;But they have spoken lies about Me&rdquo; &mdash; that they speak as if with lies about Hashem, may He be blessed, as if Hashem, may He be blessed, is distancing them. And they say: &ldquo;It is impossible for us to draw close to Hashem, may He be blessed, on account of financial pressures&rdquo; &mdash; when in truth it is the very opposite, etc. And similarly, it is explained there afterward: &ldquo;And this is what Rav Pappi said in the name of Rava: What is meant by <span class="verse">&lsquo;And I have chastised them, I have strengthened their arms&rsquo;</span> &mdash; that the sufferings in this world are in order that their arms be strengthened for the World to Come &mdash; <span class="verse">&lsquo;yet they think evil of Me&rsquo;</span> &mdash; that they say the opposite, as if Hashem, may He be blessed, sends them the sufferings for their harm, G&ndash;d forbid, to distance them, G&ndash;d forbid.</p>

<p>And if the person says: &ldquo;The truth is indeed so &mdash; that the sufferings and financial pressures come through kindness, and His intent, may He be blessed, is for good, so that precisely through this one should draw close to Hashem, may He be blessed, as above. But even so, it is difficult for me to draw close, for I have already gone very far astray and I am very distant from the Torah and the commandments, and how can I cleanse my path to return to Hashem, may He be blessed?&rdquo; &mdash; to this, the Gemara responds and says there, afterward: &ldquo;Another interpretation: Even if Israel perform mitzvos before Me only a little, like the <i>pid</i> of chickens that peck at the refuse-heap, I combine it into a great reckoning.&rdquo; Behold, it is explained to us &mdash; a fitting answer to all of the above &mdash; saying: even so, even if you are as you are, you can still return from the place where you have been ensnared and seize good every day and merit eternal life in the World to Come. For behold, even if Israel perform mitzvos only a little, like the <i>pid</i> of chickens that peck at the refuse-heap, He too, may He be blessed, combines them into a great reckoning, as above.</p>

<p>And set your heart well to these holy words of our Sages of blessed memory &mdash; how far they encourage each and every person: even if he is as he is, he can still seize Torah and mitzvos and merit a good portion for the World to Come. For even when they perform mitzvos only like a chicken pecking at the refuse-heap, etc. And understand the parable well, to understand from it the lesson (as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;to understand parable and metaphor&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">[Proverbs 1:6]</span>) &mdash; that they compared the matter to a chicken standing in refuse and dirt, etc., and pecking from there, a tiny bit at a time, its food &mdash; which is a fraction of a fraction of a single grain of wheat or a single legume. And even if Israel perform mitzvos before Him only like this chicken pecking at the refuse-heap, as above &mdash; even this, He, may He be blessed, in His mercy, combines into a great reckoning. And behold, the <i>Tanna</i> has informed you how far His mercies, may He be blessed, extend. And therefore you too can draw close, even though it seems to you that you are standing in refuse and dirt, etc. &mdash; even so, even from there you can peck at the refuse-heap and seize a little bit of good at a time. For even this is precious in His eyes, may He be blessed, as above. (And all of this is explained well according to the Torah <span class="verse">&ldquo;I will sing to my G&ndash;d while I yet live,&rdquo;</span> etc., where it is explained that even if the small amount of good is mixed with waste, even so, at least there is a good point in it, etc. &mdash; that is, as above.)</p>

<p>And if you still argue and say: &ldquo;The truth is indeed so &mdash; that Hashem, may He be blessed, sends the sufferings with mercy, a little at a time, and He also asks of us that we should at least seize mitzvos and good deeds, a little at a time, like a chicken pecking at the refuse-heap. But what shall I do, for I have become so distant that I cannot even accept these sufferings and financial pressures, and they are preventing me greatly&rdquo; &mdash; to this, they responded there, in their holy words, saying there, adjacent to this: &ldquo;Another interpretation: In the reward for crying out before Me, I will save them.&rdquo; That is to say: Behold, I am giving you good counsel for this as well &mdash; that you should cry out and beseech Hashem, may He be blessed, about this. And He will certainly save you and deliver you even from these sufferings and financial pressures. You see that in this teaching, all our words mentioned above are contained &mdash; that a person must believe in the mercies of Hashem, may He be blessed, that certainly the sufferings are for good, and he should endeavor to find within them many expanses. For in truth, Hashem, may He be blessed, exacts only a little at a time, and through this one can seize, at least a little bit at a time, Torah and mitzvos, like a chicken pecking at the refuse-heap. And through this, one will be able to cry out and entreat Hashem, may He be blessed, until Hashem, may He be blessed, saves him even from this, and he will merit to emerge from the troubles entirely and to draw close to Hashem, may He be blessed, in fullness. For certainly the intentions of Hashem, may He be blessed, in all that passes over a person, are all for great good &mdash; as the Gemara concluded there afterward: &ldquo;And this is what Rava said: What is meant by <span class="verse">&lsquo;And I will redeem them,&rsquo;</span>&rdquo; etc., as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- HEFKER §14 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;14</div>

<p>And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And G&ndash;d spoke to Moshe and said to him: I am Hashem&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 6:2)</span> &mdash; that Hashem, may He be blessed, rebuked him for having said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Why have You done evil to this people?&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 5:22)</span>. This was because Dasan and Aviram came out and stood to confront him and said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;May Hashem look upon you and judge!&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 5:21)</span>, etc. For in truth, if everyone had listened to the voice of the <span class="key-term">tzaddikay emes</span> [true righteous ones], to walk in this path &mdash; to always believe in Hashem, may He be blessed, that everything is for good, and to constantly give praise and thanksgiving to Hashem, may He be blessed, both in His goodness and in His severity, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;In Hashem I praise a word; in G&ndash;d I praise a word&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 56:11)</span> &mdash; certainly all the troubles and all the exiles would have been nullified entirely and there would have already been a complete redemption.</p>

<p>But the essential hindrance of the redemption, both generally and individually, is through the abundance of disputants, who are the aspect of Dasan and Aviram, who came out standing to confront Moshe, etc. For in truth, even though when one gives thanks to Hashem, may He be blessed &mdash; through which all the troubles drawn from the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> are nullified, etc., until the trouble is nullified entirely, etc. &mdash; even so, <span class="verse">&ldquo;this opposite this has G&ndash;d made&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Ecclesiastes 7:14)</span>, and as soon as some sprouting of the horn of salvation begins, immediately the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achra</span> and the accusers incite themselves more and more to prosecute and to intensify the trouble, G&ndash;d forbid &mdash; like two people fighting, where when one sees that his fellow is overpowering, he strengthens himself more, etc. (as is explained in the Torah <span class="verse">&ldquo;And Boaz said,&rdquo;</span> etc., <span class="inline-source">Siman 65</span>, and elsewhere). And from this come all the downfalls, may the Merciful One save us, and the estrangement of all people, and especially of the upright ones who began to draw close and then became distant, may the Merciful One save us.</p>

<p>And therefore, when Moshe came to redeem them, and <span class="verse">&ldquo;the people believed,&rdquo;</span> etc., <span class="verse">&ldquo;and they bowed and prostrated themselves&rdquo;</span> &mdash; through which the redemption began &mdash; the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achra</span> strengthened itself greatly and hardened Pharaoh&rsquo;s heart, until he said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Who is Hashem?&rdquo;</span> etc., and he said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Let the work be heavy&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 5:9)</span>, with extreme severity, not to give them straw. And this was a test for Israel &mdash; to strengthen themselves precisely then in faith, to believe that certainly the word of Hashem through Moshe, the trusted one of His house, would certainly stand forever &mdash; as indeed the majority of the upright ones followed this path. But there were found disputants &mdash; Dasan and Aviram &mdash; who led many astray after them, until they came out standing to confront Moshe and said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;May Hashem look upon you,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; as if they were zealous with the zeal of the L&ndash;rd of Hosts, and arguing on behalf of Israel, and handing a judgment to Heaven against Moshe Rabbeinu who gives his very soul for their sake &mdash; until they say: <span class="verse">&ldquo;May Hashem look upon you and judge!&rdquo;</span></p>

<p>And through the abundance of their <span class="key-term">machlokes</span>, the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> overpowered, concealing, G&ndash;d forbid, the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, from which comes all the redemption, as above. And their evil <span class="key-term">machlokes</span> intensified, as above, until <span class="verse">&ldquo;the oppression makes a wise man foolish and destroys the heart of a gift&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Ecclesiastes 7:7)</span> &mdash; which is the heart of Moshe, as our Sages of blessed memory said &mdash; until Moshe, from the intensity of his distress, said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Why have You done evil to this people?&rdquo;</span> etc. For Moshe argued: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Why is it that You sent me?&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 5:22)</span> &mdash; for this was his very argument from the outset, that he did not want to go on this mission, because of the abundance of disputants, etc., as above.</p>

<p>And Hashem, may He be blessed, answered him that certainly He would complete what is His, in His great mercy, and through the merit of the Forefathers, and through the merit of Aharon and the upright ones who accompany him &mdash; who truly believe in Moshe and nullify the divergence of their own opinions, which are the aspect of <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, to the one <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> of Moshe &mdash; through which they are included in the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, as above. And through all of this, the redemption would be complete.</p>

<p>And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And G&ndash;d (<i>Elokim</i>) spoke to Moshe and said to him: I am Hashem&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that is, the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Know that Hashem, He is the G&ndash;d (<i>Elokim</i>)&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 100:3)</span>, as explained at the end of the Torah mentioned above, where he interpreted that all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> that are drawn from the Name <span class="heb-word">Elokim</span>, are all included in <span class="heb-word">Hashem</span>, which is the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>; see there. And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And Elokim spoke to Moshe and said to him: I am Hashem&rdquo;</span> &mdash; for it is all one, for Hashem, He is the Elokim, for all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> are included in the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, and He will certainly complete what is His, to redeem them. For Pharaoh said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Who is Hashem?&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 5:2)</span> &mdash; for he did not believe in the Name <span class="heb-word">Hashem</span>, for his sustenance was only from the Name <span class="heb-word">Elokim</span>, as is brought. For he wanted to separate, G&ndash;d forbid, between the Name <span class="heb-word">Hashem</span> and the Name <span class="heb-word">Elokim</span> &mdash; which is the essence of separation, G&ndash;d forbid. That is, he wanted to deny and to separate the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> from the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, because it is impossible to grasp this through the intellect, as is explained there. But Hashem, may He be blessed, struck him with great blows and delivered Israel from them all, and demonstrated great and awesome wonders, through all of which he saw with his own eyes that all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> are from the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> &mdash; until he was compelled to acknowledge it himself and said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Hashem is the righteous One&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 9:27)</span>.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- HEFKER §15 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;15</div>

<p>And so it continues now &mdash; that whenever some sprouting of the horn of salvation is aroused, whether generally or individually, immediately the opposing side intensifies more and more, like two people fighting, etc., as above. And if one wants to strengthen himself more, they intensify even more and more, etc. &mdash; until the heart becomes very bent, as if it were impossible now, G&ndash;d forbid, to return and draw close to Hashem, may He be blessed.</p>

<p>But in the end of all ends, Hashem, may He be blessed, will complete what is His, and will redeem us with a complete redemption &mdash; through the merit of the Forefathers, and through the power of the <span class="key-term">tzaddikay emes</span> and the upright ones who accompany them, who believe in the truth and walk in the path mentioned above: to believe that everything is for good, and to constantly give praise and thanksgiving to Hashem, may He be blessed, with joy, and to strengthen themselves through this to pray and beseech Hashem, may He be blessed, as above. And through this, Hashem, may He be blessed, will save us and deliver us and bring us out from all the troubles and pressures, and will hasten to redeem us with a complete redemption, after which there will be no exile &mdash; speedily in our days, <i>Amain</i>, may it be His will.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- HEFKER §16 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;16</div>

<p>And therefore there is an obligation upon us to remember the Exodus from Egypt every day, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;In order that you remember the day you left the land of Egypt, all the days of your life&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Deuteronomy 16:3)</span>. And similarly, at the beginning of the Giving of the Torah, He began: <span class="verse">&ldquo;I am Hashem your G&ndash;d who took you out of the land of Egypt&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 20:2)</span>. And similarly, in most of the commandments, He mentioned the Exodus from Egypt. For now, all our beginning to enter the service of Hashem, each and every day, is through the Exodus from Egypt. For now, praise be to G&ndash;d, we have a good beginning &mdash; a place from where to begin &mdash; since Hashem, may He be blessed, has already completed His salvation through Moshe and brought us out of Egypt with awesome signs. For this we give praise and thanksgiving to Him, may He be blessed, every day, evening and morning &mdash; which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah/halachah</span>, through which truth illuminates, etc., until the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, through which the power of the exile of the nations is nullified, etc., as above, until we merit through this a complete redemption, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore we are obligated to remember the Exodus from Egypt every day, evening and morning, and whoever tells more of the Exodus from Egypt is praiseworthy &mdash; for all our beginning now to look forward to salvation still and to draw close to Hashem, may He be blessed, is through the Exodus from Egypt, as above. And from this we learn to understand also in particular the miracles and wonders that Hashem, may He be blessed, does with us in every generation &mdash; until even in the most particular details, Hashem, may He be blessed, does many miracles with each and every person, each and every day. For this we thank Him, may He be blessed, every day &mdash; which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah</span>, etc., etc., through which each person can draw close to Hashem, may He be blessed, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore we say every day, before the prayer of <i>Shemoneh Esrai</i>: <span class="verse">&ldquo;True and firm&rdquo;</span> (<i>Emes v&rsquo;Yatziv</i>) in the morning, and <span class="verse">&ldquo;True and faithful&rdquo;</span> (<i>Emes v&rsquo;Emunah</i>) in the evening &mdash; where we tell and give thanks to Him, may He be blessed, for the miracles of the Exodus from Egypt and for the miracles and wonders of every generation, as we say: <span class="verse">&ldquo;You are the help of our fathers,&rdquo;</span> etc., <span class="verse">&ldquo;a shield and savior for them and for their children after them in every generation.&rdquo;</span> For it is precisely through giving thanks to Him, may He be blessed, for all the miracles, etc., as above, that precisely through this we are able to enter into prayer &mdash; to pray and to beseech before Him, may He be blessed, as above. And therefore on Shabbos we add <i>Nishmas</i>, which is a wondrous praise and thanksgiving &mdash; for the essential inclusion of all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is through the holiness of the holy Shabbos, which one merits through <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span>, as above. Therefore we say then the wondrous praise and thanksgiving, which is <span class="verse">&ldquo;The soul of all living shall bless,&rdquo;</span> etc.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- HEFKER §17 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;17</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of the entire Book of Tehillim, which was composed by Dovid HaMelech, peace be upon him, who is the aspect of Mashiach, through whom the complete redemption will come. It consists of five books corresponding to the Five Books of Torah. For the essential fulfillment of the Torah is through the aspect of Tehillim, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah/hoda&rsquo;ah</span> &mdash; through which one draws close to Hashem, may He be blessed, and fulfills the Torah, as above. And therefore Moshe concluded with: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Fortunate are you, Israel&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Deuteronomy 33:29)</span>, and with this Dovid opened: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Fortunate is the man&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 1:1)</span>, as is brought in <i>Midrash Rabbah</i> on Parshas <i>Vayechi</i> and Parshas <i>V&rsquo;Zos HaBerachah</i>. For Moshe toiled greatly until he found the beginning &mdash; for he was the first redeemer, and it was very difficult to find this path of <span class="key-term">todah</span> and <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span>, because no redemption had yet preceded him, and from the time that the children of Israel began to be a nation, they immediately went down into the Egyptian exile. Therefore the mission was indeed very difficult in his eyes. But now that He has already taken us out of Egypt and given us the Torah and wondrously bestowed His kindness upon us so greatly, praise be to G&ndash;d, we have what to give thanks for &mdash; through which we can draw close to Hashem, may He be blessed, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore Moshe concluded with <span class="verse">&ldquo;Fortunate are you, Israel; who is like you, a people saved by Hashem!&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; to instruct them that they must always praise and give thanks to Hashem, may He be blessed, for the pleasantness of their lot, and to say every day with joy: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Fortunate are we! How good is our portion, how pleasant is our lot!&rdquo;</span> etc. And with that which Moshe concluded, Dovid opened the Book of Tehillim: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Fortunate is the man,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; and he composed all the chapters of Tehillim upon this &mdash; to instill in us this path, to always begin from the aspect of Tehillim, to give thanks and praise to Hashem, may He be blessed, for all the kindnesses, etc., as above &mdash; through which comes the essential drawing close to Hashem, may He be blessed, through which the redemption will come, as above.</p>

<p>And this is what our Master, our Teacher, and our Rebbe, of blessed memory, wrote &mdash; that Tehillim is conducive to <span class="key-term">teshuvah</span>. That is, to draw close to Hashem, may He be blessed, and to His holy Torah &mdash; as above &mdash; that the essential drawing close is through <span class="key-term">todah</span>, which is the aspect of Tehillim, as above. And therefore Moshe concluded with <span class="heb-word">Ashray</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah</span> &mdash; giving thanks for our portion and saying, &ldquo;Fortunate are we,&rdquo; etc. For Moshe was unable to begin with this, because he was the first redeemer and no redemption had preceded him, as above. But after he had already redeemed Israel and toiled all his days until he instilled the Torah in Israel, then he concluded with <span class="heb-word">Ashray</span> &mdash; to instruct them to walk in this path, to give thanks for their portion, etc., as above. And therefore Dovid, who came after Moshe, said: &ldquo;I will begin with this &mdash; with that which Moshe concluded&rdquo; &mdash; for now that we have already merited the Exodus from Egypt and the Giving of the Torah through Moshe, now all our beginning is through the aspect of <span class="heb-word">Ashray</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah</span>, as above.</p>

<p>And this is what our Sages of blessed memory said &mdash; that Dovid said <span class="heb-word">Ashray</span> twenty-two times in Tehillim, corresponding to those who fulfill the Torah, which is written in twenty-two letters. That is, as above &mdash; the essential fulfillment of the Torah is through <span class="heb-word">Ashray</span>, as above, and each person must say <span class="heb-word">Ashray</span> many times each day, to place joy in his heart over his portion, that he merited to be among the community of Israel, etc., as above. For the main thing is the joy of Torah and mitzvos, as is brought at length in the writings of the Ari z&rdquo;l, and especially in the words of our Master, our Teacher, and our Rebbe, of blessed memory. And so our predecessors established for us to say <span class="heb-word">Ashray</span> three times every day, and we also say every day in the morning: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Fortunate are we! How good is our portion!&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;Fortunate are we!&rdquo;</span> etc. And similarly, we say after the prayer: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Blessed is our G&ndash;d, Who created us for His glory and separated us from those who go astray,&rdquo;</span> etc. And similarly, much more. And each person must set his heart to this &mdash; to gladden himself with every single good point that he has from the holiness of Israel, etc., for this is our life &mdash; for through this comes the drawing close to Hashem, may He be blessed, as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- HEFKER §18 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;18</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of what is brought in <i>Midrash Rabbah</i>, Shemos, Chapter 23: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Then Moshe sang&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 15:1)</span> &mdash; this is what is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Your throne is established from then (<i>mai&rsquo;az</i>)&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 93:2)</span>. Said Rabbi Berechiah in the name of Rabbi Abahu: &ldquo;Even though You exist from eternity, Your throne was not settled and You were not known in Your world until Your children sang the <i>shirah</i>,&rdquo; etc. &ldquo;A parable of a king who fought a war and was victorious,&rdquo; etc. &mdash; &ldquo;Rather, He was, as it were, standing, as it says: <span class="verse">&lsquo;He stood and measured the earth&rsquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Habakkuk 3:6)</span>. But when You stood at the sea and we sang <i>shirah</i> before You &mdash; from then (<i>mai&rsquo;az</i>) Your sovereignty was settled and Your throne [established]&rdquo; &mdash; this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Your throne is established from then (<i>mai&rsquo;az</i>)&rdquo;</span> &mdash; through <span class="verse">&ldquo;Then (<i>az</i>) Moshe sang.&rdquo;</span> End of the Midrash&rsquo;s language.</p>

<p>And the general intent of the Midrash is that before Israel sang the <i>shirah</i>, Hashem, may He be blessed, was in the aspect of &ldquo;standing,&rdquo; and His throne was not yet established for Him to sit upon &mdash; that is, His sovereignty was not yet settled and He was not yet known in His world. But after they sang the <i>shirah</i>, then they established His throne, as it were, and then they seated Him, may He be blessed, as it were, upon His throne &mdash; for then His sovereignty was settled and He was known in His world. And then His sovereignty, as it were, became exceedingly great, in the aspect of <i>Augustus</i>. But at first He was only in the aspect of a king, as it says there: &ldquo;A parable of a king who won a war and they made him <i>Augustus</i>,&rdquo; etc.; see there.</p>

<p>That is, according to the Torah mentioned above &mdash; the essential drawing close to Hashem, may He be blessed, is through <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span> and songs and praises, through which truth illuminates within the fourfold speech, until one merits to reveal the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> &mdash; which means that many, who have divergent opinions (which is the essential aspect of <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>), agree to one true <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span>, etc. &mdash; through which all the troubles and all the exiles are nullified, etc., as above. And therefore, the essential knowledge of His G&ndash;dliness in the world in fullness, which is the aspect of the settling of His throne, as it were, as above &mdash; is specifically through <i>shirah</i>. For <i>shirah</i> is the essential fullness of <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span> &mdash; when the thanksgivings are said with a whole heart in song and joy. This is what Israel merited at the splitting of the Sea of Reeds &mdash; after their salvation had already begun in that they had left Egypt, and they had already said <span class="key-term">Hallel</span> and <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span> on Pesach &mdash; until they merited to topple Egypt entirely. For the abundance of divergences of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> were nullified, and the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> was revealed, and they believed in Hashem and in Moshe His servant. And the more the exile and the troubles of the Egyptians were nullified &mdash; until all the nations were nullified, for dread and fear fell upon them, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The peoples heard and trembled,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 15:14)</span> &mdash; through this, the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> was revealed even more from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, and through this the <span class="key-term">todah</span> and <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span> grew greater and greater until they sang the <i>shirah</i> with a whole heart, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Then Moshe sang.&rdquo;</span> And then, precisely, His sovereignty, may He be blessed, was settled, in the aspect of sitting upon a throne &mdash; because then the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> was revealed even more &mdash; which is the essential glory of His sovereignty, as is explained there.</p>

<p>For the essential building of His throne, as it were, is from the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> when they are gathered together into one <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> and included in the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> &mdash; from this His throne is built, as it were, which is comprised of many colors. For the main thing is that many, who have divergent opinions, are all included in one true <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span>, as above &mdash; as it was then at the time of the splitting of the Sea of Reeds, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And they believed in Hashem and in Moshe His servant&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 14:31)</span> &mdash; that they all agreed to one <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> and were included in Hashem and in Moshe with complete faith. And all the souls of Israel are hewn from the Throne of Glory, and when they are included together in one <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> in the holy faith &mdash; through this, the Throne of His Glory, may He be blessed, is built and enlarged, for its entire structure comes from the souls of Israel who are hewn from there. And then His sovereignty was settled, like a king sitting upon his throne &mdash; in the aspect of sitting and not standing &mdash; for He was well known in His world and was settled in the mind and heart of each and every person, in the aspect of sitting upon a throne, as above.</p>

<p>And all of this they merited through <i>shirah</i>, which is the fullness of <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span> with a whole heart, as above. For all the songs are comprised of the ten types of melody through which the Book of Tehillim is composed, which are the aspect of simple, double, triple, quadruple song &mdash; as is explained elsewhere &mdash; and this is the aspect of the fullness of the fourfold speech, which is hinted at in the verse: <span class="verse">&ldquo;I am not a man of words &mdash; not from yesterday, nor from the day before, nor from then (<i>mai&rsquo;az</i>)&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 4:10)</span> (see there well in the Torah mentioned above). &ldquo;A man of words&rdquo; &mdash; this is the aspect of simple song. &ldquo;Also from yesterday&rdquo; &mdash; that is, today and yesterday &mdash; this is the aspect of double. &ldquo;Also from the day before&rdquo; &mdash; this is the aspect of triple. &ldquo;Also from then (<i>mai&rsquo;az</i>) that You speak&rdquo; &mdash; this is the aspect of quadruple. For Hashem, may He be blessed, debated with Moshe for seven days, as our Sages of blessed memory said and as Rashi explains &mdash; for the three instances of <span class="heb-word">gam</span> [&ldquo;also&rdquo;] are amplifications. And these seven days correspond to the three lines of truth that illuminate within the fourfold speech, so that through these seven days the three lines of truth would illuminate within the fourfold speech &mdash; through which the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> would be revealed, etc., which is the essential completion of the repair of the redemption. But Moshe said on the seventh day: <span class="verse">&ldquo;I am not a man of words &mdash; not from yesterday, nor from the day before, nor from then,&rdquo;</span> etc. And even though Hashem, may He be blessed, said to him: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Who gave man a mouth?&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 4:11)</span>, he replied: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Send, please, by the hand of whom You will send&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 4:13)</span> &mdash; &ldquo;for I know that I am not their final redeemer,&rdquo; etc., as our Sages of blessed memory said. That is, he said that he had not yet merited the completion of the repair of the fullness of the speech, which is the aspect of <span class="heb-word">malchus peh</span> [&ldquo;sovereignty of the mouth&rdquo;], hinted at in the verse &ldquo;also from <i>then</i> (<i>mai&rsquo;az</i>),&rdquo; which is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Your throne is established from then (<i>mai&rsquo;az</i>),&rdquo;</span> as is brought there regarding this verse for this matter. For this completion of the repair of the fourfold speech will only be through Mashiach, who will merit the holy <i>malchus</i>. But Hashem, may He be blessed, decreed upon Moshe that even so, he was compelled to go &mdash; for it was necessary to begin the first redemption, so that they would merit <span class="key-term">todah/hoda&rsquo;ah</span>, in order to reveal the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, etc., until in the end of all ends, the completion of the final redemption would come through this &mdash; in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;As in the days of your going out from Egypt, I will show him wonders&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Micah 7:15)</span>, as explained above.</p>

<p>And then, when Moshe completed the first redemption and the Egyptians fell and died at the shore of the sea, and <span class="verse">&ldquo;they believed in Hashem,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; then Moshe saw that the word of our G&ndash;d will stand forever. And therefore <span class="verse">&ldquo;Then Moshe sang&rdquo;</span> (<i>yashir</i>, with a <i>yud</i>) &mdash; for the <i>yud</i> alludes to the future, and as our Sages of blessed memory said: &ldquo;From here we see that in the future Moshe will sing.&rdquo; That is, he drew the <i>shirah</i> from the future song &mdash; which is the aspect of simple, double, triple, quadruple song, which is the aspect of the fourfold speech. For in the future, all of this will be in ultimate fullness, and now he drew the <i>shirah</i> from there. And through this, the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> was revealed even more &mdash; which is revealed through the fourfold speech, for the <i>shirah</i>, which is simple, double, triple, quadruple song, is drawn from there, as above. And therefore then His throne was established and His sovereignty was settled, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Your throne is established from then,&rdquo;</span> as above.</p>

<p>And therefore the <i>shirah</i> concluded: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The peoples heard and trembled; terror gripped the inhabitants of Philistia,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;Dread and fear shall fall upon them; by the greatness of Your arm they shall be still as a stone,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;You shall bring them and plant them on the mountain of Your inheritance, the foundation for Your dwelling that You have made, Hashem; the Sanctuary,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 15:14&ndash;17)</span>. For the essential repair is in the aspect of the Bais HaMikdash, which is the aspect of the Throne of Glory, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;A glorious throne, exalted from the beginning, the place of our Sanctuary&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Jeremiah 17:12)</span> &mdash; for there are all the blessings and thanksgivings and all the songs and praises that the Levites sang on the platform. And there are all the <span class="key-term">halachos</span>, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;If a matter be too wondrous for you&hellip; you shall rise and go up&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Deuteronomy 17:8)</span>, etc. And there all the souls of Israel gather together and are included in the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;For there the tribes went up&hellip; to give thanks to the Name of Hashem&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 122:4)</span>, etc.</p>

<p>And all of this they merited through the power of the miracles of the Exodus from Egypt and the splitting of the Sea of Reeds, through which all the Egyptians and all the seventy nations were nullified &mdash; for they were all terrified and frightened: the mighty ones of Moav, the chiefs of Edom, and all the inhabitants of Canaan, who are the essential blemish of the divergences of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>. Through the power of the miracles, they were all compelled to acknowledge the truth &mdash; that all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> are drawn from the <span class="key-term">Echad Ha&rsquo;pashut</span>. And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;By the greatness of Your arm they shall be still as a stone&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that they fell silent and were nullified, in the aspect of the nullification of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>. And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;They shall be still as a stone (<i>even</i>)&rdquo;</span> &mdash; <i>even</i> [stone] is the aspect of <i>av</i> [father] and <i>ben</i> [son] as one &mdash; that is, the aspect of the totality of the souls of Israel, who are in the aspect of children of the Omnipresent, who are included in their Father in Heaven in His <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>. And then, from the great power of the awesome miracles and wonders, then also all the peoples &mdash; dread and fear fell upon them until they fell silent and were nullified like a stone; like Israel, who were included in His unity in the aspect of father and son as one &mdash; so too the abundance of their divergences was nullified, and they were compelled to acknowledge the truth. And this is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;they shall be still as a stone,&rdquo;</span> as above.</p>

<p>And therefore, adjacent to this: <span class="verse">&ldquo;You shall bring them and plant them on the mountain of Your inheritance,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; that is, the building of the Bais HaMikdash, where the essential revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> etc., takes place &mdash; which is the aspect of sitting upon the Throne of His Glory, for the Bais HaMikdash is the aspect of the Throne of Glory, etc., as above. And it is <span class="verse">&ldquo;the foundation for Your dwelling&rdquo;</span> &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;Your dwelling&rdquo;</span> precisely, the aspect of sitting upon a throne, etc., as above. And similarly Shlomo said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;A foundation for Your dwelling forever&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(I Kings 8:13)</span>, as above. And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Hashem shall reign forever and ever&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 15:18)</span> &mdash; for through this is the essential revelation of His sovereignty forever and ever &mdash; that His sovereignty is settled upon a throne, as it were, and He is known in His world, as above. And therefore we repeat the verse <span class="verse">&ldquo;Hashem shall reign forever and ever&rdquo;</span> when we say the Song at the Sea every day &mdash; that is, the aspect of king and <i>Augustus</i> mentioned above, which is the essential aspect of His sitting upon His throne, when His sovereignty is enlarged more and more, in the aspect of <i>Augustus</i>, as explained there in the Midrash mentioned above; see there well.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- HEFKER §19 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;19</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of how we begin on Rosh Hashanah: &ldquo;The King sits upon a throne, lofty and exalted&rdquo; &mdash; for then is the essential settling of His sovereignty upon the throne, as it were. For on Rosh Hashanah the world was created, and He, may He be blessed, created it with very many diverse activities. And this is our entire service on Rosh Hashanah &mdash; to reveal to all who enter the world that Hashem, may He be blessed, created the world, and that all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> are drawn from His <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, may He be blessed. And therefore we engage on Rosh Hashanah in an abundance of thanksgivings and songs and praises, as our predecessors established for us in the many <i>piyutim</i>, all of which are wondrous thanksgivings and songs &mdash; such as <span class="verse">&ldquo;You are our G&ndash;d in the heavens and on the earth,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;Supreme King,&rdquo;</span> etc., etc. For through thanksgivings, the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, as above &mdash; through which comes the essential repair of the aspect of the Throne of Glory to sit upon, as it were, as above. And therefore we begin then: &ldquo;The King <i>sits</i> upon a throne&rdquo; &mdash; and we say it without the Name of Hashem, precisely &mdash; to show that then is the essential beginning of His sitting upon the throne, etc. For throughout the rest of the year we say &ldquo;the King <i>Who sits</i>&rdquo; &mdash; that He sat already, namely from Rosh Hashanah, when Israel, as it were, seated Him upon His throne. And therefore on Rosh Hashanah we say &ldquo;the King <i>sits</i>&rdquo; &mdash; for now, on Rosh Hashanah, when Israel reveal that He created the world today and drew all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> from His <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, as above &mdash; therefore now He sits upon the throne, etc., as above.</p>

<p>And therefore the blessings of <i>Malchiyos</i>, <i>Zichronos</i>, and <i>Shofros</i> that are added on Rosh Hashanah begin with the praise <i>Alainu</i>. For this is the essence of Rosh Hashanah &mdash; to give thanks, to praise, to laud the Master of all, etc. &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;Who has not made us like the nations of the lands,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; which is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Fortunate are we&rdquo;</span> mentioned above, through which is the essential revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, etc., as above &mdash; which is the essential holiness of Rosh Hashanah, as above. And therefore, with this praise of <i>Alainu</i>, they conquered Jericho and entered the Land of Israel, as our Sages of blessed memory said &mdash; for the essential purpose of their entering the Land of Israel was to build the Bais HaMikdash, where the essential revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> etc. takes place, which is merited through <span class="key-term">todah/hoda&rsquo;ah</span> &mdash; through which we give thanks and praise to Him, may He be blessed, for the pleasantness of our lot, etc. &mdash; which is the aspect of the wondrous praise of <span class="verse">&ldquo;<i>Alainu</i> to praise,&rdquo;</span> etc., as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- HEFKER §20 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;20</div>

<p>And therefore we say <i>Alainu</i> every day after the prayer. For the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah/hoda&rsquo;ah</span> mentioned above, which is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Fortunate are we&rdquo;</span> and <i>Alainu</i>, etc. &mdash; that we say three times every day &mdash; from this is the beginning and this is the end and the goal. And as was explained above, the end is embedded in the beginning and the beginning is embedded in the end &mdash; for the more we praise and give thanks to Him, may He be blessed, for having chosen us from all the nations, etc. &mdash; the more the speech is completed and His <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed, etc. And the more it is revealed, the more the <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span> grows &mdash; for through the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, the exiles and troubles are nullified more, etc. &mdash; and so it cycles around for the good, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore we say <span class="verse">&ldquo;Fortunate are we,&rdquo;</span> etc. and many songs and praises and thanksgivings before the prayer, and similarly afterward we say: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Blessed is our G&ndash;d, Who created us for His glory and separated us from those who go astray,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; until we conclude with <i>Alainu</i> to praise, which is a wondrous and awesome praise for having merited the holiness of Israel. For the end is embedded in the beginning, etc., as above. For <span class="key-term">todah</span> and <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span> is our entire service in this world, and it is our ultimate purpose for the World to Come &mdash; for this is the essential delight of the World to Come, as is explained at the beginning of the sefer mentioned above. And therefore, adjacent to <i>Alainu</i>, we say: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Whoever studies <i>halachos</i> every day is assured that he is a person of the World to Come&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Megillah 28b)</span> &mdash; and afterward we say <i>Alainu</i> to praise, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah</span> mentioned above. For <span class="key-term">todah</span> and <span class="key-term">halachos</span> are one aspect &mdash; the aspect of the delight of the World to Come, as above. And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And You are holy, enthroned (<i>yoshaiv</i>) upon the praises of Israel&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 22:4)</span> &mdash; that through the praises of Israel, the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah/hoda&rsquo;ah</span> &mdash; through this, He, may He be blessed, is in the aspect of <i>yoshaiv</i> [sitting, enthroned], as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- HEFKER §21 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;21</div>

<p>And this is what we say before the <i>shofar</i>: the <i>mizmor</i> <span class="verse">&ldquo;All the peoples, clap hands,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;For Hashem, the Most High, is awesome &mdash; a great King,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 47:2&ndash;3)</span>. &ldquo;A great King&rdquo; precisely &mdash; the aspect of <i>Augustus</i> mentioned above. And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;He leads peoples beneath us, and nations under our feet&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 47:4)</span> &mdash; that all the peoples and nations, who are the essential <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, will all be subdued and nullified to us, we who are included in Him, may He be blessed. This is the aspect of the inclusion of all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, which are very, very distant, within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> &mdash; which is the essential awesome greatness of His sovereignty and glory, may He be blessed, in the aspect of &ldquo;a great King,&rdquo; etc., as above.</p>

<p>And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;He shall choose our inheritance for us&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 47:5)</span> &mdash; that is, the Bais HaMikdash, where this essential revelation takes place, as above. And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;G&ndash;d has ascended with a blast&rdquo;</span> etc., <span class="verse">&ldquo;sing to G&ndash;d, sing,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 47:6&ndash;7)</span> &mdash; that is, the aspect of all the ten types of melody that are drawn through the <i>shofar</i>, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;play well with a blast&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 33:3)</span>, as is explained elsewhere, etc. And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;G&ndash;d reigns over the nations; G&ndash;d sits upon His holy throne&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 47:9)</span> &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;sits&rdquo;</span> precisely, as above. And similarly, it concludes afterward: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The nobles of the peoples have gathered&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 47:10)</span> &mdash; who are the converts, as our Sages of blessed memory said &mdash; that all of this is the aspect of the inclusion of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, as above &mdash; through which <span class="verse">&ldquo;G&ndash;d sits upon His holy throne,&rdquo;</span> in the aspect of sitting upon a throne, as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- HEFKER §22 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;22</div>

<p>And this is what we say on Shabbos: &ldquo;On the seventh day He was elevated and sat upon the Throne of His Glory&rdquo; &mdash; for the essential revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, etc., is on Shabbos, as above &mdash; which is the aspect of His sitting upon a throne, as it were, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of: &ldquo;The Holy One, blessed be He, the One above, does not sit upon the Throne of His Glory until she is made into the mystery of one,&rdquo; etc. &mdash; and this entire holy passage that we say at the onset of Shabbos; see there well and you will understand wondrous allusions according to all that was explained above. For when the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> below, through this His unity, may He be blessed, is revealed above, etc., as above. And the revelation of His <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> below &mdash; this is the aspect of &ldquo;she is made into the mystery of one&rdquo; &mdash; that the aspect of the <i>Shechinah</i>, meaning the indwelling of His G&ndash;dliness among those below, is unified in the ultimate unity through the repairs mentioned above, through which the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> specifically in this world. And through this, the aspect of the Throne of His Glory is repaired for Him to sit upon, as above. For through this, His <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed above &mdash; and then, precisely, His sovereignty is settled and He is known in His world &mdash; which is the aspect of the repair of His throne, as above. And therefore &ldquo;the Holy One, blessed be He, does not sit upon the Throne of His Glory above until she is made into the mystery of one&rdquo; &mdash; that is, that all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> are included in the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, etc., as above. And the entire passage speaks of this. For this is the mystery of Shabbos, etc. &mdash; &ldquo;for the precious, holy throne is unified in the mystery of one and is prepared for the holy King to rest upon it,&rdquo; etc. See there well and understand.</p>


<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- NACHALOS SUBDIVISION -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<h2 class="sub-header">Nachalos <span class="sub-header-en">[Laws of Inheritance]</span></h2>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- NACHALOS §23 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;23</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of the order of inheritance &mdash; that the essential inheritance belongs to the son. And if he has no son: <span class="verse">&ldquo;You shall transfer his inheritance to his daughter&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Numbers 27:8)</span>, and if he has no daughter, etc. And it has already been explained above (in &sect;4) that the commandment of inheritance to children is because the begetting of children is one and the same aspect as the birthing of <span class="key-term">halachos</span>, which is drawn through the supporters of Torah who sustain with their money the <span class="key-term">tzaddikay emes</span>, who birth <span class="key-term">halachos</span> through this; see there well.</p>

<p>And therefore the son precedes the daughter &mdash; for the daughter, relative to the son, is in the aspect of <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>. For the further a created being is from Him, may He be blessed, the more it is in the aspect of a diverse activity &mdash; as was explained above regarding converts; see there. For the souls of the children of Israel are all in the aspect of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, as above &mdash; for they are a portion of G&ndash;d from above and are included in Him, may He be blessed. And therefore all the seventy souls of the House of Yaakov are all called &ldquo;one soul,&rdquo; as above. But the woman, relative to the man, is in the aspect of <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> &mdash; for she was taken from him, and her creation involves great divergence from the man. For man and woman are very extreme divergences, and even so, at their root they are in the ultimate unity, as is brought in the writings of the Ari z&rdquo;l, and is brought in the words of our Master, our Teacher, and our Rebbe, of blessed memory &mdash; that at the roots of the souls, the soul of the man and his partner emerge together, for at their root they are one soul; only below they are divided.</p>

<p>And therefore, through the union of man and woman in holiness according to the Torah &mdash; through this is the essential inclusion of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>. But because all the overpowering of the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achra</span> is in the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, where they have their hold, and they incite to separate, G&ndash;d forbid, the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> &mdash; for the essential power of the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achra</span> is in the aspect of denials, for the <i>Samech Mem</i> is called &ldquo;another god &mdash; denials,&rdquo; etc., as is brought elsewhere &mdash; therefore they lie in ambush there greatly regarding the union mentioned above. And therefore there is the essential battle of the person, as is known.</p>

<p>And the essential repair is through begetting children according to the Torah &mdash; for through all the children that are begotten, the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> is revealed even more. For the children that are begotten are themselves in the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah/halachah</span>, as above, through which comes all the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, etc., as above. For the more the children of Israel multiply, and they all agree to one <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> and believe in His unity, may He be blessed &mdash; through this, His glory, may He be blessed, is enlarged even more. For the essential glory of Him, may He be blessed, is when His <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from within many diverse activities, and the more the diverse activities multiply, and yet they are all included together in His unity &mdash; through this, His glory, may He be blessed, is revealed more and more. For this is exceedingly precious in His eyes, may He be blessed, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the greatness of the mitzvah to beget children &mdash; so that Israel should multiply from generation to generation, and they should all agree to one <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span>, to believe in His <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, may He be blessed. For the essential divergence of activities is the divergence of opinions &mdash; for even though the world is full of innumerable divergences, as above, even so, the main thing is the wondrous extent of the divergences among human beings, that no one resembles his fellow in his face or in his movements. And the main thing is the divergence of opinions among human beings &mdash; in which one sees even more the wonders of the Creator, may He be blessed. For this is the rule: the Holy One, blessed be He, never does the same thing twice. And therefore no creature resembles its fellow, and no person resembles his fellow in his appearance, and especially not in his opinions. And similarly, no generation resembles its fellow. And even a father and son &mdash; their opinions are not equal, and there are many divergences between them, as is visible to the senses. For even though in some matters they are alike, even so, there are many divergences between them in their opinions. And from the day of the creation of the world until the end, there have never been two people entirely alike &mdash; not in one generation and not across two generations. It turns out that every new birth is in the aspect of a diverse activity.</p>

<p>And when all these births across all the generations agree to one <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> and say <span class="verse">&ldquo;Hear, O Israel, Hashem,&rdquo;</span> etc. and believe in the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> &mdash; this is the essential revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from within very many <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, which is exceedingly precious in His eyes, may He be blessed. And therefore it is a great mitzvah to beget children, so that the children of Israel should multiply even more, and they are all included in His unity, may He be blessed &mdash; through which His glory, may He be blessed, is enlarged even more, through many <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> that diverge with many diverse divergences from generation to generation, as above, and yet they are all included in His unity, may He be blessed &mdash; which is exceedingly precious in His eyes, may He be blessed, as above.</p>

<p>And now it is well explained what was written at the beginning of the Torah &mdash; that he connected the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah/halachah</span> with <span class="key-term">holadah</span> [birth], for it is all one aspect, as above. For through <span class="key-term">todah/halachah</span>, the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, which is itself the aspect of the begetting of children, as above. And therefore the son precedes the daughter &mdash; for the essential inclusion of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> within the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is through the son, the male, who is closer to the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, as above. And through him the woman ascends with him and is included there, in the aspect of &ldquo;a woman ascends with him&rdquo; &mdash; which is the essential purpose of the union in holiness, for the sake of begetting Israel, the main thing being in order that the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> be revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, as above. But everything is through the man, as above, and therefore he precedes in inheritance, as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- NACHALOS §24 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;24</div>

<p>And if he has no daughter, the inheritance returns upward to his father&rsquo;s house. This is the aspect of the return of the bloods that rise upward at a time of distress, G&ndash;d forbid. And when one merits to emerge from the distress &mdash; which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah/halachah</span>, the aspect of <span class="key-term">holadah</span> &mdash; then the bloods, which are the aspect of money, return and flow in their proper order within the legs, etc., as is explained there. But when one does not merit <span class="key-term">holadah</span>, G&ndash;d forbid &mdash; this is the aspect of one whose soul is still in the aspect of distress, may the Merciful One save us, when the bloods rise upward.</p>

<p>And therefore, in truth, our Sages of blessed memory said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Whoever does not leave a son to inherit him &mdash; the Holy One, blessed be He, is filled with wrath (<i>evrah</i>) toward him,&rdquo;</span> in the aspect of &ldquo;like a pregnant woman (<i>ubarah</i>)&rdquo; <span class="inline-source">(Bava Basra 116a)</span>. For when he does not beget a son to inherit him, the bloods remain above &mdash; which is the aspect of pregnancy without birth, G&ndash;d forbid, from which come all the troubles, may the Merciful One save us.</p>

<p>And therefore his father&rsquo;s household receives the inheritance and the money of the estate &mdash; for they need to repair him, by receiving the money, whose repair is through the aspect of <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraysa</span>, etc., as above. And therefore the father precedes all those who descend from him &mdash; for first one must return to the father, who is the root of the inheritance and the bloods, etc.</p>

<p>And therefore the daughters of Tzelafchad argued: <span class="verse">&ldquo;If we are not considered seed, let our mother undergo <i>yibum</i>&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Bava Basra 119b)</span> &mdash; for this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">yibum</span> and <span class="key-term">chalitzah</span>. And this is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">yibum</span> of Yehudah, for the blemish of Er and Onan who corrupted their way, etc. For the essential repair is through begetting children, to bring the souls into bodies specifically &mdash; for the son of Dovid does not come until all the souls in the <i>Guf</i> [storehouse of souls] are used up, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And a redeemer shall come to Tzion, and to those who return from transgression in Yaakov, says Hashem; and as for Me, this is My covenant with them&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Isaiah 59:20&ndash;21)</span>, etc. &mdash; the initial letters of which spell <span class="heb-word">guf</span> [body], as is brought in the Kavanos; see there.</p>

<p>For specifically when the souls, which are a portion of G&ndash;d from above, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> &mdash; when they are drawn into physical bodies, which are the aspect of very diverse activities (for in one body alone there are many limbs, faculties, senses, four elements, and innumerable divergences, and all the more so between one body and another) &mdash; when all these bodies nullify themselves to the soul and all say with one heart: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Hear, O Israel, Hashem our G&ndash;d, Hashem is One&rdquo;</span> &mdash; and are included in His <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, may He be blessed &mdash; this is the essential revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, which is exceedingly precious in His eyes, may He be blessed.</p>

<p>And therefore, when the soul (<i>nefesh</i>, <i>ruach</i>, etc.) comes to this world and does not clothe itself in a body, G&ndash;d forbid &mdash; it is a very great and immense blemish, may the Merciful One save us. For as soon as the soul comes to this world, which is abundant in husks as is known, they seize hold of it greatly and draw it into the abundance of divergences of the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achra</span> that hold onto the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> of this world, and it cannot ascend to be included in the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>. For from this world it is impossible for the soul to ascend and be included in the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> except specifically when it comes inside a physical body &mdash; for then it is drawn to the ultimate extreme of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, and precisely then it is able to rise up and be included from there specifically in the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>. For this is why Hashem, may He be blessed, created man with the entire world that depends upon him, in physical bodies &mdash; so that precisely from the ultimate extreme of physicality, which is very, very distant from Him, may He be blessed, from there precisely they will be included in His unity, may He be blessed &mdash; which is the essential glory of Him, as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- NACHALOS §25 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;25</div>

<p>And therefore the angels protested the creation of man and said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;What is man that You should remember him?&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 8:5)</span>. And similarly, they protested the giving of the Torah to Israel in this physical world, for they said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Place Your glory upon the heavens!&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 8:2)</span>. For certainly even all the angels are in the aspect of <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> relative to Him, may He be blessed &mdash; for He, may He be blessed, is above all spirituality, and is exalted and elevated above all the angels. Therefore they thought that also through them the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> could be revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> &mdash; which is the essential purpose of the creation of man and the giving of the Torah. But Hashem, may He be blessed, rebuked them and did not wish to listen to them, and created man in a physical body specifically, and gave us the Torah in this physical world specifically. For the essential revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is specifically from within very diverse activities that are the most distant &mdash; which are human beings clothed in physical bodies specifically, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the great severity of the sin of wasting seed in vain, G&ndash;d forbid &mdash; for then spirits etc. are created without a body, because the drop was not drawn to a G&ndash;d-fearing woman so that from it would come the aspect of <span class="key-term">holadah</span>, through which precisely the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> is drawn, as above. But when the drop does not come into a body, G&ndash;d forbid, spirits etc. are made from it, G&ndash;d forbid, from which it is very difficult for the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> to be revealed, as above. And therefore the essential repair for this is through the recitation of <i>Shema</i> upon the bed, which is the aspect of the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, through saying <span class="verse">&ldquo;Hear, O Israel.&rdquo;</span> And the essential repair is when one merits to say it with such concentration that one fashions bodies for the drops, etc., as is explained in the Kavanos.</p>

<p>And therefore, in truth, the essential repair is through the <span class="key-term">tzaddikay emes</span>, when one merits to draw close to them, etc. But in any case, it is understood from the Kavanos that it is impossible to repair them except by bringing them into the aspect of bodies; see there. That is, as above. And this is the aspect of the ten chapters of Tehillim that our Master, our Teacher, and our Rebbe, of blessed memory, established to recite for this repair &mdash; for they are the aspect of the ten types of melody, the aspect of simple song, etc., mentioned above, through which comes the essential revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> &mdash; through which is the essential repair, as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- NACHALOS §26 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;26</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;You, Hashem, are enthroned forever; Your throne is from generation to generation&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Lamentations 5:19)</span> &mdash; &ldquo;from generation to generation&rdquo; precisely. For it has already been explained above that the essential repair of His throne to sit upon is through <span class="key-term">todah/halachah</span>, through which the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed, etc., as above. And therefore, precisely through the abundance of generations, they repair and prepare His throne for Him to sit upon &mdash; in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Your throne, from generation to generation,&rdquo;</span> precisely. For precisely through the begetting of the generations, the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, etc., as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- NACHALOS §27 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;27</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;For a hand is upon the throne of Hashem &mdash; Hashem&rsquo;s war against Amalaik, from generation to generation&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 17:16)</span> &mdash; that the Holy One, blessed be He, swore that His Name and His throne are not complete until the memory of Amalaik is blotted out. For Amalaik is the aspect of a denier, as is brought elsewhere &mdash; who constantly intensifies with denials and confusions of faith, and fights against the true <span class="key-term">tzaddikim</span> and the upright ones who engage in revealing the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> &mdash; which is accomplished through the abundance of generations, as above, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and to generation after generation is His faithfulness,&rdquo;</span> which concludes <i>Mizmor l&rsquo;Todah</i> &mdash; which speaks of all of this, as is explained in the Torah mentioned above &mdash; through which comes the essential preparation of His throne, etc., as above.</p>

<p>And therefore Amalaik, who blemishes all of this &mdash; His Name, may He be blessed, and His throne are not complete until the memory of Amalaik is blotted out. For the essential repair of the throne in fullness is through the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, etc., which is drawn through the abundance of generations, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Your throne, from generation to generation.&rdquo;</span> And Amalaik, who blemishes all of this &mdash; therefore the war of Hashem against Amalaik is <span class="verse">&ldquo;from generation to generation,&rdquo;</span> precisely. And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;For a hand is upon the throne of Hashem &mdash; Hashem&rsquo;s war against Amalaik, from generation to generation&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that His throne, as it were, is not complete until He wins His war against Amalaik in every generation. And then it will be fulfilled: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And Hashem shall sit forever, having established His throne for judgment&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 9:8)</span> &mdash; that the Name will be complete and the throne will be complete, as Rashi explains. For the throne will be completed through the upright ones of every generation, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Your throne, from generation to generation,&rdquo;</span> as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- NACHALOS §28 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;28</div>

<p>And the wise person who desires truth can understand in his heart, according to our words, the immensity of the war in every generation &mdash; and in particular, what is done with him in that generation in which he lives. For the essential war with each and every individual in particular is the overpowering of the flooding of the bloods, from which come all the troubles in body, soul, and money. For the essential troubles are the overpowering of the desires and evil traits that embitter a person&rsquo;s life and bring him to what they bring him, G&ndash;d forbid &mdash; and from there come all the sufferings in body, money, and children, etc., G&ndash;d forbid.</p>

<p>And at the time of the intensification of the troubles, one does not know at all what to do, and the bloods flood upon the heart &mdash; like one who seeks counsel and strategy to emerge from the trouble, as is explained at the beginning of the Torah mentioned above. And afterward, Hashem, may He be blessed, in His mercy brings him out of the trouble &mdash; for Hashem, may He be blessed, performs revealed and hidden miracles and wonders with every person, every single day, as above. And as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The wicked watches the righteous,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 37:32)</span>. And as our Sages of blessed memory said: &ldquo;Every day,&rdquo; etc. &mdash; &ldquo;and were the Holy One, blessed be He, not helping him,&rdquo; etc. &mdash; for <span class="verse">&ldquo;Hashem will not abandon him in his hand&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 37:33)</span>. And as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;He rescues the poor from one who is stronger than him,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 35:10)</span>.</p>

<p>And all the salvations and miracles are all through the power of the <span class="key-term">tzaddikay emes</span>, who instill in us the ability to cry out and to raise our eyes at every moment to Hashem, may He be blessed &mdash; which is the essential glory of Him, may He be blessed, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Call upon Me on the day of trouble; I will deliver you, and you will honor Me&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 50:15)</span>.</p>

<p>But even though Hashem, may He be blessed, does many kindnesses and miracles and wonders with us every day and at every time, in every generation, and with each individual in particular &mdash; even so, the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achra</span>, the aspect of Amalaik, constantly undermines, slandering and accusing and inciting and provoking each and every person. For he is the Satan, he is the inciter, he is the accuser, as our Sages of blessed memory said: &ldquo;He descends and incites,&rdquo; etc. And as is brought in the holy Zohar regarding the war of Amalaik: &ldquo;The battle is above and below&rdquo; &mdash; that is, as above; and understand.</p>

<p>And therefore one must walk very, very much with the counsel mentioned above &mdash; to look at every moment at the immensity of the expanses and salvations and wonders that He has already done with us, etc., as above, and to find expanses even within the troubles themselves, as above. And through this, one will be accustomed always to give praise and thanksgiving to Him, may He be blessed, for everything that &ldquo;until here He has helped us&rdquo; with His immense wonders. And as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;I have awakened, and I am still with You&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 139:18)</span> &mdash; and as Rashi explains: &ldquo;I have come to the end of all the generations, and I am still with You&rdquo; &mdash; that is, even now, in these latter days, which is the aspect of the end of all the generations, even now &ldquo;I am still with You&rdquo; &mdash; that there is still in each and every one of us the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;yet a little, and there is no wicked one,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 37:10)</span> &mdash; which is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;I will sing to my G&ndash;d while I yet live (&lsquo;b&rsquo;odi&rsquo;),&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; that one must walk in this very much, as he, of blessed memory, warned us. And the main thing is to give thanks and praise to Hashem, may He be blessed, for this always, and especially in a time of trouble, G&ndash;d forbid &mdash; that precisely then one should strengthen himself to pay attention, to look at the wondrous true and eternal salvations that Hashem, may He be blessed, has already performed for him, etc.</p>

<p>And through the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah/halachah</span>, etc. &mdash; through this, one will merit that truth will illuminate, etc., until one draws the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> &mdash; through which the trouble is nullified. And through this, the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah</span> grows, etc., as above &mdash; and so it cycles around for the good, etc., as above. And if the opposition, the aspect of Amalaik, returns and intensifies &mdash; the choice is in his hand to return and strengthen himself through all the above. And as soon as he sets his heart to this, Hashem, may He be blessed, will help him in this greatly &mdash; for <span class="verse">&ldquo;the kindnesses of Hashem have not ceased,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Lamentations 3:22)</span>. And so each time, until he merits, through His mercy, may He be blessed, and through the power of the <span class="key-term">tzaddikay emes</span>, to win the war &mdash; and then he will merit <span class="key-term">todah</span> in fullness, which is the essential delight of the World to Come. Fortunate is he! And there will be fulfilled in him: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Fortunate is the person whose strength is in You&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 84:6)</span>, etc. For one needs boldness and immense strengthening and great stubbornness beyond measure &mdash; whoever desires to draw close to Hashem, may He be blessed. And the essential strengthening is through all the above; and understand well, very well.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- NACHALOS §29 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;29</div>

<p>And regarding <span class="key-term">yibum</span> and <span class="key-term">chalitzah</span> that we mentioned above, we did not explain it well, for this is not the place for it.</p>

<p>And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And she shall remove his shoe from upon his foot&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Deuteronomy 25:9)</span> &mdash; for there the soul of the deceased is bound, as is brought. For the essential blemish is in the legs (<i>raglayim</i>) &mdash; where the bloods need to flow in their proper order when one merits <span class="key-term">holadah</span>. And this one who did not merit to leave seed blemished in this &mdash; and therefore: <span class="verse">&ldquo;She shall remove his shoe from upon his foot&rdquo;</span> &mdash; &ldquo;his foot&rdquo; precisely. And therefore the <span class="key-term">halachos</span> are called <span class="verse">&ldquo;the goings (<i>halichos</i>) of the world&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Habakkuk 3:6)</span> &mdash; for the essential fullness of the <span class="key-term">halachah</span> is that one should merit through it to walk (<i>lailaich</i>) in it, to draw close through it to Hashem, may He be blessed, to His service &mdash; the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;the goings of the world&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that one should merit to remain standing in holiness forever and ever.</p>

<p>For the world in general is called the aspect of &ldquo;legs&rdquo; relative to Him, may He be blessed, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And the earth is My footstool&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Isaiah 66:1)</span>. And the woman and the money, where the essential overpowering of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> takes place, are called &ldquo;his legs,&rdquo; as is explained elsewhere. And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The heavens are My throne and the earth is My footstool; what house will you build for Me?&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Isaiah 66:1)</span>. For the essential repair of His throne in the heavens is precisely through &ldquo;the earth, My footstool&rdquo; &mdash; through the legs, which are the very lowest levels, where the essential abundance of <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> resides &mdash; when they are included in His unity, may He be blessed, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Hashem in the heavens has established His throne, and His sovereignty rules over all&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 103:19)</span>. For precisely when they know that His sovereignty rules over all, and all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> are from Him, may He be blessed &mdash; then precisely <span class="verse">&ldquo;in the heavens He has established His throne,&rdquo;</span> as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <i>Mishkan</i> and the Bais HaMikdash, the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Exalt Hashem our G&ndash;d and prostrate yourselves at His footstool,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 99:5)</span>. And this is the aspect of what is brought in the writings [of the Ari z&rdquo;l] &mdash; that the essential completion of the repair will be when it is fulfilled: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And His feet shall stand on that day,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Zechariah 14:4)</span>, in the aspect of &ldquo;until the feet reach the feet&rdquo; &mdash; that is, as above. And therefore the essential repair is through all the above, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah/halachah</span>, the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;the goings of the world,&rdquo;</span> the aspect of the repair of the legs, as above.</p>


<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- APOTROPOS SUBDIVISION -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<h2 class="sub-header">Apotropos <span class="sub-header-en">[Laws of Guardianship]</span></h2>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- APOTROPOS §30 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;30</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of what our Sages of blessed memory said in the Mishnah: &ldquo;A guardian (<i>apotropos</i>) whom the father of orphans appointed does not swear; one whom the <i>beis din</i> appointed does swear&rdquo; <span class="inline-source">(Gittin 52a)</span>. For it has already been explained &mdash; the matter of inheritance that belongs to children: the begetting of children is drawn through the money of holiness of the <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraysa</span>, from which comes all the money in the world, as above. For the essential obligation to leave children is only for this purpose &mdash; so that the children who were born through the <span class="key-term">halachos</span> that were born through the <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraysa</span>, from which come all the births in the world, as above, should draw all the repairs that are drawn through the <span class="key-term">halachos</span>, which are the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah/hoda&rsquo;ah</span> &mdash; which is to illuminate truth in the world and to complete the speech, until they merit to reveal the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from within the abundance of <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> &mdash; which are the children of the seed of Israel who have multiplied in the world. For the more the seed of Israel multiplies, among whom there is great divergence of opinions, as above &mdash; and when they are all included in one <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> and unify His Name, may He be blessed &mdash; through this, the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed even more from within very many diverse activities, which is the essential preciousness of the holiness of the enlargement of His glory, may He be blessed, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of what the children say <span class="key-term">Kaddish</span> after the death of their father and mother. For this person who has departed &mdash; his entire purpose is to merit a portion of the World to Come. And the essential delight of the World to Come is <span class="key-term">todah/hoda&rsquo;ah</span>, as above, through which the holiness of the holy Shabbos is drawn, which is the aspect of the World to Come, through which the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed, etc. &mdash; for the sake of all of which man comes to this world. And therefore, after his death, when he needs to come to this &mdash; to the aspect of the delight of the World to Come, which is to give thanks and praise to His Name, may He be blessed, as above &mdash; therefore the children say <span class="key-term">Kaddish</span> after him, which is not a prayer for the deceased but rather a wondrous and awesome praise and thanksgiving to Hashem, may He be blessed, as is brought. For <span class="key-term">Kaddish</span> includes all kinds of praises and blessings and thanksgivings, etc. &mdash; for it is an exceedingly wondrous and awesome praise that &ldquo;shatters all bars of iron,&rdquo; as is brought in the holy Zohar. And as we say: &ldquo;May He be blessed and praised and glorified and exalted,&rdquo; etc. &mdash; &ldquo;Blessed is He, above all blessings and songs and praises,&rdquo; etc. And therefore we say <span class="key-term">Kaddish</span> after all the blessings and thanksgivings, and similarly after all the <span class="key-term">halachos</span> that are studied &mdash; for it is the pillar between world and world, as is brought. For <span class="key-term">Kaddish</span> includes all the thanksgivings and songs and praises and elevates them all to their supernal root, higher and higher, unto the Infinite.</p>

<p>And therefore this departed one, whose entire repair is that the parts of good within him should be gathered &mdash; according to what he merited to do good in the world, the entire purpose of which is <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span>, which is the delight of the World to Come, and he now needs to come to this, that he should have some portion in the delight of the World to Come, which is <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span>, as above &mdash; therefore his children say <span class="key-term">Kaddish</span> after him, which is the totality of all the thanksgivings and songs and praises, etc., and elevates them all, as above. And therefore, through this precisely, the children give their father merit for the World to Come &mdash; for praise and thanksgiving, this is the entire delight of the World to Come, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore the essential thing is that the children specifically should say <span class="key-term">Kaddish</span> &mdash; for his essential repair is through his children specifically, whom he merited to beget in the world and to multiply the seed of Israel, all of whom engage all their days in thanksgivings and blessings. For every single Jew says every day many blessings and thanksgivings, as our Sages of blessed memory established for us &mdash; to say blessings and thanksgivings over every matter in the world, and especially in the morning and evening at the time of prayer &mdash; for <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span> is the entire delight of the World to Come, as above. And through this, all the repairs mentioned above are accomplished, until one merits to reveal the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from the abundance of <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> &mdash; which is accomplished through the abundance of children that he merited to beget, through <span class="key-term">todah/halachah</span>, as above.</p>

<p>Therefore the children specifically say <span class="key-term">Kaddish</span>, which is the totality of all the thanksgivings &mdash; in order to elevate all the blessings and thanksgivings that this departed one merited to engage in during his lifetime. For the essential repair is through the children who were born through this &mdash; for through them specifically, the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed even more from within the abundance of <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, which is the essential completion of the fullness of the repair, as above. And therefore each person must, during his lifetime, before he departs from the world, command his children and arrange the order of the division of his possessions and money to his children. For the essential root of money and its repair is according to what he merited to support true <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span>, through whom <span class="key-term">halachos</span> are born, from which come all the births of children, as above. And every single Jew has a portion in this according to his level. And therefore he must arrange, according to his level, the order of the division of his money to his children after him &mdash; that each one should receive his portion properly, according to the root of his portion above in the <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraysa</span> who birth <span class="key-term">halachos</span>, from which come all his births &mdash; through which comes the entire repair of the departed one. For <span class="key-term">todah/halachah</span> and <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraysa</span> and the births of children are all one aspect, as is explained in the Torah mentioned above &mdash; and everything depends upon each other.</p>

<p>And this is the entire purpose and repair of the departed one for the World to Come, as above &mdash; for through all of this, the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed, etc., as above. And therefore he must appoint a guardian (<i>apotropos</i>) himself during his lifetime. For the guardian appointed over the orphans, who is in the aspect of &ldquo;father of orphans,&rdquo; must be appointed by the mouth of the father of the children himself &mdash; in order that he arrange his inheritance according to the mind of the father himself, according to what he drew upon himself the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah/hoda&rsquo;ah/halachah</span>, according to what he merited with his money to be among the <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraysa</span> &mdash; which is the entire repair of the money, from which come the births of children, etc., as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- APOTROPOS §31 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;31</div>

<p>And therefore a guardian whom the father of orphans appointed does not swear &mdash; for he is not suspected of falsehood, for truth surely illuminates in him, as is explained there in the Torah mentioned above &mdash; that through <span class="key-term">todah/halachah</span>, truth illuminates, etc. And therefore, since the owner of the inheritance himself appointed him as guardian, truth surely illuminates in him in this matter. For since the departed one, the owner of the inheritance himself, appointed him as guardian according to his own mind, according to his level, according to what he merited to clarify his money so as to have a portion among the <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraysa</span> &mdash; which is the essential repair of the inheritance and the money from which come all the children, as above &mdash; therefore, surely, according to his level, truth illuminates, etc.</p>

<p>For through the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah/halachah</span>, the aspect of <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraysa</span>, the aspect of the births of children &mdash; through all of this, truth illuminates, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Grant truth to Yaakov, kindness to Avraham,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Micah 7:20)</span>. And therefore this guardian is not suspected of falsehood and is trusted without an oath at all, since the father of the children himself appointed him according to his level, according to his portion in the delight of the World to Come, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraysa</span>, etc., as above.</p>

<p>But if he did not merit to appoint a guardian himself, to transmit by himself to the guardian the order of his inheritance according to his level, etc., as above &mdash; then the <i>beis din</i> must be the &ldquo;father of orphans&rdquo; and appoint the guardian. For only the <i>beis din</i> has the power for this, for the <i>beis din</i> illuminates truth &mdash; for before them are all the <span class="key-term">halachos</span> of all the laws and judgments of the Torah, through which truth illuminates, as above. For this is the essence of the <i>beis din</i> &mdash; that they should know all the <span class="key-term">halachos</span> and judge with true and righteous judgments. And therefore the <i>beis din</i> must be three, the aspect of the three lines of truth mentioned above.</p>

<p>But the <i>beis din</i> cannot clarify the truth of each individual except through the oath &mdash; as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The owner of the house shall approach the judges for an oath&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 22:7)</span>. For as soon as they come to court, this is because there is a denial between them, and all denials are drawn from the flooding of the bloods mentioned above, from the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;men of blood hate the innocent&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Proverbs 29:10)</span>, as is brought there in the Torah mentioned above; see there. For all of this is the aspect of the blemish of <span class="key-term">todah/halachah</span>, the blemish of the money of holiness, which is in the aspect of <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraysa</span> who birth <span class="key-term">halachos</span> &mdash; for he denies his fellow, which is the opposite of all of this. Therefore the <i>beis din</i> cannot clarify except through the oath. For an oath is the aspect of binding, as is brought &mdash; the aspect of the illumination of the three lines of truth within the fourfold speech, which is the aspect of the seven days of creation, as is brought elsewhere. This is the aspect of <i>shevuah</i> [oath], from the word <i>sheva</i> [seven] &mdash; the aspect of the binding of the weekdays to the seventh day, which is Shabbos, which is <span class="verse">&ldquo;an eternal covenant between Me and the children of Israel,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 31:17)</span>. For Shabbos is &ldquo;the Name of the Holy One, blessed be He,&rdquo; the aspect of &ldquo;the Torah is the Name of the Holy One, blessed be He&rdquo; &mdash; and this is the aspect of the oath, which is in the Name and with holding an object, which is the Torah.</p>

<p>For when there is a denial, which is the blemish of truth, the <i>beis din</i> cannot illuminate truth except through the oath, which includes all the repairs of truth &mdash; which is the illumination of the three lines of truth within the fourfold speech, etc. And therefore, since the departed one did not merit to appoint a guardian himself and did not illuminate by himself the aspect of truth that he merited to clarify, according to his portion, in <span class="key-term">todah/halachah</span> in the aspect of <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraysa</span>, as above, until the <i>beis din</i> was compelled to involve themselves in appointing a guardian &mdash; therefore he requires an oath. For when truth is not clarified in fullness and the <i>beis din</i> needs to clarify it, they cannot clarify it except through the oath, etc., as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- APOTROPOS §32 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;32</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;For I have known him, in order that he command his children and his household after him, and they shall keep the way of Hashem, to do <i>tzedakah</i> and justice&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Genesis 18:19)</span>. For the essential bequest that a person must command his children and his household after him is that they should keep the way of Hashem, to do <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span> and justice &mdash; <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span> and justice precisely. That is, that they should give <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span> to true <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span> who birth <span class="key-term">halachos</span>, which are the judgments of the Torah. And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span> and justice &mdash; that is, <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span> to true <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span>, through whom the judicial <span class="key-term">halachos</span> of the Torah are born and revealed &mdash; which is the essential repair of the money of this departed one who labored for it during his lifetime, whose entire repair is when the money comes to true <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span> from whom <span class="key-term">halachos</span> are born, which are the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah/hoda&rsquo;ah</span>, the delight of the World to Come &mdash; and to this he must now enter, that he should have a portion in the delight of the World to Come, as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- APOTROPOS §33 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;33</div>

<p>And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Truth and the judgment of peace, judge in your gates&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Zechariah 8:16)</span>. For the judges must judge truth in order to merit through this peace &mdash; that all should be included in one <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span>, through which the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, etc., as above.</p>

<p>And therefore our Sages of blessed memory said: &ldquo;Whoever judges a true judgment to its truth becomes a partner with the Holy One, blessed be He, in the act of creation&rdquo; <span class="inline-source">(Shabbos 10a)</span> &mdash; as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And it was evening and it was morning, one day&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Genesis 1:5)</span>, etc. For it is written &ldquo;one day&rdquo; and not &ldquo;the first day&rdquo; &mdash; to teach that the Holy One, blessed be He, was alone in His world. That is, to teach that all the divergences in creation, which are the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and it was evening and it was morning&rdquo;</span> &mdash; which includes all the divergences in the world, for the divergence between day and night, between light and darkness, is the greatest of all divergences (and as we say in the blessing of <i>Krias Shema</i>: &ldquo;and with understanding He changes the times&rdquo;), and in this are included all the many divergences of each and every day, without end &mdash; and everything was created and continues to exist in order that the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> should be revealed precisely from within the abundance of <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, as above.</p>

<p>And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And it was evening and it was morning&rdquo;</span> &mdash; which are the totality of all divergences &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;one day&rdquo;</span> &mdash; in the aspect of Him being alone in His world. That is, to reveal His unity, may He be blessed &mdash; that the lone Primordial One created everything, and all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> are drawn from His unity, may He be blessed. And therefore the judge who judges a true judgment to its truth merits this &mdash; that he becomes a partner with the Holy One, blessed be He, in the act of creation, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And it was evening,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;one day.&rdquo;</span> For through truth, the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> &mdash; which is the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and it was evening and it was morning &mdash; one day,&rdquo;</span> as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- APOTROPOS §34 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;34</div>

<p>The sum of the matter is that a person must accustom himself to give thanks and praise to Hashem, may He be blessed, always, in all that passes over him, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;In Hashem I praise a word; in G&ndash;d I praise a word&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 56:11)</span> &mdash; both in His goodness and in His severity, G&ndash;d forbid, as our Sages of blessed memory said. And this is a good and wondrous counsel &mdash; that even when a person has become as distant from Hashem, may He be blessed, as he has become, and also in the affairs of this world he is greatly pressed in livelihood and children, etc. (as is common among the majority of the world, as explained elsewhere) &mdash; he must precisely then seek and find an expansion within the straits of the trouble, and also remind himself of all the good things and wonders that Hashem, may He be blessed, has already done with him. And the main thing: that He did not make me a gentile and separated us from those who go astray, etc.</p>

<p>And to remind himself that nothing will remain of him or of any person at all except what he seized in this world of some good from the holiness of Israel &mdash; and only this is his portion from all his toil. And therefore each person, even the worst of the worst, must rejoice in this greatly, and his mouth should be filled with His praise, etc. all day long &mdash; to give thanks and praise and laud, etc. the Fashioner of creation, Who did not make us, etc. &mdash; Who did not set our portion like theirs, etc. And once he is accustomed to this, he will certainly seize, every day, to learn some <span class="key-term">halachos</span> of the Torah, which are His knowledge, may He be blessed &mdash; through which one comes to know Him, may He be blessed, and is included in Him, may He be blessed. And through this itself, one will emerge from all the troubles, as above. And through this, the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> will be revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, etc. &mdash; and through this comes the essential nullification of the trouble, etc. &mdash; and so it cycles around for the good, until in the end of all ends, he will certainly merit his good ultimate purpose, which is the delight of the World to Come &mdash; which is to give thanks and praise to Him, may He be blessed, forever and to all eternity.</p>

<p>And the essential thing for all of this is love of friends and peace &mdash; that one should have great love and peace with all Israel, and especially with those who walk in this path. And he should be among the <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraysa</span>, both with his money and with his body &mdash; that he should support with all his strength the <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span> who engage in this path, who birth <span class="key-term">halachos</span>. And through this, he will merit to beget worthy children who engage in Torah, etc., etc. &mdash; as was explained above: <span class="key-term">todah/halachah</span> and <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraysa</span> and the births of children are all one aspect and depend upon each other. And one must begin from every single good point among them, until he merits what he merits. Fortunate is he!</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- APOTROPOS §35 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;35</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of what our Sages of blessed memory said: &ldquo;What is meant by the verse: <span class="verse">&lsquo;Who is the wise man who will understand this, and to whom the mouth of Hashem has spoken that he may declare it &mdash; on what account has the land been destroyed, parched like a desert, with none passing through?&rsquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Jeremiah 9:11)</span>. <span class="verse">&lsquo;And Hashem said: Because they forsook My Torah,&rsquo;</span> etc. &mdash; <span class="verse">&lsquo;and did not heed My voice and did not walk in it&rsquo;</span>&rdquo; <span class="inline-source">(Jeremiah 9:12)</span>. And they explained there: &ldquo;that they did not bless over the Torah first&rdquo; <span class="inline-source">(Nedarim 81a)</span>.</p>

<p>And the matter is astonishing, as all the commentators were astonished by it. And especially that which they said there: &ldquo;This matter was asked of the Sages and the Prophets and they could not explain it, until the Holy One, blessed be He, Himself explained it&rdquo; &mdash; and it is wondrous. What is this great commotion &mdash; who does not know all this, that the destruction of the Bais HaMikdash was because they transgressed the Torah? Is not the entire Torah full of this? For Moshe Rabbeinu, peace be upon him, himself already warned them: <span class="verse">&ldquo;If you walk in My statutes,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;and if you do not listen,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Leviticus 26)</span>. And similarly, in innumerable other places, he told them that if they transgress the Torah they would be lost from the land, etc. And similarly, all the Prophets warned them about this. And what is this &mdash; that now they asked everyone &ldquo;on what account was the land destroyed,&rdquo; and they could not explain it, until Hashem, may He be blessed, Himself explained it: &ldquo;Because they forsook My Torah,&rdquo; etc.?</p>

<p>But the essential matter is that Hashem, may He be blessed, asked the Sages and the Prophets to understand this well and to declare on what account the land was destroyed &mdash; in a manner that good would come to us from it, that we would understand through this good counsel for how to begin to repair the corruptions that caused the destruction of the Bais HaMikdash. And this is the essential severity and depth of the question that Hashem, may He be blessed, asked the Sages and the Prophets, and they could not explain it. For what was, was &mdash; and what difference does it make if it was destroyed on account of whatever it was destroyed on account of? It is already destroyed! But the essential thrust of what Hashem, may He be blessed, sought to ask the Sages and the Prophets &mdash; that they should understand this and declare on what account the land was destroyed &mdash; is that they should explain the matter well, in a manner that we would understand from it counsel for how to emerge from the corruptions that caused the destruction of the Bais HaMikdash. And therefore they could not explain it, for this is very, very deep &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;deep, deep &mdash; who can find it?&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Ecclesiastes 7:24)</span>.</p>

<p>Until the Holy One, blessed be He, Himself explained it: &ldquo;Because they forsook My Torah, and did not heed My voice, and did not walk in it.&rdquo; That is, even though they had already transgressed very severe transgressions &mdash; idolatry, etc. &mdash; even so, in the inner depths of their hearts, their hearts were still burning for Hashem, may He be blessed. For <span class="verse">&ldquo;many waters cannot extinguish the love&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Song of Songs 8:7)</span> between Israel and their Father in Heaven, <span class="verse">&ldquo;and rivers cannot wash it away.&rdquo;</span> And therefore they should have strengthened themselves, at least to seize some <span class="key-term">halachos</span>, to learn at least a little every day. But &ldquo;they forsook My Torah entirely.&rdquo; And not only that, but &ldquo;they did not heed My voice&rdquo; &mdash; &ldquo;hearing depends upon the heart&rdquo; &mdash; that is, they were at least obligated to hear and to attach themselves to the voice of Hashem that calls with a great voice in a person&rsquo;s heart every single day and at every time, that he should return to Him. And every person must incline his heart to hear the voice of Hashem &mdash; that at least he should have strong desires and great yearnings for Hashem, may He be blessed, which is very precious, as is explained elsewhere.</p>

<p>And the main thing: &ldquo;And they did not walk in it &mdash; that they did not bless over the Torah first.&rdquo; For certainly they did not fall in one stroke to such falls, to transgress the law entirely and throw off the yoke as it was at the time of the destruction. And certainly at first they engaged in Torah somewhat &mdash; only &ldquo;they did not bless over the Torah first.&rdquo; That is, they did not set their hearts to rejoice in the Torah, and to bless and give thanks and praise to Hashem, may He be blessed, at every time, for the wondrous and awesome kindness that He did with us, in that He chose us from all the nations and gave us His Torah, the hidden treasure, which is our life, etc. &mdash; and this is our entire hope forever.</p>

<p>And as is explained in the commentators, this is the essential meaning of the blessing over the Torah &mdash; to rejoice with all one&rsquo;s strength in the pleasantness of our portion and our lot. And therefore our Sages of blessed memory said that the blessing over the Torah requires great care &mdash; that is, the entire matter mentioned above that we have explained: that each person, even if he has fallen and become as distant as he has, even so, he precisely must be accustomed to <span class="key-term">todah</span> and <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span>, to give thanks for the small amount of good points that still remain in him, etc. And through this, he will merit to emerge from all the troubles and to draw close to Hashem, may He be blessed, etc., as above.</p>

<p>And this is: &ldquo;And they did not walk in it&rdquo; &mdash; for this is a wondrous path and way to draw close and to raise oneself to Hashem, may He be blessed, from all kinds of falls and descents in the world, without end or limit. And had they walked in this path, certainly they would not have fallen so far and they would not have had such troubles. And now, our entire hope to return to our land and to our Bais HaMikdash is through this &mdash; for this matter depends upon nothing but <span class="key-term">teshuvah</span>. But it is very difficult to return, for the adversary lies in wait very, very greatly and spreads himself in length and breadth. And everyone desires to fear Your Name, and even so, most are very far from the paths of <span class="key-term">teshuvah</span>. And the main reason is because they do not set their hearts to rejoice in the small amount of good that is in them &mdash; for sadness and melancholy harm more than anything, and as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Because you did not serve Hashem your G&ndash;d with joy and with gladness of heart&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Deuteronomy 28:47)</span> &mdash; that the essential destruction and all the troubles, may the Merciful One save us, are all because they did not serve Him, may He be blessed, with joy &mdash; as is brought in the writings of the Ari z&rdquo;l. That is, as above; and understand well.</p>

<p>And therefore Hashem, may He be blessed, was compelled to explain it Himself &mdash; in order to hint to us now, in every generation, hints of counsel for how to draw close now to Hashem, may He be blessed, from wherever one is, to repair the corruptions through which the destruction occurred &mdash; until we merit a complete redemption soon. And therefore all the above is called &ldquo;walking&rdquo; &mdash; for it is the repair of the legs, as above, the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;the goings of the world&rdquo;</span> &mdash; through which comes the approach of the redemption, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and His feet shall stand,&rdquo;</span> etc., as above. For it is a wondrous path and way for every person in the world, etc., as above.</p>



<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- APOTROPOS §36 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;36</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of the work of the Mishkan, which they were commanded after the sin of the <i>eigel</i> [golden calf] &mdash; which occurred through the abundance of gold. Through this, the <i>eirev rav</i> [mixed multitude] incited and lured them to separate the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, G&ndash;d forbid, from the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> &mdash; which is the essential sin of idolatry. And the repair was through the Mishkan, which is the aspect of the Bais HaMikdash, the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;throne of glory, exalted from the beginning,&rdquo;</span> the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;the place of Your dwelling,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <i>shekalim</i> &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;When you raise the head of the children of Israel,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 30:12)</span> &mdash; that they should all be included together through the counting, and the counting should not cause, G&ndash;d forbid, the aspect of separation, which is the <i>sitra d&rsquo;mosa</i> [the side of death], in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and there shall not be a plague among them.&rdquo;</span> And this is through their giving a ransom for their souls &mdash; the aspect of <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraysa</span>, etc.</p>

<p>For the <i>eirev rav</i> blemished the money &mdash; for through the abundance of money they contended against Moshe. And not only did they not want to be among the <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraysa</span>, they even reversed to the opposite extreme &mdash; assembling upon Aharon to make them an idol from the money. For just as when one merits that money should be in holiness &mdash; the essence of which is through giving one&rsquo;s money to <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span>, to be among the <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraysa</span>, through which <span class="key-term">halachos</span> are born, etc. &mdash; through which the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> is drawn, as above &mdash; so too, in reverse, when one blemishes the money and chases after money only for one&rsquo;s own desires, and even contends against the true <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span> who engage in birthing <span class="key-term">halachos</span> &mdash; then one separates the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> and causes heresies in the world. This is the aspect of the blemish of the <i>eirev rav</i>, which came through the abundance of money, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;and enough gold&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Deuteronomy 1:1, per Chazal)</span> &mdash; through which they made idolatry and denied Hashem and separated in their minds the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> from the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>. This was the nature of all the matters of idolatry in the earlier generations &mdash; because it is impossible to comprehend in the mind how all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> are drawn from the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, through this they came to heresies until they made idolatry, and they had many false wisdoms in this, as our Sages of blessed memory said. And similarly, the heresies that are found now, in our many sins, through the investigators [philosophers] and those who contend against the true tzaddikim, who engage in external wisdoms &mdash; all of this is drawn from this, from the aspect of the sin of the <i>eigel</i>, from which we have not yet been purified, and all the visitations come through this, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And on the day that I visit,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 32:34)</span>. May Hashem, may He be blessed, protect and save us from now on.</p>

<p>And therefore the repair for this is the <i>shekalim</i> that they gave as donation for the Mishkan, from which the <i>adanim</i> [sockets] were made, upon which the entire Mishkan was erected. For there, in the Mishkan, all the <span class="key-term">halachos</span> of the Torah were born and revealed, as Rashi explains &mdash; that from the day the Mishkan was erected, Hashem did not speak to Moshe about any of the <span class="key-term">halachos</span> of the Torah except in the <i>Ohel Mo&rsquo;ed</i>. And therefore the <i>shekalim</i>, from which the <i>adanim</i> were made upon which the Mishkan stood, are in the aspect of the <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraysa</span> &mdash; for through the <span class="key-term">halachos</span> born from there, and likewise the blessings and thanksgivings that took place in the Mishkan, through all of this all the repairs mentioned above were accomplished, until the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> was revealed from there, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And I will meet with you there,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 25:22)</span> &mdash; in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And the Mishkan shall be one&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 26:6)</span>.</p>

<p>And therefore they were commanded to count them through the <i>shekalim</i>. For Moshe found this very difficult, as our Sages of blessed memory said, and as is brought in the <i>piyyut</i> of <i>Parashas Shekalim</i> &mdash; for how could he count Israel, who are above counting, for the entire holiness of Israel is to be included in the ultimate <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, for they are all as one man, as above, and as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;that cannot be counted,&rdquo;</span> etc. But Hashem, may He be blessed, commanded them to count them precisely through the <i>shekalim</i> &mdash; for through the <i>shekalim</i>, which are the aspect of the <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraysa</span>, through which the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> &mdash; which is very precious to Hashem, may He be blessed, when the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed below in this world, precisely from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>. And the more the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> multiply, which is the abundance of divergent opinions &mdash; when they are included together in one <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> to believe in the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, it is more and more precious in His eyes, may He be blessed, as above.</p>

<p>Therefore, through giving the <i>shekalim</i>, they must be counted precisely &mdash; for the counting is the aspect of multiplicity and divergence. They also needed to be counted by the number of names, mentioning each one by his name, which corresponds to the divergence of his intellect and his mind. And through the abundance of divergences, the plague can prevail, G&ndash;d forbid &mdash; which is the <i>sitra d&rsquo;mosa</i>, whose hold comes from the world of separation, from the abundance of divergences. But through the <i>shekalim</i>, etc. &mdash; through which the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed precisely from within the abundance of <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, etc. &mdash; through this, precisely a great repair is made through the counting, which is the aspect of the revelation of the abundance of divergences. For precisely through this, His glory, may He be blessed, is enlarged and exalted &mdash; through the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, may He be blessed, precisely through the abundance of divergences, as above &mdash; through all of them acknowledging one <span class="key-term">da&rsquo;as</span> and giving <i>shekalim</i> to the donation of the Mishkan, where His divinity is revealed, etc., as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- APOTROPOS §37 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;37</div>

<p>And therefore they were commanded to give specifically a half-shekel &mdash; to teach that each individual Jew has no completeness except through his fellow. For the essential repair is that they should all be included one within the other in love and unity &mdash; and each one is the aspect of a half, until he is included in his fellow, and his fellow in his fellow, until they are all included, in the abundance of their divergent minds, in the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> &mdash; which is very precious to Hashem, may He be blessed, as above.</p>

<p>And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The wealthy shall not give more and the poor shall not give less&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 30:15)</span> &mdash; which is the aspect of what is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;A person&rsquo;s ransom is his wealth, and a pauper does not hear rebuke&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Proverbs 13:8)</span>, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;and the noble is not distinguished before the poor&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Job 34:19)</span>, as Rashi explains there &mdash; that this was said regarding the <i>shekalim</i>, that each one gave equally a half-shekel, the wealthy and the poor, etc. That is, as above &mdash; for the essential purpose of the <i>shekalim</i> is to merit inclusiveness and unity. Therefore they all had to give equally, so that there would be no division and separation between the wealthy and the poor &mdash; and the wealthy should not grow proud or rebuke the poor. To teach that this is the essential repair of <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span>, whose essence is to be among the <span class="key-term">tom&rsquo;chay Oraysa</span> &mdash; for the essential thing is to merit love and unity, and the wealthy should not be proud over the poor. For the essential thing is to be included in the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, which is impossible to be included in except through humility and self-nullification, the aspect of love and unity &mdash; that each one should nullify himself before his fellow. And this He hinted to them through the <i>shekalim</i> &mdash; that He commanded they all give equally, the wealthy shall not give more and the poor shall not give less, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and the noble is not distinguished before the poor&rdquo;</span> mentioned above, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and a pauper does not hear rebuke.&rdquo;</span> To teach that they are all equal before Him, may He be blessed, and they all have a portion in the erection of the Mishkan &mdash; through which the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> that are included together, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore, in truth, regarding the other donations of the Mishkan, each one gave according to the blessing of Hashem and according to the generosity of his heart, as Rashi explains there: &ldquo;Three donations are mentioned here.&rdquo; But regarding the <i>shekalim</i>, He warned them that they all give equally &mdash; so that the wealthy would learn and understand hints for themselves, that they should never be proud of their giving, even when they give much. For it is fitting for them to understand that Hashem, may He be blessed, could erect the Mishkan through the poor just as through the wealthy &mdash; for <span class="verse">&ldquo;wealth and honor come from before Him,&rdquo;</span> and He can impoverish this one and enrich that one.</p>

<p>And certainly, whoever has a little true understanding, it is fitting for him to understand that he should not be proud &mdash; even the wealthy one who gives much <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span> to true <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span>. On the contrary, it is fitting for him to be ashamed and greatly self-nullified &mdash; who is he that he has merited this, that Hashem, may He be blessed, has given him such wealth that he merits to support the <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span>? And moreover, he still has much wealth and riches remaining in his house, for certainly he does not even give half of his wealth. And the poor and destitute person, who is a worthy person just like him and usually more so than him, has no bread or garment in his house, and also does not merit to support the <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span> with his money. And how can one be proud of the wealth that Hashem, may He be blessed, has given him, that much remains with him and he also supports the <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span>, that he merits to have an everlasting investment?</p>

<p>And all of this, Hashem, may He be blessed, hinted to them through the <i>shekalim</i> that He commanded they all give equally &mdash; to teach that, just as the <i>adanim</i> that uphold the Mishkan were made through the donation of the <i>shekalim</i> that all gave equally, so too Hashem, may He be blessed, could have made the entire Mishkan through all of them equally. But He desires to bestow merit upon each one according to his worth, according to His designs that have been reckoned for him. But you, the wealthy &mdash; do not be proud, for everything is from Him, as David said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;For everything is from You, and from Your hand we have given to You&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(I Chronicles 29:14)</span>. For the essential <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span> is to support the <span class="key-term">talmidai chachamim</span> who birth <span class="key-term">halachos</span> &mdash; which is the aspect of the erection of the Mishkan that the tzaddikim, in the aspect of Moshe in every generation, engage in &mdash; for the essential thing is love and inclusiveness, through which the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, etc., as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- APOTROPOS §38 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;38</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of Purim, which is the obliteration of Haman-Amalaik. For Amalaik blemishes everything mentioned above, as was explained above (in &sect;27). For <span class="verse">&ldquo;Amalaik is the first of the nations&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Numbers 24:20)</span> &mdash; he is the aspect of a heretic and he wants to confuse and cast blemish upon the &ldquo;beginning&rdquo; and the &ldquo;start&rdquo; &mdash; as if Hashem, may He be blessed, has not yet begun to save at all. For he was the first to come to wage war against Israel when they went out of Egypt, and he strengthened himself in his wickedness to stand against Israel, for whom Hashem, may He be blessed, had performed such miracles in the Exodus from Egypt, until Pharaoh was compelled to acknowledge <span class="verse">&ldquo;that Hashem is the righteous One&rdquo;</span> and expelled them from Egypt. And Amalaik is such a brazen one that he went out against them, and as Rashi explains there on the verse <span class="verse">&ldquo;Write this as a memorial in the book&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 17:14)</span> &mdash; a parable of a boiling bath, etc. For he is a heretic from beginning to end, denying the miracles and wonders that Hashem, may He be blessed, does with us at all times, and blemishing all the repairs explained above &mdash; and the main thing is that he provokes and strengthens himself so that the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> should not, G&ndash;d forbid, be revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, as above.</p>

<p>And he lies in wait against all Israel constantly, and principally he strengthens himself, G&ndash;d forbid, in time of exile and trouble &mdash; for then he wants to cast heresies into the heart, as if Hashem, may He be blessed, has not yet begun to save Israel at all. And this is the aspect of the strengthening of Haman-Amalaik at the end of the exile of Babylon &mdash; for he said: since Nevuchadnetzar has already prevailed and destroyed the Bais HaMikdash which stood for several hundred years and exiled Israel from their land, etc. &mdash; they no longer have hope to return, G&ndash;d forbid. And therefore he and his impure offspring strengthened themselves to halt the rebuilding of the Bais HaMikdash &mdash; for he said that hope was lost for Israel, G&ndash;d forbid. And this is what is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;There is one nation&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Esther 3:8)</span>, and our Sages of blessed memory expounded: &ldquo;Their G&ndash;d is asleep&rdquo; [<i>yashein</i> = <i>yeshno</i>] &mdash; meaning, that He would no longer save Israel, G&ndash;d forbid, as if He were asleep.</p>

<p>And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;scattered and separated among the nations, and their laws are different from every nation&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Esther 3:8)</span> &mdash; he said that they are scattered and separated among the nations, in the aspect of the abundance of divergent opinions and dispute, the aspect of scattering and separation among the nations, having fallen to the minds of the seventy nations. All of this is the opposite of the inclusiveness of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> in the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, as above. And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;and their laws are different,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; he said that the law of Israel is in the aspect of the strengthening of divergences and scattering and separation, G&ndash;d forbid. For he denied the holy law of Israel &mdash; that the entire law of our holy Torah is that through the law of our holy Torah, one is included in the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, through every single mitzvah and through every letter and word of the holy Torah. For &ldquo;the Torah, Israel, and the Holy One, blessed be He, are all one.&rdquo; And Haman wanted to turn the dish upside-down, G&ndash;d forbid, and said that everything is in reverse.</p>

<p>And therefore he wanted to prevail over Israel &mdash; to destroy, to kill, and to annihilate, etc. &mdash; for he is the aspect of the overpowering of the bloods in the time of trouble. For he is from the seed of Eisav, <span class="verse">&ldquo;the reddish one&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Genesis 25:25)</span> &mdash; on account of the overpowering of the evil bloods, from which comes the <i>sitra d&rsquo;mosa</i>, which is drawn from the sin of the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil, as our Sages of blessed memory said: &ldquo;Where is Haman [hinted] from the Torah? As it is said: <span class="verse">&lsquo;Is it from the tree?&rsquo;&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Chullin 139b; Genesis 3:11)</span> &mdash; for then death was decreed, and therefore he wanted to annihilate Israel, G&ndash;d forbid. And so it is in every generation and in every person, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Hashem&rsquo;s war against Amalaik from generation to generation&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 17:16)</span> &mdash; for he prevails upon every person at all times with all kinds of stratagems to make him fall, G&ndash;d forbid. For he is the tempter, he is the accuser, etc. &mdash; for first he entices the person to whatever he entices him, and afterwards he prosecutes him, until some trouble or suffering comes upon him, G&ndash;d forbid. And it is he himself who weakens and confuses the person&rsquo;s heart so that he does not cry out and supplicate before Hashem, may He be blessed &mdash; for he puts into his heart as if hope is lost, G&ndash;d forbid, and he wants to make him forget all the good things and kindnesses and miracles and wonders that Hashem, may He be blessed, has done with our fathers and with each and every individual in particular.</p>

<p>And the repair for all of this is the aspect of Mordechai, who is the aspect of the true tzaddik, the aspect of <i>mor d&rsquo;ror</i> [pure myrrh] &mdash; <i>maray dachya</i> &mdash; which is the chief spice of the anointing oil, with which the entire Mishkan and its vessels were anointed, and Aharon the Kohen and his sons. For all of their service in the Mishkan and the Bais HaMikdash was entirely to include all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> in the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, as above &mdash; for there was the essential revelation of divinity, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And I will meet there with the children of Israel,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 29:43)</span>, as above.</p>

<p>And the essential holiness of the Mishkan and its vessels was drawn through the anointing oil, which is a good fragrance of holiness, drawn from an exceedingly, exceedingly exalted holiness that has the power to sanctify the entire Mishkan and its vessels, etc. &mdash; to elevate and bring them from profane to holy. For the essence of holiness is being included in the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, where lies the root of all holinesses. Thus, the anointing oil that Moshe made had such wondrous power to elevate the entire Mishkan and its vessels &mdash; which were made of gold and silver and copper and blue-purple and red-purple, etc., etc. &mdash; in which there was an abundance of divergences and many hues in the silver and gold, etc., which are the totality of all worldly desires, especially the desire for money, which is the aspect of the overpowering of the bloods, etc. mentioned above. And the Mishkan, which was made from all of this, was the repair for all of this, as above. And all its holiness was drawn through the anointing oil, through which the Mishkan and its vessels were sanctified, and it elevated everything &mdash; all the many hues and divergences &mdash; so that they would be included in the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, where lie all the holinesses. Through this, the Mishkan had the power to atone for the children of Israel, to purify them from all the impurities, all of which are the aspect of the heresies drawn from the aspect of separation mentioned above, which separates, G&ndash;d forbid, the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, etc., as above.</p>

<p>For the essential repair is through the aspect of good fragrance, which is the life of the soul, which is the aspect of the anointing oil made with such exalted preparations that it has the power to draw a good fragrance to all who are distant from holiness &mdash; who cannot be revived except through the aspect of good fragrance, in the aspect of what is said regarding the souls of Israel who are cast down in the exile of their desires and traits, G&ndash;d forbid: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Support me with cakes of raisins, spread my bed with apples, for I am lovesick&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Song of Songs 2:5)</span>, as Rashi explains there &mdash; that these are kinds of fragrances.</p>

<p>For in our many sins, in the extremity of our weakness now, in the intensity of the bitterness of exile, our strength has already been so weakened that we do not feel the pleasantness and sweetness of the honeycomb &mdash; the words of sweetness of the true tzaddikim who revive us with such pure utterances, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;All food is abhorred by their soul,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 107:18)</span>. And our life-force comes only from what we smell from afar &mdash; a little of the good, holy, and awesome fragrance of the holy Torah-novelties of the true tzaddikim. And this is the aspect of the fragrance of the anointing oil, through which everything is sanctified and enters from outside to inside &mdash; from which comes the holiness of Mordechai, as above, who subdues the <i>kelipah</i> of Haman-Amalaik who wants to cast blemish upon the beginning of the salvation, as if Hashem, may He be blessed, has not yet begun to save at all.</p>

<p>And Mordechai knows all of this and in his wisdom instills the holy <i>emunah</i> in Israel, and illuminates the heart of man, and reminds him at all times of all the good things and miracles and wonders that Hashem, may He be blessed, has already done with us, in general and in particular, etc. And as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Bless Hashem, O my soul, and do not forget all His bounties,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 103:2)</span>. And through this, one has the power to cry out and supplicate before Hashem, may He be blessed, that He should save us even now, as above.</p>

<p>Through this came the intensity of the miracle of Purim &mdash; that Haman-Amalaik was subdued and fell. And in His mercy, may He be blessed, He frustrated his counsel and spoiled his thought, and everything was turned to good, from one extreme to the other, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And it was reversed &mdash; that the Jews dominated,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Esther 9:1)</span>. And they established these days of Purim as joy and feasting and a festival for all generations &mdash; to make known that even in our servitude, our G&ndash;d has not forsaken us. This is the intensity of the miracle and the wondrous salvation of Purim, which is greater than all the festivals, as our Sages of blessed memory said &mdash; for the essential miracle is what we saw, that even in our servitude, in the intensity of exile, Hashem, may He be blessed, watches over us so much, with wondrous providence, and arranged events for good from beginning to end. That precisely through Haman, the wicked Vashti was killed, and afterwards, through this very thing, the intensity of the miracle came about, that Haman was hanged through Esther &mdash; with such wondrous providences, as is explained in the holy Megillah.</p>

<p>And one must set his heart well to this, to understand from this that, just so, even now, He has not withdrawn His kindness from us. And one must strengthen himself in joy always, to draw the holiness of the joy of Purim &mdash; to believe that Hashem, may He be blessed, is with us even now, in the intensity of this exile &mdash; and to give <span class="key-term">todah</span> and <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span> every day for the past, and to beseech for the future, etc., as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- APOTROPOS §39 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;39</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;words of peace and truth&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Esther 9:30)</span> &mdash; this is the aspect of the three lines of truth that illuminate within the speech, through which the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, which is the aspect of peace, as above.</p>

<p>And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;seeking good for his nation&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Esther 10:3)</span> &mdash; the aspect of <span class="key-term">halachos</span>, for he was seeking good for Israel and clarifying all the <span class="key-term">halachos</span> of the Torah, as our Sages of blessed memory said &mdash; that he would open with matters and expound them. And: <span class="verse">&ldquo;speaking peace to all his seed&rdquo;</span> &mdash; the aspect of peace mentioned above, which is the aspect of the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, etc. &mdash; which is the essential completion of the fullness of the repair, as above.</p>

<p>And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;to all his seed&rdquo;</span> precisely &mdash; for the essential thing is that peace should be drawn, the aspect of the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, to all the seed of Israel who are born in every generation, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;A seed will serve Him; it will be told to Hashem for a generation&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 22:31)</span>. For the essential war of Amalaik is in every generation anew &mdash; because in every generation, souls are drawn in wondrous novelties anew, for no two people in all the generations are alike, as was explained above (&sect;23). And because of the abundance of divergences and new forms of intelligence that arise in every generation, Amalaik wants to strengthen himself to separate in thought, G&ndash;d forbid, the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> from the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, as above. And therefore: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Hashem&rsquo;s war against Amalaik from generation to generation.&rdquo;</span></p>

<p>And this is the aspect of all the vain wisdoms that arise anew in every generation &mdash; both the external wisdoms, which are the wisdom of philosophy that grow stronger in every generation, and the other wisdoms of the world of foolishness and vanity, where each one imagines that the world has now become wiser, as if in previous generations they had no intellect at all, to desire such implements and adornments, etc. &mdash; as such foolish talk is common among the youth. And all of this is drawn from the aspect mentioned above &mdash; because in truth, at the root of the holiness of the souls, they are drawn in every generation in the aspect of innovation for good, for the essential glory of Hashem, may He be blessed, is precisely that in the abundance of the immense divergence of opinions, they should be included in His <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, as above. And <span class="verse">&ldquo;G&ndash;d has made one corresponding to the other&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Ecclesiastes 7:14)</span> &mdash; therefore the aspect of the contamination of Amalaik wants to reverse everything, as if today they are wiser for evil. But Hashem, may He be blessed, fights him in every generation, as above, through His true tzaddikim, and reveals such wondrous <span class="key-term">halachos</span> and Torah-novelties in every generation &mdash; so that through this, in every generation, the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is ever greater, from within the abundance and divergence of the many opinions, which are the aspect of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, as above.</p>

<p>This is the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;seeking good for his nation and speaking peace to all his seed&rdquo;</span> precisely, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and unto generation after generation is His faithfulness,&rdquo;</span> in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;generation to generation praises Your works,&rdquo;</span> etc., as above. And understand well, to connect everything from beginning to end, and you will understand counsel and strengthening to draw close always to Hashem, may He be blessed, and to give thanks to His Name, may He be blessed, always &mdash; which is the essential ultimate purpose, the aspect of the delight of the World to Come, as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- APOTROPOS §40 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;40</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of Pesach and the greatness of the mitzvah of relating the story of the Exodus from Egypt, as was explained above (in &sect;16).</p>

<p>For now that we have already merited to go out of Egypt, etc. &mdash; praise be to G&ndash;d, we have a good beginning, etc., as above &mdash; therefore we must abundantly tell of the Exodus from Egypt, etc.</p>

<p>And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;We were slaves to Pharaoh in Egypt.&rdquo;</span> For the essential redemption was through Shabbos &mdash; through Hashem, may He be blessed, in His mercy drawing upon them Himself the aspect of the holiness of Shabbos upon the six days of the week. Through this, the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> was revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> &mdash; that all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> are all drawn from the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> Himself, may He be blessed. This was then revealed very, very greatly through all the great, awesome, and immense signs and wonders that Moshe did before the eyes of all Israel &mdash; turning water to blood and blood to water, sending frogs, and when he wished, removing them through his prayer. And similarly with all the plagues with which he struck Pharaoh, etc. &mdash; demonstrating that all of nature and all the workings of the diverse activities in the entire world are all in the hand of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, and they are in His hand like clay in the hand of the potter. And He reveals His secret to His servants the tzaddikim, so that they can rule over the world and direct everything as they wish.</p>

<p>And all of this was drawn at that time by Hashem, may He be blessed, Himself, in the aspect of an awakening from above, as is brought &mdash; for they were not yet worthy of the redemption, for they had not yet drawn the repairs mentioned above that are drawn through <span class="key-term">todah</span> and <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span> and <span class="key-term">halachos</span>, etc. &mdash; for it was the first redemption, and they had not yet received the Torah, where all the <span class="key-term">halachos</span> are, as was explained above. But Hashem, may He be blessed, had compassion upon them, through the merit of the Patriarchs and through the little good He found in them, until through His awesome wonders He compelled Moshe to go and redeem them, and He drew upon them Himself the aspect of the holiness of Shabbos upon the weekdays, until the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> was revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, through all the signs and wonders, etc., as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <i>Shabbos HaGadol</i> before Pesach &mdash; for the essential miracles of Pesach were through the holiness of Shabbos, as above. And therefore it is called <i>Shabbos HaGadol</i> [the Great Shabbos] &mdash; for this is the essential greatness of Hashem, may He be blessed &mdash; when His unity, may He be blessed, is revealed from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, as above, which is accomplished through Shabbos, as above.</p>

<p>And this is why we begin &ldquo;We were slaves,&rdquo; etc. &mdash; for before the redemption, in the time of exile (that is, before they merited to draw the holiness of Shabbos to the weekdays), we were slaves &mdash; because the aspect of the weekdays held sway, which are the aspect of &ldquo;servant,&rdquo; as is explained there in the Torah mentioned above. <span class="verse">&ldquo;And Hashem our G&ndash;d brought us out from there,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; that is, Hashem, may He be blessed, Himself brought us out from there, with a strong hand and an outstretched arm, even though we were not worthy &mdash; for we had not yet drawn upon ourselves all the repairs mentioned above. Even so, Hashem, may He be blessed, had compassion upon us and brought us out Himself, through the power of His wondrous mercy, as above.</p>

<p>And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And had the Holy One, blessed be He, not brought out our fathers from Egypt, behold we and our children and our children&rsquo;s children would still be enslaved to Pharaoh in Egypt.&rdquo;</span> That is, the essential Exodus from Egypt was to reveal His divinity, may He be blessed, from generation to generation forever, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And you shall make known to your children and your children&rsquo;s children&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Deuteronomy 4:9)</span>, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;and unto generation after generation is His faithfulness&rdquo;</span> &mdash; which one merits through Torah/<span class="key-term">halachah</span>, from which come all the holy births of the seed of Israel, the holy nation. But at that time, they were not yet worthy of this &mdash; only Hashem, may He be blessed, Himself drew in His mercy all the repairs mentioned above, until He redeemed them Himself. But had the Holy One, blessed be He, not brought out, etc. &mdash; behold we and our children, etc., would still be enslaved, etc. &mdash; for now that we have already merited the Exodus from Egypt and we have a good beginning, as above, through this we merit each time the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah/halachah</span>, as above, through which the births of children are drawn in the holiness of Israel &mdash; and we are able to teach them and make known to them, from generation to generation, from father to son, the works of Hashem, for they are awesome, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;generation to generation praises Your works,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; until all of them walk in this path, in the path of the holy Torah, to give thanks and praise to Hashem, may He be blessed, always, etc. &mdash; and to engage in <span class="key-term">halachos</span>, etc., until they reveal in each generation the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, which is accomplished anew in every generation, as above. All of this is the aspect of the holiness of Shabbos, which is the aspect of &ldquo;son,&rdquo; to nullify the aspect of the servitude of the weekdays. But had the Holy One, blessed be He, not brought out our fathers from Egypt in His mercy, by Himself, as above &mdash; behold we and our children and our children&rsquo;s children would still be enslaved, etc. &mdash; for we would not have merited the birth of children in holiness, in the aspect of &ldquo;son,&rdquo; the aspect of freedom &mdash; but all the children and children&rsquo;s children would have been in the aspect of servitude, as above, from which came the entire exile of Egypt, as above.</p>

<p>And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And even if we were all wise, all understanding, all elders, all knowing the Torah &mdash; it is a mitzvah upon us to tell of the Exodus from Egypt.&rdquo;</span> That is, at first glance it is difficult &mdash; why did He emphasize so many times the telling of the Exodus from Egypt? For the essential purpose of the Exodus from Egypt was for the sake of the Giving of the Torah, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;When you bring out the nation from Egypt, you shall serve G&ndash;d on this mountain&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 3:12)</span> &mdash; which is the Giving of the Torah. And it would have been fitting to tell only of the miracle of the Giving of the Torah. And why did He emphasize more the telling of the Exodus from Egypt? And even the Giving of the Torah itself began: <span class="verse">&ldquo;I am Hashem your G&ndash;d Who brought you out of the land of Egypt,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 20:2)</span>. And similarly in most of the mitzvos.</p>

<p>But according to the above, it is well explained &mdash; for the essential intensity of the miracle is the beginning, which is the Exodus from Egypt, which was the first redemption, which was very difficult because &ldquo;this depends upon that,&rdquo; etc., as above. And this is: &ldquo;And even if we were all wise, etc., all knowing the Torah &mdash; it is a mitzvah upon us to tell of the Exodus from Egypt&rdquo; specifically, even more so. Even though now we already know the Torah, which is the essential purpose for which we went out of Egypt, as above &mdash; even so, it is a mitzvah upon us to tell of the Exodus from Egypt, which is the beginning, through which we merited to know the Torah &mdash; for that beginning was the most difficult of all, as above. And we need now to tell about this even more &mdash; for even now, all the keeping of the Torah depends upon this. For the more one gives thanks and praises Him, may He be blessed, for the greatness of His kindness of the beginning, which is the aspect of the Exodus from Egypt, which was very difficult &mdash; the more one tells and gives thanks and praises Him, may He be blessed &mdash; so are all the repairs mentioned above drawn even more, through which the <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span> in turn grows ever greater, etc. &mdash; and so it cycles around for the good, as above. Through all of this, one merits joy, which is the essential thing &mdash; to strengthen oneself from wherever one is, to rejoice in the salvation of Hashem, etc. &mdash; through which everyone can enter into the keeping of the Torah, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore, even if we were all wise and understanding and elders and knowing the Torah and all that has passed over us has already passed and we have merited the salvation of Hashem and immense wonders &mdash; it is a mitzvah upon us to tell of the Exodus from Egypt, when the beginning was, as above &mdash; through which one merits to strengthen himself in joy even now, through which comes the essential keeping of the Torah, as above. And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And whoever tells more of the Exodus from Egypt &mdash; behold, this is praiseworthy.&rdquo;</span> For each and every person must tell abundantly of the Exodus from Egypt, in general and in particular &mdash; how many miracles and wonders Hashem, may He be blessed, did with us &mdash; so that the <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span> should grow each time even more, through which comes the essential repair, as above. And this is: &ldquo;And whoever tells more of the Exodus from Egypt &mdash; behold, this is praiseworthy.&rdquo; And it is brought in the Kavanos: &ldquo;behold, this is praiseworthy&rdquo; &mdash; in <i>chasadim</i> [kindnesses] &mdash; that is, the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;whoever is wise, let him observe these things, and they will contemplate the kindnesses of Hashem&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Psalms 107:43)</span> &mdash; the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;the faithful kindnesses of David&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Isaiah 55:3)</span>, which are drawn through <span class="key-term">todah/hoda&rsquo;ah</span>, as is explained there.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- APOTROPOS §41 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;41</div>

<p>And this is: &ldquo;It happened with Rabbi Eliezer and Rabbi Yehoshua,&rdquo; etc. &mdash; who were telling of the Exodus from Egypt all that night, until their students came and said to them: &ldquo;Our teachers, the time for the morning <i>Krias Shema</i> has arrived.&rdquo; The time for <i>Krias Shema</i> precisely &mdash; for through the abundance of telling of the Exodus from Egypt, the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed even more from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>, as above, which is the aspect of <i>Krias Shema</i> &mdash; to reveal the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> in the world, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Hashem our G&ndash;d, Hashem is One.&rdquo;</span> &ldquo;Hashem our G&ndash;d&rdquo; &mdash; that is, His divinity that dwells and is clothed within us, within all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span>. &ldquo;Hashem is One&rdquo; &mdash; everything is included and unified in His <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, may He be blessed. And as our Sages of blessed memory said, one must extend the <i>dales</i> of <i>echad</i> in order to crown Him above and below and in the four directions &mdash; which are the totality of the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> in all six extremities, all of which are included in His unity, may He be blessed. For Hashem is One, and everything is drawn only from Him, may He be blessed.</p>

<p>And all of this is revealed through the abundance of telling of the Exodus from Egypt. And therefore Hashem, may He be blessed, arranged it so that these tzaddikim told of the Exodus from Egypt, etc., until their students came &mdash; those who received the <span class="key-term">halachos</span> from them, which are also the aspect of <span class="key-term">todah</span>, as above &mdash; and said to them: &ldquo;Our teachers, the time for <i>Krias Shema</i> has arrived,&rdquo; etc. &mdash; for through this, the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed, which is the aspect of <i>Krias Shema</i>, as above.</p>

<p>And to sweeten further and explain the statement mentioned above &mdash; &ldquo;Whoever tells more of the Exodus from Egypt,&rdquo; etc. &mdash; it is thus: For all the kinds of counsel that our Sages of blessed memory illuminated for us, with which one can strengthen himself &mdash; the adversary constantly lies in wait to push him away from them, G&ndash;d forbid. Therefore, one needs great stubbornness. And so it is with the matter mentioned above &mdash; that one must strengthen himself to give thanks always to Hashem, may He be blessed, for all the kindnesses and wonders, etc., even if he is as he is, for even so, He has already bestowed upon us immense wonders. But the adversary constantly strengthens himself to cause forgetfulness and concealment, G&ndash;d forbid, etc.</p>

<p>Therefore a person must strengthen himself to tell abundantly of the Exodus from Egypt, etc., in the aspect mentioned above. And this is: &ldquo;Whoever tells <i>more</i>&rdquo; &mdash; <i>&ldquo;more&rdquo;</i> precisely &mdash; for one must increase so much, until he increases the telling of the Exodus from Egypt over the hinderer, until it exceeds him and nullifies him &mdash; in the manner our Sages of blessed memory said regarding the nullification of a prohibited substance: &ldquo;one increases over it and nullifies it.&rdquo; And this is: &ldquo;And whoever tells <i>more</i>&rdquo; of the kindnesses of Hashem, etc. &mdash; which is the aspect of the Exodus from Egypt, etc., as above &mdash; who increases the telling over the hinderer until he nullifies him, as above &mdash; &ldquo;behold, this is praiseworthy,&rdquo; as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- APOTROPOS §42 -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-marker">&sect;42</div>

<p>And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And I will pass through the land of Egypt &mdash; I, and not an angel; I, and not a seraph; I, and not an emissary; I am Hashem &mdash; I am He and not another.&rdquo;</span> That is, during the Exodus from Egypt, the revelation of the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> from within the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> was so great that even above, His <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span>, may He be blessed, was revealed &mdash; as is explained there in the Torah mentioned above: that when the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed below, His <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> is revealed also above, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;You are One and Your Name is One, and who is like Your nation Israel, one nation in the land,&rdquo;</span> etc.</p>

<p>And this is: &ldquo;And I will pass through the land of Egypt &mdash; I, and not an angel; I, and not a seraph,&rdquo; etc. &mdash; for all the concealments and hiddennesses were nullified. For sometimes Hashem, may He be blessed, clothes His conduct through the angels, in the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;Behold, I am sending an angel before you&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 23:20)</span> &mdash; which was said after the sin, and Moshe did not desire this. For then one can err, G&ndash;d forbid, as Acheir erred through this. And as the verse itself there warns: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Beware of him, do not defy him,&rdquo;</span> and our Sages of blessed memory expounded: &ldquo;Do not exchange Me for him&rdquo; &mdash; for from there is drawn the error of all idolators. And similarly the errors of the naturalist philosophers of today &mdash; for the angel is called <i>Elokim</i>, which has the numerical value of <i>ha&rsquo;teva</i> [nature]. But at the time of the Exodus from Egypt, Hashem, may He be blessed, had compassion upon us and revealed His <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> below and above &mdash; that there is no governance in the world except through Himself alone, in the aspect of: &ldquo;I, and not an angel; I, and not a seraph,&rdquo; etc. &mdash; &ldquo;I am Hashem; I am He and not another.&rdquo; For all the diverse activities in the world &mdash; all are from Him, may He be blessed, Himself, as above.</p>

<!-- ======================= -->
<!-- SHAYACH L'EIL (belongs above) -->
<!-- ======================= -->

<div class="section-note"><i>Shayach l&rsquo;eil</i> &mdash; This belongs above [at the end of the Apotropos section]:</div>

<p>And therefore we say <i>Birchas Kohanim</i> [the Priestly Blessing] after <i>Birchas HaTorah</i> [the Blessing over the Torah]. For <i>Birchas HaTorah</i> is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span> mentioned above &mdash; that we bless and give thanks every day, immediately in the morning, for the pleasantness of our portion, that we merited to receive the Torah, which is the essential path to draw close to Hashem, may He be blessed, from wherever one is, as is explained above (in &sect;5). Through this, all the repairs mentioned above are accomplished, until one merits that all the <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</span> should be included in the <span class="key-term">achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</span> &mdash; which is the aspect of peace and unity among all Israel, that all the divergent opinions should be included together, etc., as above.</p>

<p>This, Aharon the Kohen merited more than anyone else &mdash; through the fact that he was not jealous of Moshe his brother, even though he [Moshe] was greater than him, and he went out to greet him with joy, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And he shall see you and rejoice in his heart&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Exodus 4:14)</span>. And through this, he merited the <i>Kehunah</i>, as our Sages of blessed memory said: &ldquo;In reward for &lsquo;and he shall see you,&rsquo; etc., he merited the <i>Choshen HaMishpat</i> [Breastplate of Judgment] upon his heart.&rdquo;</p>

<p>Therefore we say <i>Birchas Kohanim</i>, which is the holiness of Aharon the Kohen, after <i>Birchas HaTorah</i> &mdash; for they are of one aspect and depend upon each other, as above. And therefore <i>Birchas Kohanim</i> concludes with peace, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;and grant you peace&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Numbers 6:26)</span> &mdash; for through the <span class="key-term">hoda&rsquo;ah</span> mentioned above, which is the aspect of <i>Birchas HaTorah</i>, one merits peace and unity, as above. And all of this we merited through Aharon the Kohen, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore our Sages of blessed memory said: &ldquo;Be of the students of Aharon, loving peace and pursuing peace&rdquo; <span class="inline-source">(Avos 1:12)</span> &mdash; that is, as above. And this is: &ldquo;loving the creatures and bringing them close to the Torah&rdquo; &mdash; for the essential drawing close to the Torah is through the aspect mentioned above, through <span class="key-term">todah/hoda&rsquo;ah</span>, which is <i>Birchas HaTorah</i>, through which one merits peace, which is the aspect of the holiness of Aharon the Kohen, as above.</p>



<div class="translator-summary">
  <h3>&#9670; Translator&rsquo;s Summary &#9670;</h3>

  <p>This collection of halachos applies the law of <i>perikah u&rsquo;te&rsquo;inah</i> (helping unload and load an animal) across multiple spiritual dimensions, drawing on several of Rabbainu&rsquo;s Toros.</p>

  <div class="flowchart">
    <span class="step"><b>Avaidah 3, &sect;&sect;15&ndash;16</b> (LM I:13): The <i>tzadik</i> can raise even the farthest souls through <i>ibbur</i> &mdash; &ldquo;Go out and see the might of your Master.&rdquo; But only <i>&ldquo;with him&rdquo;</i> &mdash; the person must make some effort himself. Physically: the burden of livelihood derives from distance from Torah/hashgachah shelaimah.</span>
    <span class="arrow">&darr;</span>
    <span class="step"><b>Halacha 1</b> (LM I:59): Hatred blemishes <i>da&rsquo;as</i> &rarr; burden falls. Love/helping rectifies <i>da&rsquo;as</i> &rarr; burden is raised. <i>Kavod</i> (honor) = root of souls = the <i>Samech</i> that supports all who fall. But an elder whose honor would be damaged is exempt/forbidden.</span>
    <span class="arrow">&darr;</span>
    <span class="step"><b>Halacha 2</b> (LM II:7): True compassion = helping a Jew shed the burden of sin. Finding merit in a sinner (<i>LM I:282</i>) judges him favorably &rarr; lifts the spiritual burden &rarr; lifts the physical burden. Livelihood flows from the &ldquo;sea of wisdom&rdquo; when <i>da&rsquo;as</i> illuminates.</span>
    <span class="arrow">&darr;</span>
    <span class="step"><b>Halacha 4</b> (LM II:2): Shabbos = simple unity; weekdays = diverse activities. Drawing Shabbos holiness into the week reveals that all multiplicity flows from the One. Strife/suffering = disconnect from this unity. Helping the &ldquo;enemy&rdquo; unload = abandoning hatred = restoring unity = rest for all. A convert&rsquo;s inclusion reveals <i>achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</i> from the most remote &ldquo;changed activities.&rdquo;</span>
  </div>

  <p><b>Recurring themes:</b> (1) Hatred/sin = heaviness/falling; love/merit-finding = lightness/raising. (2) <i>Da&rsquo;as</i> and <i>kavod</i> are intimately linked &mdash; both are needed to bear and lift burdens. (3) The Torah commands engagement with even the fallen, but with wisdom about who can be reached. (4) Physical burdens and spiritual burdens are inseparable &mdash; rectifying one rectifies the other.</p>

  <p><b>Note:</b> The subdivision <i>Hefker v&rsquo;Nichsay HaGer</i> continues from &sect;30 (<i>Apotropos</i>) through &sect;42, elaborating on: the signs and wonders in Egypt revealing that all <i>pe&rsquo;ulos mishtanos</i> derive from Him alone; the personal application &mdash; <i>todah</i> and <i>hoda&rsquo;ah</i> even in the midst of distress; the rooster pecking in the refuse-heap (even tiny mitzvos are cherished); the cycle of struggle and redemption in every generation; Rosh Hashanah and <i>Alainu</i> as the ultimate revelation of <i>achdus ha&rsquo;pashut</i>; the Shabbos Zohar passage; the laws of inheritance and their connection to all the above. These sections await translation in a continuation.</p>
</div>

<p class="nachnach">Na Nach Nachma Nachman MayUman</p>


